Volunteer teachers who teach Chinese at the Ministry of Tourism consider Cambodia as a close friend and plan to establish a Cambodian Students' Association.
The Ministry of Tourism has partnered with Chinese volunteer teachers to provide free basic Chinese language training with Kuoyang, a teacher with more than 15 years of teaching experience in China, with good methods and tips for students. .
Speaking to Fresh News on the evening of May 22, 2023, Guo Yang considered her students and other Cambodians as close friends and enjoyed volunteering to teach Chinese to Cambodian students. Give loyal love back to the teacher.
Xiao Miu Leng, who is also a Chinese student with her teacher, expressed her happiness when she came to study with her teacher, who has many convenient teaching methods for all students. For almost six months now, Miao Leng has been able to read, listen to some Chinese, compose sentences in Chinese on his own, use grammar, and read books in comprehensible Chinese.
Sieu Mieu Leng also thanked Kuoyang and other assistant teachers who volunteered to teach Cambodian students. This teaching helps Miu Leng to complete her knowledge of Chinese, re-learn the knowledge she had learned before, and encourage Miu Leng to have the courage to practice singing songs in Chinese, as well as increase her understanding of culture and way of life. Of the Chinese people.
After teaching for almost six months, Chinese teachers should see that the Cambodian students who come to learn Chinese are diligent, but they still lack the method to learn quickly, so teachers need to Teach them to know the tips to learn to be better, easier to grasp, especially to record what is important.
The teacher is of the opinion that sharing knowledge and culture between teachers and students and between students and students alike will make it easier for them to learn Chinese, increase class friendships, and gain mutual knowledge. Learning with native teachers also helps students become more fluent in Chinese.
This kind teacher also plans to establish an association to provide Chinese language teaching and other education to Cambodian students because she has a sincere love for the Cambodian people. Teachers are optimistic that only education will increase the human resources needed to invest in the development of the nation.
The students of Ms. Kuoyang and her Cambodian friends are very grateful for the enthusiasm and dedication of the teachers who volunteered to teach Chinese to Cambodia directly. The achievements of the teachers will contribute to building human resources in Cambodia to a certain extent. "Teachers' smiles are always in the hearts of Cambodian students!" Thank you, Chinese teacher!
NEC Releases Preliminary Results of National and International Registration of Journalists for the 7th National Assembly Election
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a press release on the preliminary results of the registration of national and international journalists to cover the 7th National Assembly Election 2023. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on May 23, 2023.
As of May 22, 2023, the NEC has recognized and issued certificates to a total of 220 national journalists from 21 units and a total of 30 international journalists from 14 units to cover The 7th National Assembly election process in 2023 and is reviewing the registration of some national and international journalists.
On May 25, the Constitutional Council held a meeting to review and decide on the complaints of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party after the NEC did not register their names for the National Assembly election.
(Phnom Penh): On May 25, 2023, the Constitutional Council will hold a plenary meeting to review and decide on the complaint of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer National Unity Party regarding the rejection of the National Election Committee. (NEC) on the registration of both parties in the list of voters for the 7th National Assembly election.
A press release obtained by Fresh News confirms that the Constitutional Council will hold a plenary session chaired by Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, from 9:00 am at the White House, Chamkarmon. :
1: Complaint of the Candlelight Party against the decision No. 233 of the NEC dated 15 May 2023 of the National Election Committee and demanded that the National Election Committee accept List of political parties running for election and list of candidates for the 7th National Assembly election in 2023 of the Candlelight Party, which has 25 constituencies.
2: Complaint of the Khmer National Solidarity Party to the Constitutional Council to consider and decide on the possibility of registration for the election and registration of candidates for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 of the Khmer National Unity Party.
Separately, 18 political parties have been officially recognized by the NEC on the registration of political parties for the 7th National Assembly election to be held on July 23, 2023 after Those parties meet all the conditions of the election law. Minister of Commerce Leads a Delegation to Discuss the Draft Law on the Approval of the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement
This meeting was also attended by high-ranking members from all the specialized committees of the National Assembly. At the beginning of the meeting, Ms. Nin Saphon, Chairperson of the Ninth Committee and Member of the Standing Committee, warmly welcomed Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce on behalf of the Royal Government and his colleagues to discuss and defend the above draft law.
In addition, she informed the meeting about the detailed review and study of the draft law on the approval of the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement, as a result of which the draft law was properly prepared in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution, the law and Relevant legal standards in accordance with the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government, the 6th legislature of the National Assembly.
The Minister clarified and informed the meeting about the objectives, content as well as the benefits that Cambodia will receive from the ASEAN Trade in Services Agreement, which will provide benefits to Cambodia when this agreement enters into force.
On that occasion, the President highly appreciated the efforts of the Minister, leaders at all levels, as well as civil servants of the Ministry of Commerce, who actively carried out professional duties in accordance with the policies and strategies of the Royal Government. The results are a source of pride, especially the drafting of laws and regulations under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
