The Minister, who chairs the Public Administration Reform Committee, stressed that leadership is the art of thinking and decision-making. The importance of leadership is to be used in the lives of all people, whether civil servants, workers, farmers, students and all citizens struggle to learn, do business, work in accordance with the business to lead life, overcome difficulties and obstacles. Body.
The Minister shared the theory of education with some practical work experience that he personally went through as a public administration official for more than 40 years, especially the last three years as Minister of Public Works. Overcome the complex difficulties caused by Kovid-19, inspire work in an innovative, proactive spirit, work normally, be resilient, keep up with the changes of the times.
Through this lecture, the Minister highlighted the recent progress of public administration reform under the precious direct guidance of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, which has made Cambodia free from the war of national division and bring the Cambodian society to Peace, national unity and prosperous development from January 7, 1979 to the present.
Minister Prum Sokha expressed his strong hope that through this shared lecture, it will become a concept for thinking and contributing to help all the students who attend to be able to use it for the benefit of building their lives, building their future destiny. And the motherland of Cambodia, dear.
