The Manila Central Post Office is the capital's busiest office building. The building is the country's main mail sorting and distribution center and is the headquarters for the Philippine Postal Corporation.
The historic post office building, recognized as a national landmark, was built in 1926 with tall pillars in a classic style. It was badly damaged during World War II and was rebuilt in 1946.
