(Battambang): Mr. Phan Phalla, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, stated that the Small and Medium Enterprise Bank of Cambodia (SME Bank) has made significant contributions to the Royal Government in addressing the lack of financing of small and medium enterprises while large enterprises Small and medium-sized enterprises are considered by the Royal Government to be the backbone of the economy, both in terms of job creation and support for national economic growth.
He said that as of April 2023, the Bank for Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia has provided direct lending operations with a total amount of $ 62.4 million to 275 small and medium enterprises, of which There are 75 enterprises with female entrepreneurs.
Mr. Phan Phalla said that over the same period of the co-financing program, the Small and Medium Enterprise Bank of Cambodia has partnered with participating financial institutions (PFIs) to provide loans in the amount of $ 148 million. A total of 2,967 enterprises, of which 739 are women entrepreneurs.
Speaking at the inauguration of the Cambodian Small and Medium Enterprise Bank, Battambang Branch on May 22, 2023, Mr. Phan Phalla stated: “In 2019, small and medium enterprises accounted for more than 90% of both businesses All created in Cambodia and employ about 70% of the total population. At the same time, small and medium enterprises contribute about 58 percent of GDP.
The senior official stressed that the Royal Government had initiated the establishment of the Cambodian Small and Medium Enterprise Bank in a timely manner, during and after the outbreak of Kovid 19. It is important to support small and medium enterprises to maintain their business balance.
At the same time, Dr. Lim Oun, Director General of the Bank for Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia, said that the bank decided to select the location of Battambang province as the first branch because Battambang is an economic center in Cambodia with economic activity. The main ones are: trade, tourism, agriculture, especially small and medium enterprises, including: agro-processing, handicraft and production business.
Dr. Lim Oun added that the SME Bank was established by the Royal Government in 2020 under the technical and financial guardianship of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the supervision of the National Bank of Cambodia. The Bank has a mission to provide effective and sustainable financing and commercial banking services to support small and medium enterprises to promote economic diversification and exports in line with government policies.
