(Phnom Penh): The Fisheries Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has issued a notification on the 2023 fishing season.
The closed season for fishing in freshwater fisheries is set as follows:
* From June 1 to September 30 for freshwater fisheries, including Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Kratie, Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom and parts of Phnom Penh and Kandal Province in the north. Chaktomuk River parallel
* From July 1 to October 31, including Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Takeo, Kampong Speu and parts of Phnom Penh and Kandal, located south of the Chaktomuk River.
During the closed fishing period, all fishermen must use only household fishing gear as stated in Prakas No. 458, dated October 22, 2012.
