Russia and Ukraine have been fighting for nearly nine months for the city of Baghdad, destroying what was once a popular wine industry to the point that some analysts believe it no longer has strategic value. And. But why are both Ukraine and Russia so determined for this ghost town?
For Ukraine, the decisive defense of Bakmut is a heroic symbol of a decisive sacrifice of fresh blood to protect the territory and the nation. Russia, meanwhile, needs victory to bolster its military after a series of humiliating defeats in Ukraine's 2022 counterattack.
What does the loss of Baghdad mean to Ukraine? In a speech on Sunday, May 21 at the G7 summit in Hiroshima, Japan, Zelensky said that Baghdad was completely destroyed. And he seems to be referring to the fact that even if Russia captures the city, it is only a triumph.
But while Bakmut is considered by some to be a symbol of no strategic value, the loss of the city will more or less hurt the morale of the Ukrainian army after months of bloodshed. So far, no figures have been released for the number of Russian and Ukrainian soldiers killed in the battle of Bakmut, but both Moscow and Kiev claim to have killed hundreds of enemy soldiers a day. ⁇.
