Speaking to Fresh News, Brigadier General San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, confirmed that the shocking case of child abduction in Phnom Penh by a Chinese woman was untrue. No incident occurred.
Brigadier General San Sok Seiha pointed out that after seeing the posting of false information on Facebook, which is a fake page and some fake Facebook accounts that spread false information with the intent to intimidate and cause insecurity and chaos. To the society that there is a case of a Chinese woman abducting a child, in fact, this case is not true.
After seeing the news on social media, the Press and Quick Reaction Team has been working together to find out the truth until the morning of May 22, 2023. The specialized force of the Office of Investigation and Implementation of the Immigration Work Plan in collaboration with the Post Force Kork Khleang Administrative Police, Sen Sok District, conducted a search and brought a Chinese woman to be interrogated at the Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate.
After questioning, the Chinese woman confirmed that she lost her son in Central Market on April 20, 2023. The director of Central Market saw a 3-year-old boy wandering in Central Market looking for his parents, so the police contacted Mith Samlanh to take care of him.
To clarify, officials contacted the mother in China for clarification. The mother confirmed that the woman and the boy were indeed her daughter and grandson, and that her daughter There have been brain problems for many years (neurosis), often forgetfulness and dementia.
After the interrogation, the competent authorities reported to the Embassy of the People's Republic of China, as well as prepared the relevant documents, continued the procedure, sent to the General Department of Immigration and asked for guidance from the authorities to deport from the Kingdom of Cambodia.
