This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over a Joint Ceremony at Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, May 22, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over three celebrations at the Municipal Special Economic Zone. Sihanouk, an achievement born of politics or the "Belt and Road" initiative.
The three programs are: 1) Conversation program with more than 20,000 workers, 2) Visit the achievements in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone and 3) Inauguration of a tire factory. These three events are held to celebrate the 10th anniversary of the Belt and Road Initiative.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the meeting was attended by a total of 24,239 workers from 175 factories in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
According to the Minister, Samdech Techo Prime Minister has visited the SEZ four times already, the first time in 2008 at the groundbreaking ceremony of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, the second in 2016 during the ceremony. Congratulations on the acquisition of 100 investment companies in Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone and the 3rd and 4th in 2018 twice in a meeting with workers in Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
Investment operations in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone will have an export-import value of about $ 2.5 billion by 2022 and provide employment for nearly 30,000 workers.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has good relations and provides benefits to local people, such as providing jobs in the area, renting houses, selling food, transportation, etc. As well as participating in building achievements, humanitarian activities with local communities in the region.
The tire factory, which will be inaugurated tomorrow, is a Chinese investment company called General Thai Tech Technology (Cambodia), co-owned by Kuo Chui and CEO Thao Kuochong, with a $ 300 million investment. It is the largest investment project in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone and the first project with an investment of over 100 million US dollars from Jiangsu Province in Cambodia.
This factory is a kind of factory that uses modern technology in line with the policy of developing the Cambodian industrial sector, which is a high value-added industry, using natural rubber raw materials that are locally available, nearly 5,000 tons per year, which can help promote the market. Cambodia's natural rubber.
The plant can produce nearly 1.3 million tires of all kinds a year, which will employ about 1,150 workers.
