Indo-Pacific trade agreement talks close to supply chain agreement (Video inside) (Tokyo): 14 countries in US-led Indo-Pacific trade talks close to agreement on supply chain Supply chain coordination is underway and an agreement could be announced soon next week. According to Bloomberg News.
The talks focused on systems to provide early warning when countries see the risk of disrupting the supply chain. The aim is to avoid the global disruption experienced during the Kovid-19 outbreak.
The supply chain is one of the four "pillars" within the framework that countries began discussing last year, including a clean economy focused on the transition to renewable energy, Bloomberg reported. And the fight against climate change, economic equity, which includes tax issues and corruption, and trade.
Although the supply chain agreement will move forward, some of the remaining pillars may be more difficult to resolve than the supply chain, such as the pillars of trade, which India is not involved in due to concerns about its commitment to the environment and the environment. Work. Trade is also an issue that historically countries have had to overcome before reaching an agreement.
The United States has developed the Indo-Pacific Economic Framework Initiative (IPEF) as a way to counteract China's growing influence and re-establish its base of American influence after it was lost. Withdraw from previous efforts to establish local trade laws. According to Bloomberg News.
National Police General Commission: In the case of posting and distributing stories about kidnapping children on social media as fictional information, the specialized force is launching a search for those groups
(Phnom Penh): The Department of Technology Crimes of the General Commission of the National Police on May 21, 2023 came out to claim that the case that was shared on social media, child abduction, kidney surgery or other child abduction cases are It is a fabrication with the intention of polluting society.
The Department of Technology Crimes said that after receiving the information, experts immediately launched an immediate investigation and determined that all the information was fake, created by anti-government groups. Legitimate government. Currently, the specialized department is collecting evidence to implement legal procedures.
"The Department of Technology Crime Prevention would like to inform the public that in the past, the Facebook page of Anurak, Kam Tep Limhong and some Facebook accounts have published information about child abduction or kidney abduction.
After receiving the above information, the department assigned an expert officer to conduct an urgent investigation, and as a result, it was determined that this information was false information created by a group that has a tendency to oppose the legitimate government. Currently, the specialized department is collecting evidence to implement legal procedures.
"The department hopes that the public and the public who use social media, please do not continue to share the above false information to avoid misunderstanding or social insecurity."
