On that occasion, Samdech Kittisangha Dr. Men Sam An expressed his pride that his ideas are applied every year by setting topics in line with the situation and circumstances of the country and internationally, and this year's theme is Tenth is "Islam joins the fight against human trafficking and modern slavery."
Samdech Men Sam An continued that this topic is very suitable for the current environment, as it is a policy that has been vigorously implemented and is active in the grassroots of our country and also participates in the movement to maintain values. Participation in the prevention, eradication, fight against human trafficking and modern slavery in the Muslim community.
At the same time, Samdech Kittisangha Bandith also expressed his pride and admiration with the Cambodian Islamic community for the results of the participation of candidates (Kri-Kri Ah Hafiz-Hafiz) representing Cambodia on the international stage. Shows that Cambodia is a small country with a small number of Muslims, but can get good results among large countries and a large number of Muslims who participated in the competition.
Duke Sos Kamrey, head of the Cambodian Islamic Supreme Council and chairman of the Blessing Committee, said that Islam joins in the fight against human trafficking and modern-day slavery, with specific principles in eliminating, preventing and combating Modern human trafficking and slavery are considered crimes, a serious sin that the perpetrators must be punished and go to hell inevitably.
The duke added that the message of Islam to eradicate human trafficking and slavery, including Islam, recognizes the true freedom of all classes of people. Full rights and freedoms, especially for women and children, under the guidance of Allah.
