Donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit were handed over to 477 needy families in Pailin City
(Pailin): Donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, were handed over to 477 needy families in Pailin Sangkat, Pailin City.
The handover ceremony was held on the afternoon of May 20, 2023 by Mr. Yi Chhean, Honorary Chairman of the Pailin Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Pailin Province. This was attended by members of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross and the working group.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Yi Chhean brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always pay high attention to the well-being of all people regardless of color. Any color, religion, or political affiliation.
He expressed his deepest condolences to the parents and siblings now and emphasized that this gift is a show of care for all people from the leadership, especially the Cambodian Red Cross, which has Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun. Rany Hun Sen is the president, as mentioned, "The Cambodian Red Cross is everywhere for everyone - do not leave anyone behind" and "Where there is suffering, there is the Cambodian Red Cross."
Mr. Yi Chhean also reminded Grandma Oum Puming that this season is the end of the dry season and there is a lot of rain, so please be very careful of other disasters such as fire and wind. . In addition, health is very important, please pay close attention to personal health and young children, they are very susceptible to various diseases this season.
The Honorary President said that people who do not yet have an ID card or an expired ID card, please invite everyone to get an ID card. He added that there is peace, then we have everything like today, we all live under the shadow of peace, so let's unite to keep the peace.
Humanitarian donations provided to each family: 50 kg of rice, 1 bag of fish sauce, 1 box of noodles, 1 bag of fish and some money.
Prince Sar Kheng: Cambodia urgently needs peace and opposition to the return of war
(Battambang): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Battambang and Prey Veng Provinces, stated that Cambodia needs the most important thing: peace and opposition to the return of war.
During the meeting with 2,389 civil servants, retired armed forces and veterans in Banan district, Battambang province this morning, May 21, 2023, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng affirmed that in order to make peace In the long run, we must strengthen to keep this peace from falling into war.
On that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the civil servants, competent forces and authorities at all levels in Banan district who have worked hard to fulfill their roles and responsibilities. It has a high sense of responsibility to develop local districts, communes and villages in all areas and contribute to the success of the political program of the Royal Government.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also thanked and appreciated the working group of the Royal Government in Banan district at all levels for providing all kinds of support, both resources and spirit to make the Banan district administration and communes throughout the district more capable of development. Its base, especially the provision of public services to the people.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continued that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, policies and measures have been put in place with the support and active participation of government officials, competent forces, authorities at all levels and the people. All over the country, including in Banan district. Samdech also informed about the joint work direction of the Royal Government, including the work direction for 2023 and the direction for the next 5 years.
Samdech appealed to all people to be ready to vote for the 7th National Assembly on Sunday, July 23, 2023 for everyone to support the election for the Cambodian People's Party to continue to lead the country towards Towards better, safer, more peaceful, everything is up to date.
