(Phnom Penh): The Special Forces of the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police launched an operation to crack down on illegal drugs, arresting three female suspects along with four types of drugs weighing approximately 150 kg in Phnom Penh. And Kandal province.
Follow the orders of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and Gen. Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General for Anti-Drug Crimes, and Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes.
Speaking to Fresh News this morning, May 21, 2023, General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, confirmed that the operation was carried out on May 20, 2023 by the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes of the General. National Police Commission.
General Khieu Sopheak confirmed that during the drug crackdown operation, the specialized police force arrested three female suspects and confiscated four types of drugs weighing about 150 kilograms and a car.
The general also claimed that the National Police is currently conducting a search to arrest the ringleaders and their accomplices and oppose money laundering.
Please be informed that the specialized force of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes under the direct leadership of Lt. Gen. Khuong Sarath, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes has been actively working to crack down on drug crimes in 25 capitals and provinces throughout the country. Major drug trafficking offenses. Kandol Chrum Commune Residents Receive Free Medical Examination and Treatment by Volunteer Doctors in Ponhea Krek District
