Dr. Hun Manet Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony of Svay Tros Pagoda in Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): Dr. Hun Manet, Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, on May 20, 2023, inaugurated the boundary and inaugurated achievements in Po Rainsy Meanchey Pagoda Wat Svay Tros) is located in Boeung Tros Village, Phnom Touch Commune, Mongkul Borey District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Speaking on that occasion, Dr. Hun Manet said that peace is the common value of the Royal Government's efforts for the nation and the people. The basis for studying and evaluating the values and values that come from peace is made by comparing the past several generations with our present, which is a reality.
According to Hun Manet, the history we can recall is the glorious Angkorian period and the bitter period of the flames of war after Angkor. We do not live in the past, but we who drank the water must remember the source and be committed to preserving what is peace, freedom and all opportunities that are a blessing for the Cambodian people today.
In fact, after the liberation on January 7, 1979, there were only 2,000 pagodas and about 5,000 monks, but now there are more than 5,000 pagodas and more than 70,000 monks. Grandparents in Mongkol Borei district have been through five generations of regime, they know which generation is the best, happy generation, peaceful and able to celebrate happily and do not want the next generation After going through the bitterness of the past.
He added that the environment that allows us to develop and build many achievements as now depends on three main factors: peace, rights, freedom and progress of people's livelihood.
He emphasized that the field of religion has played an important role for the nation and its people in the education of life skills, both in personal life, in the family and in the society, on the basis of good morals and virtues. No religion teaches people to quarrel, but religion teaches people to love, respect, celebrate and be tolerant of each other, especially to help each other when there is a need or emergency.
Celebrating and practicing good religion consistently brings peace of mind and body. Physical peace teaches us to live peacefully, not to steal, not to do evil, not to discriminate, and to help one another in all circumstances. Peace of mind is to teach us to have a pure and pure heart without being tainted with all kinds of misfortunes.
At the same time, Dr. HUN Manet said that the success of Cambodia in hosting the 32nd SEA Games, which for the first time in the history of Cambodia is a national pride in both Cambodia and International environment.
