Over the years, the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, due to its adherence to the concept of "joint success", has attracted investment from enterprises around the world. Currently, a total of 175 enterprises from China, Southeast Asia, Europe and the United States have invested in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
The main activity of the company is to produce equestrian equipments and apparel with a production capacity of 22,000 equipments and equipments per month. These products are exported to Ireland, the US and European warehouses in Rotterdam, the Netherlands. In addition, the company also supplies goods directly to major customers from Germany, Belgium, Sweden and Sweden.
Mr. Lamar Thompson, CEO of the company, stated that the most important reason for his company to decide to invest in Sihanoukville SEZ is because Sihanoukville SEZ is close to Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, which is convenient for transportation. Can help reduce the cost of shipping the company.
After a year of construction, in 2014, the company officially began operations, mainly producing PVC Christmas trees and other Christmas gifts for export to the United States.
(Phnom Penh): Over the past 10 years, the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has attracted a total of 175 enterprises to invest and provide nearly 30,000 jobs, and the volume of exports and imports of local enterprises continues. Rise to a new high.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone laid the groundwork for the groundbreaking in February 2008. Since then, the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has accelerated construction. Especially since the "Belt and Road" initiative was launched ten years ago, the SEZ has seized this opportunity, striving to become a major project of the "Belt and Road" joint venture. Between China and Cambodia.
The past 10 years, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has achieved many fruitful development achievements, 10 years of construction of "One Belt and One Road" and also 10 years of rapid development and continuous improvement of the area. Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
For the past 10 years, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has adhered to the combination of building, development and structure of Cambodia's economic development, striving to attract active and grassroots industrial enterprises with original industrial enterprises, attracting large-scale enterprises. Large industries rely on port resources and support industries in the production chain to enhance regional industrial competitiveness.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone also developed strongly in 2013, with a total of 54 factories and factories with about 9,000 workers working in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has now become an international industrial park. Attracts 175 enterprises (companies) from China, Europe, the United States, Southeast Asia and other countries in the region, which has created nearly 30,000 job opportunities.
The volume of imports and exports of regional enterprises increased from $ 139 million in 2013 to $ 2.493 billion in 2022, which has become a strong impetus for Cambodia's economic and industrial development. To be the "engine" of the economic development of Sihanoukville and the "golden bowl" of the people.
Over the past 10 years, the development of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has boosted the development of the surrounding villages of the SEZ.
In addition, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone also conducts charitable activities every year through the "Cambodia-China Friendship Public Charitable Volunteer Organization".
At the same time, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone also acts as a full bridge to promote exchanges and practical cooperation between Sihanoukville and Jiangsu Province in areas such as economy, trade, health care, education and culture. Promoted people-to-people contacts between the two places effectively.
In the field of health, the Jiangsu Provincial People's Administration has sent a team of foreign aid doctors from Jiangsu Province to visit and treat patients in Sihanoukville and other places for free six times in a row and to examine and treat you. Nearly 8,300 people in Sihanoukville.
In December 2021, Wuxi People's Hospital and Sihanoukville Special Area Health Post began jointly implementing a remote video consultation project. For the education sector, the Jiangsu Provincial Administration has donated computer rooms to the Sihanoukville-Jiangsu Friendship Trap Primary and Secondary School, as well as classrooms, basketball courts and water supply forums.
The Red Cross of Jiangsu Province and the Red Cross of Wuxi City have donated libraries, kindergartens, toilets, etc. to further improve the school's teaching environment.
