Ministry of Health and Relevant Ministries Inspect the Treatment and Rehabilitation of Drug Addicts at the National Center for Drug Treatment Services in Keo Phos Commune, Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): A delegation from the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation led by Dr. Ker Ratha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, on May 19, 2023, inspected the treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts at the National Center. Provides voluntary and community-based drug treatment services in Rithy 2 Village, Keo Phos Commune, Stung Hav District, Preah Sihanouk Province.
Mr. KER Ratha said that the inspection of the treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts at the National Center in order to strengthen cooperation and coordination in promoting the treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts by Volunteer and community-based for the better.
Drugs have caused many problems to the society besides security and social safety. Drug use has become another new public health issue that the world is paying attention to and incorporating into sustainable development goals. Drug addiction is also a chronic health problem that is difficult to treat, and after treatment, drug addicts often relapse several times before reaching drug cessation. Absolutely addictive.
So far, the treatment of drug addicts in Cambodia has been diverse, using different approaches, and in the past, the Ministry of Health, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and the National Authority for Combating Drugs have provided training on treatment and Rehabilitation of drug addicts to health and social workers who already work at the National Center.
Through the training at that time, new knowledge was provided to both health and social workers to support the provision of better quality and efficiency services, which will lead us to a model approach that is ideal for the country. Cambodia (Best practice) to qualify the National Center for the Treatment and Rehabilitation of Drug Addicts Voluntarily and Community-Based.
Dr. stated that with the attention and support of His Excellency Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Chairman of the Committee in charge of the treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts, the process of treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts. Voluntary and community-based in this national center, well done responsibly.
The Ministry of Health, through the General Department of Health Technology, which has the Department of Mental Health and Substance Abuse, will continue to provide technical support through regular training and technical inspections through regular governance to strengthen treatment capacity. Drug addicts to health officials working in this center to have better capacity.
The Health Department of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration will receive support from His Excellency the Board of Governors of Preah Sihanouk Province to receive more staff and budget to support the process.
The Department of Health must prepare drug plans, equipment and urine tests for drugs according to specific needs and request training for new staff. However, we still have a long way to go, going through many challenges that need to be addressed together, including human resources issues, budget issues, and service quality assurance, which are important factors in determining The standard of effective service.
Fire at M Star Embedery factory in Sen Sok district, the authorities used 10 trucks of water to control
