Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that after receiving information from residents reporting to professional officers, he immediately ordered all fire trucks. All targets work out fire trucks to intervene as well.
Colonel Prohm Yorn continued that in the above operation, the specialized force immediately intervened and sprayed water, in which our specialized police force sprayed water to prevent the flames from spreading further.
During the above operation, the specialized police force used nearly 20 fire trucks, including 18 fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Office, using 9 trucks of water and 1 truck of Cambodia Beer Company using 1 truck of water.
