Reuters reports that after the first agreement of the US-Taiwan Trade Initiative on the 21st Century was signed, negotiations will begin on other more complex trade sectors, including agriculture and trade. Digital services, standards and working environment, state enterprises and non-market policies and practices.
US Trade Representative Katherine Tai said in a statement that the agreement strengthens US-Taiwan relations and shows that the two countries can work together to accelerate trade priorities for the people. Its.
"We look forward to continuing these negotiations and concluding a strong trade agreement and a high standard that addresses economic challenges in the 21st century," Tai said.
In a statement, Taiwan's Trade Negotiation Bureau called the agreement "historically significant" and said Taiwan intends to conclude negotiations on all remaining issues by the end of this year.
The deal is not expected to change tariffs, but proponents of the deal say it would strengthen US-Taiwan economic ties, open the island to more US exports and boost the economy. Increase Taiwan's ability to withstand economic pressure from China. According to Reuters.
