Liu Pengyu, a spokesman for the Chinese Embassy in Washington, made the announcement at a press conference held by the Chinese embassy. He added that Beijing is open to all levels of relations with the United States, but only on the basis of mutual respect.
The Chinese embassy later said in an emailed statement that the two sides were still discussing the details of the plan, Reuters reported.
Spokesmen for Ms. Tai and Ms. Ray Mondo did not respond to a request for comment from the news agency.
Washington has expressed eagerness to hold high-level meetings with China in an effort to prevent escalating tensions from escalating into conflict.
