Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News that the owner of the house that caught fire was 46-year-old Kuch Vanny, a furniture owner. Type of construction: 7 meters by 20 meters, galvanized steel structure.
Colonel Prohm Yorn continued that in the case of the fire in the back, it caused the fire to damage the equipment in the back about 30%, but did not cause the fire to spread to the neighbor's house. As for the rescue operation, Colonel Prohm Yorn confirmed that 5 specialized office vehicles use 2 water trucks and 2 70th Brigade vehicles use 2 vehicles.
