The Council of Ministers approves the "Draft Law on Civil Statistics, Statistics and Identification" (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): After reviewing and discussing, the Cabinet fully approved the "Draft Law on Civil Statistics, Statistics and Identification" in The meeting will be chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Friday morning, May 19, 2023.
Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, said that the preparation of the "Draft Law on Civil Statistics, Statistics and Identification" aims to amend any legal provisions that are not yet appropriate. In addition, new regulations have been added and new systems have been introduced, such as the Common Identity System (IPIS).
The Minister said that the draft law brings together all the legal standards related to civil status, statistics, civil status and identification to be integrated into a single law, which was previously under different legal standards. Combining all the provisions into one law makes it easy for users and law enforcers alike.
The draft law incorporates provisions relating to the basic rights and obligations of citizens to ensure its robustness is protected by law.
According to Mr. Phay Siphan, this draft law is a new achievement that is designed not only to be able to respond to the problems encountered during the past implementation, but also to ensure transparency in the provision of services and Prepared up-to-date regulations in line with developments in society, as well as prepared predictions for the future advancement of digital technology.
This draft law applies to all people living in the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Cambodians living abroad as well.
The draft law on civil status, statistics, civil status and identification has 12 chapters and 182 articles as follows:
