The British multinational telecommunications company (BT) on Thursday announced plans to cut 55,000 jobs by 2030, accounting for about 40 percent of its global workforce. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Thursday, May 18, 2023.
The company said the shutdown was partly due to adaptation to new technologies, including artificial intelligence.
The new technology will play a bigger role in areas such as call management and network diagnostics, making the job less labor-intensive, the company said.
