The White House and Republicans in Congress are facing the question of how much the White House, which manages the US government, can borrow.
The US House of Representatives is responsible for determining the current debt of $ 31.4 trillion. The debt ceiling has risen more than 78 times since 1960. Debt ceilings are sometimes seen as suspending the government for a short period of time and then resuming at a higher cost level, further raising the debt ceiling.
The U.S. government has approved a series of stimulus bills to offset the worst effects of the pandemic, which eventually totaled $ 5 trillion.
Now that the two sides have not changed their stance on concessions, the stalemate is expected to bring the US economy closer to disaster. However, on Wednesday, Joe Biden expressed confidence that an agreement could be reached soon with Republican leaders to avoid a catastrophic debt crisis.
