(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, expressed optimism that the tourism vocational school under construction at these two locations will help promote the development of human resources in the tourism sector and promote better tourism services.
It should be informed that the Royal Government is building the first two tourism vocational schools in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville to provide human resource training in tourism.
On the morning of May 18, 2023, Minister Thong Khon inspected and encouraged the workers, engineers and team at the construction site of Tourism Vocational School in Phnom Penh (near Aeon Mall Sen Sok).
On that occasion, the Minister said that one of the main goals of the Ministry of Tourism is to train human resources in the tourism sector, so Cambodia needs to have special tourism vocational training schools in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville, Siem Reap and other provinces with tourism potential.
"The construction of this tourism vocational training school will help promote the development of human resources in the tourism sector, promote better tourism services," he said.
"If you want to start a tourism business, each business owner must have at least a basic level of tourism professional staff or a manager who has completed tourism professional training."
Mr. Chhay Khunlong, Director of the Vocational School of Tourism, said that the construction of the building in Phnom Penh began on December 15, 2022, while in Sihanoukville began on January 3, 2023. So far, the construction of school buildings in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville has exceeded the plan, so the construction project may be completed before or in April 2024.
Mr. Chhay Khunlong used to say that the school will provide a reasonable price for this study, about $ 600-700 per year. In addition, the school also plans to provide some scholarships to poor students and seek cooperation with financial institutions to provide loans to students who want to study tourism vocational skills at this national school, as well as raise funds to provide funding to those students. .
