As technology advances and there are many scams on the Internet, a spokesman for the Ministry of Defense urges all social media users to be careful and research before publishing or distributing any allegations. To affect the honor of the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense. Mob Leader Demonstrates Breaking CNRP 2013 Election Fraud Plan (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Even though it has been almost 10 years, they may not have forgotten about the eruption of protests and attacks in the polling stations during the 5th National Assembly election by supporters of the former party National Rescue.
The political battle in Cambodia in 2013 can be considered as a hot battle and there is a fierce competition between the CPP and the former CNRP.
On the evening of July 28, 2013, after each polling station closed and the ballots were counted, many surprises occurred. Many polling stations in Phnom Penh have been attacked by former CNRP supporters for alleged irregularities. Election officials at some polling stations were also detained by former CNRP supporters.
To make matters worse, violence erupted between former CNRP supporters and police in front of Stung Meanchey pagoda, leading to the arrest of police and the burning of military police vehicles. On election night, there was also a roadblock at the Kbal Thnal flyover by former CNRP supporters.
At first glance, it could be seen as a protest demanding justice for the election by former CNRP supporters. However, it is not known whether the former CNRP leaders' malicious intentions disrupted the election and created an excuse for illegal activities to seize power from the winning party.
The good, the bad, the black and the white cannot be hidden forever, that is, things will be revealed over time, just sooner or later. Ten years after the water became clear, the truth was also exposed to the evil and poisonous tricks of the former CNRP.
Korom Dala was one of the leaders in mobilizing intellectual students to take part in the protests organized by the CNRP at the time. Korom Dala was also involved in protests at the polling station and in the clashes in front of Stung Meanchey pagoda.
In a press conference, Mr. Kor Dala revealed that all the protests at the polling stations were organized by the former CNRP leader. He cited the example of a polling station in Meanchey district where former CNRP supporters forced election officials to recognize invalid ballots. In addition, they detained election officials for not following them.
According to Korom Dala, both the violence in front of Stung Meanchey pagoda and the violence on Veng Sreng Road were organized by former CNRP leaders. Their intention is to use mass force to seize power from the CPP.
