World Bank: Cambodia's economy is gaining momentum towards a full recovery of 5.5% this year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodia's economy is gaining momentum towards a full recovery due to There was a boost from exports and growth in services and agriculture. The World Bank says so in its latest report on the Cambodian economy, released on May 18, 2023.
However, a prolonged slowdown in overseas demand could weaken manufacturing for export, and continued global financial tightening could pose a risk to Cambodia's financial sector. Rely heavily on outside capital for investment.
"In order to sustain Cambodia's economic recovery, it is necessary to diversify our products and tourism destinations," said Mariam Salim, World Bank Country Manager for Cambodia. At the same time, Cambodia also needs to increase its competitiveness by expanding its transport network, reducing trade barriers and streamlining customs procedures.
For the medium term, the economy is expected to grow by 6%, supported by the dynamic momentum of exports of goods and services and by increasing investment, especially under the public-private partnership. On major infrastructure projects, such as seaports and roads.
The report says Cambodia can drive this growth by investing in infrastructure connectivity and human resource development, ensuring financial stability and promoting export diversification to expand the resilience of the economy and its competitiveness. Body.
The Economic Update focuses on short- and medium-term economic developments and is published twice a year.
