(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Representative of the Royal Government of Cambodia, on the morning of May 18, 2023, signed the Public-Private Partnership Agreement for the Highways Infrastructure Project. Connect from Phnom Penh to Bavet with Mr. Zhou Yong, Representative of China Road and Bridge Corporation (CRBC) at the Ministry.
At the same time, this PPP contract is also prepared and implemented under the framework of PPP law and legal documents in force and based on the principle of non-guarantee for the project and maintain "B" and the terms of the contract as the Phnom Penh-Krong Expressway project. Sihanouk, according to the noble decision of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the project to build a 135.10-kilometer expressway from Phnom Penh to Bavet, with four lanes passing through Kandal, Prey Veng and Svay Rieng provinces, was built with an investment capital of approximately one. $ 35 billion and a four-year construction period, funded by the China Roads and Bridges Corporation (CRBC) and managing the road business for 50 years before being handed over to the government.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, to cross the bridge to the expressway, a 3,700-meter-long bridge over the Mekong River at the point where it connects from the Third Ring Road to Lvea Em District requires budget. Nation to build more than 200 million dollars for people to cross the bridge to each other free of charge.
Please be informed that the financing for the construction of the bridge across the Mekong River will be sourced from the national budget, with the construction contract being given to the same CRBC company, which will lead to free transportation across the bridge. The construction of this bridge must be completed before or simultaneously with the opening of the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway in accordance with "B" and the conditions as stated in the PPP agreement.
Please note that the infrastructure of the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway will be connected with Vietnam's Ho Chi Minh-Mok Bai Expressway project, which is expected to be completed at the same time.
The Phnom Penh-Bavet Second Expressway Project will officially open its groundbreaking ceremony on June 7, 2023 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Siem Reap City plans to complete the feasibility study by the end of May, and plans to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) soon.
Drug bust arrests Chinese man, seizes nearly 5 kilograms of drugs and more than 40 kilograms of chemicals
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Drug Department of the National Police launched an operation to crack down on drug offenses by arresting a Chinese suspect and confiscating nearly 5 kilograms of drugs and more than 40 kilograms of chemicals, including drugs. Not clear than the other 53 kg in Phnom Penh.
The crackdown follows orders from National Police General Neth Savoeun, Deputy National Police Commissioner, and Gen. Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner for Anti-Drug Crimes, and Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, director of the Anti-Drug Department.
According to the report of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes obtained by Fresh News on May 18, 2023, this operation took place on May 14, 2023 at house No. 37, Phum Tek Panha, Sangkat Samrong Krom. Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, the suspect is named Zhou Guochao, male, Chinese nationality.
The confiscated items include 4 kilograms of 684 grams of methamphetamine, 3 kilograms of chemical compounds, 40 kilograms of chemical substances and 53 kilograms of unspecified substances.
Currently, the suspect and the exhibits have been sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court by the specialized force of the Anti-Drug Department to build a case.
Please be informed that the specialized force of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes under the direct leadership of Lt. Gen. Kheung Sarath has launched operations to crack down on drug crimes like rain all over the country every day, especially major drug trafficking crimes.
