Contrary to Cambodia's practice, Samdech Techo Prime Minister cited the practice of some countries by using equality measures. For example, 20% of the population is vaccinated, so 20% of the population is divided into provinces, but 20 out of 100 people are vaccinated.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Because each country has different measures, some countries use equality measures, but we use the approach that starts watering in Phnom Penh and Kandal province to succeed." So there is a vaccine and it is not certain that the situation can be controlled if the wrong measures are taken. This is a closed experiment to be compiled for later.
