Meanwhile, the envoy of President Joe Biden, Joseph Yun, told reporters at a ceremony that an agreement with Palau would be officially signed next week in Papua New Guinea, while an agreement with Macedonia would also be signed. Must be signed at the same time.
Joe Biden initially planned to attend the signing ceremony, but on Tuesday the White House said he had canceled a visit to Papua New Guinea due to public debt problems in the United States. . Some analysts believe the decision will undermine Pacific island nations' confidence in the United States.
