This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen handed over diplomas to more than 1,000 medical students
The University of Health Sciences is a state-run educational institution that trains health professionals. The University of Health Sciences has been fully accredited for 5 years from 2019 to 2023 by the Accreditation Commission of Cambodia.
In addition to training and research, the university has expanded to provide health services to people in the community, especially the university has cooperated with Samdech Techo's team of volunteer youth doctors, HE Hun Many's team of volunteer doctors to provide medical services. Free of charge to people in the community.
From 1980 to the present, 31,202 students have successfully graduated from the University of Health Sciences. To date, the university has sent 1,207 students for internships and pursuing master's and doctoral degrees abroad, including in France, Belgium, the United States, Australia, Japan and Korea.
According to the Minister, a survey by the University of Health Sciences among graduates from 2020 to 2022 shows that 97% of the population is employed.
Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen hands over diplomas to more than 1,000 medical students
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, May 18, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will preside over the graduation ceremony for medical students. A study of 1,396 people from the University of Health Sciences. The ceremony will take place at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
