On the occasion of presiding with Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen on the night of May 17, 2023 to officially close the 32nd SEA Games hosted by Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen affirmed that What has been organized here is clearly a so-called "sport of living in peace", because without peace it is not possible to organize this great event.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said excitedly, "Today we really understand what the meaning of sports is to live under peace. If you want to organize such a ceremony, it is necessary to work with the Royal Government to protect peace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that the success of hosting the 32nd SEA Games, which Cambodia has been proud of for 64 years, is now a common achievement of the Cambodian people. This also shows the solidarity and friendship among ASEAN countries.
Proudly speaking, Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who took his life as a capital to liberate the country from the flames of war until peace and development as it is today, expressed his desire to see Cambodia host a great event now Again in 2043, for the next 20 years.
It should be informed that after 16 days of hard competition with joy and brotherhood, the 32nd SEA Games 2023, which was held for the first time in Cambodia in 64 years, has closed completely. As the host, Cambodia ranked fourth with a total of 282 medals, including 81 gold, 74 silver and 127 bronze medals.
The SEA Games in Cambodia has attracted a lot of attention and also left a lot of good memories for the Southeast Asian nation, the spirit of the SEA Games.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen apologizes to Cambodians and foreign friends for any inadvertent mistakes in organizing the 32nd SEA Games (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Although the 32nd SEA Games ended successfully and proudly However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on behalf of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has not forgotten to apologize to the Cambodian people and foreign friends if there is an unintentional mistake in organizing this first event.
This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen presided over the closing ceremony of the 32nd SEA Games 2023, which is hosted by Cambodia. House on the night of May 16, 2023.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "I also apologize to the Cambodian people as well as our friends among ASEAN, if any mistakes happen unintentionally, we will be ready to accept criticism to build and Improve for the future.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked all foreign friends who have contributed to Cambodian sports from the beginning until the current SEA Games.
After failing to host the SEA Games several times over the past 64 years due to the crisis of war and the need to rebuild the country from the flames of war, Cambodia has achieved its goals and ambitions. The SEA Games in 2023. The tournament started on April 29 and the official opening ceremony was held on May 5.
In organizing the 32nd SEA Games, the Royal Government of Cambodia has covered the cost of accommodation, meals and transportation of delegates, and decided not to sell tickets to the competition, which makes foreigners Very appreciative that Cambodia is a small country but has a big heart.
(Phnom Penh): At almost 7 pm on May 16, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen arrived at the Moradok Techo National Stadium to close the SEA Games. 32nd, 2023, which Cambodia hosts.
The closing ceremony of the spectacular SEA Games in Cambodia was also attended by national and international sports leaders, sports delegates from 11 countries and a total of 60,000 national and international guests.
The SEA Games in Cambodia has generated a lot of interest and also left a lot of good memories for the Southeast Asian nation in the spirit of the SEA Games.
Mr. Thong Khon, Permanent Vice President of the National Organizing Committee of the SEA Games and President of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia, the organization of the SEA Games in Cambodia has brought a lot of prominence, including the request for the sport (fire sports), The Parade of Sports, the opening of the SEA Games (Olympic level), especially the admission fee, no live broadcast and no money from the sports delegation.
Mr. Thong Khon reminded that the SEA Games in Cambodia is also highly appreciated and appreciated by sports delegations from all countries, including the organization of competitions, hospitality, accommodation and food.
Mr. Thong Khon claimed that the SEA Games in Cambodia also received high attention from the media, both national and international, which made the event even more popular. In particular, it has contributed to promoting Cambodia more to the international arena.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the 20th SEA Games in 1999, Cambodia was ranked 10th with zero medals.
Samdech Techo considered this achievement to belong to the whole Cambodian nation, which strives to stand up for nation building in general and in sports in particular.
Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, said that as a Cambodian citizen, he is very proud and appreciates all the team in all areas, all dedicated to physical, mental, time and personal resources. There is also a group of young volunteers who seem to be the lifeblood of the Southeast Asian Games from before the start to the end.
Mr. Hun Many would like to thank the many other relevant technical teams who participated in this great mission. In particular, forces at all levels that protect the safety, security and order for athletes, participants and foreign friends to come to Cambodia with brotherhood, happiness and fun beyond the competition.
He added that the participation of all of you has really contributed to the hosting of the 32nd SEA Games to be a proud success in the spirit of Cambodia.
