The United Nations forecast is lower than the International Monetary Fund (IMF) forecast earlier this year that global economic growth will slow to 2.9 percent in 2023 from 3.4 percent. 2022 and for 2024 will increase slightly to 3.1 percent.
The United Nations said that although the outlook for the United States, the European Union and China has improved, "for many developing countries, the outlook for growth has slowed amid tightening credit conditions and growth." "External financing costs."
