Processed duck beak snails or duck beak shells are very popular and increase the income of local people.
(Koh Kong): The Peam Krasop community in Peam Krasop commune, Mondul Seima district, Koh Kong province, has expanded from a beekeeper or duck beak cluster to a processor for export to the market with strong support. Provide employment opportunities for local communities to earn additional income.
Mr. Vong Dara said that he started raising duck beak shells as a family for 27 years and recently started to open an enterprise to produce and process duck beak shells to a standard for distribution and export. Abroad.
Mr. Dara described that in the process of processing shellfish for export, his handicrafts are sold whole, half-shelled and pureed. It takes 10 to 12 months for ducks to be harvested before they can be harvested and sold on the market.
Mr. Vong Dara said: "Currently, the market has improved because the officials of the Ministry of Environment and other stakeholders have found the market and helped to promote the people of Phnom Penh and the provinces to know the duck beak. Today, there are customers who own marts, supermarkets and other restaurants in Phnom Penh, ordering for distribution.
He stated that in one day, his craft can take 200 to 300 kilograms of shells to cook for the meat to send to the supermarket. With 10 kg shells, we can process 1 kg of shellfish meat. While the price of shells per kilogram is between 3,000 riel and processed, he can sell 1 kg for 40,000 riel.
Net Pheaktra, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that for the Peam Krasop community, 150 families raised about 60 hectares of snail-beaked ducks. With a harvest of between 2,000 and 3,000 tons per year. In addition to the current breeding, the Peam Krasop community has expanded to create this handicraft to process the duck beak for distribution in the market, with strong support from consumers.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra also urged the handicraft processing of snails, duck beak or duck beak to comply with hygiene standards to ensure that this processed product has the support of customers. At the same time, he also thanked the relevant ministries and institutions for providing support to the Peam Krasom community.
The senior official of the Ministry of Environment said that the protection and conservation of the mangrove forest, which is a natural resource, is also the basis for expansion as well as ensuring the sustainability of various resources for the benefit of the people in the community. Yes and so on.
It should be noted that Vong Dara's duck beak handicraft received an investment package from UNIDO to support the production process to be competitive and meet export market standards.
