Mr. Hun Manet inspires the new generation of young people to study hard for a lifetime in a peaceful society
(Kratie): Mr. Hun Manet, Chairman of the Scholarship Committee for Poor Students, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit encouraged Cambodian students and youth to continue their studies for life as the country has already achieved complete peace Before, there were not many opportunities to study because the country was in a state of war.
This warning was made on the occasion of Mr. HUN Manet at the graduation ceremony for the winners of the University of Management and Economics (UME) in Kratie province, a total of 800 students on May 16, 2023.
He joined in congratulating the graduates and graduates after many years of hard work and study. He considers that this is also a new step in life to get a formal certification of qualifications as a quality human capital who is actively involved in social, religious and working in ministries - government institutions. Private sector and NGOs.
Mr. Hun Manet encouraged Cambodian students and young people to continue their education for the rest of their lives while the country is as peaceful as it is today, because in the days when our parents and grandparents were at war, there were not many opportunities to study.
"This is a source of great pride for the whole family, especially for some families whose parents did not have the opportunity to study during a time when the country was in turmoil," he said.
Mr. Hun Manet instructed all students to continue to study hard throughout their lives, either to hone their skills or acquire new skills to meet the needs of the labor market, especially in the context of the Industrial Revolution 4.0. Which will bring opportunities for growth and socio-economic development.
(Phnom Penh): The 32nd Southeast Asian Games, also known as the SEA Games, held for the first time in Cambodia, will officially close on Wednesday, May 17, 2023. Although it was held for the first time after many failures in 64 years, Cambodia has been praised from all directions for organizing this event well, especially reviving the spirit of the Olympic Games.
In an interview with Fresh News, Mr. Thong Khon, Permanent Vice President of the National Organizing Committee of the SEA Games and President of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia, said that hosting the SEA Games is always a challenge and a time. Difficult because of the prevalence of the Kovid 19 crisis.
Mr. Thong Khon emphasized that despite the difficulties caused by the Kovid 19 crisis, the spirit of building national pride has urged the National Organizing Committee to work together to overcome all difficulties and eventually organize the SEA Games. Planning.
Mr. Thong Khon, Permanent Vice President of the National Organizing Committee of the SEA Games, emphasized that the organization of the SEA Games in Cambodia has brought many highlights, including the request for the Fire Victory (Fireball), the Fire Parade Sports, the opening of the SEA Games (Olympic level), especially free admission, no live broadcast and no money from the sports delegation.
According to Thong Khon, during the SEA Games, Cambodia receives about 16,000 international tourists a day.
As one of the executives of the SEA Games, Mr. Thong Khon expressed his happiness and pride.
