(Koh Kong): Officials from the Ministry of Environment, Koh Kong Provincial Authority, civil society organizations, journalists and relevant departments, as well as more than 500 students this morning, May 16, 2023, marched to open the second zero trap campaign in Koh Kong province. .
The second Zero Trap campaign was held to mark World Endangered Species Day. The second phase of the Zero Trap Campaign will run for five months from March 3 to July 2023 and will be implemented in five provinces: Kampong Speu, Pursat, Koh Kong, Battambang, Pailin and Siem Reap.
The second Trap Zero Campaign in Koh Kong Province aims to reduce and prevent the number of traps in protected areas in Kampong Speu Province as well as in protected areas in Cambodia and to cultivate a greater love for wildlife in Among the public.
The Opening Ceremony of the Second Zero Trap Campaign in Koh Kong Province was led by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign and Koh Kong provincial leaders at all levels.
It should also be noted that the trap crisis is not unique to Cambodia. According to the WWF 2020 report, an estimated 12 million traps are present in the protected areas of several other countries in Southeast Asia, such as Laos, Vietnam, Malaysia and Indonesia. According to the same report, these traps are the source of the loss of some rare animals such as big tigers, leopards, tigers, clouds, wild dogs, bears and so on.
