(Koh Kong): Eddie Lefter, Chief of Law Enforcement Division of the Cardamom Mountain Wildlife Conservation Program of the Wildlife Alliance, has expressed his belief that through the introduction of strict enforcement plans and government economic measures for Local communities will reduce crime against natural resources.
Addressing the media during a visit to the Koh Kong Provincial Rice Farm on May 15, 2023, led by Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Neth Pheaktra and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, Eddie Lefter emphasized: "Natural resource crime remains. "It simply came to our notice then. There was a slight decrease, but we stopped and observed a decrease."
"The Royal Government of Cambodia has issued a strict order to prevent the destruction of natural resources, and we believe that this strong message will lead to the destruction of natural resources," he said. Will decrease.
Mr. Pheaktra said that through the measures put in place by the Ministry of Environment and the Wildlife Alliance (WA), which are cooperating in conserving the area, the protected areas in the province, especially in the range Cardamom Mountain has improved and the location is also part of a carbon credit sale.
The ministry is also strengthening the effectiveness of conservation through the introduction of local community development plans, which are funded to strengthen law enforcement and strengthen economic development for local communities, the official said.
APSARA Authority plans to study and preserve the ancient road from Phnom Bakheng to Rolous area, Prasat Bakong district
(Siem Reap): The Apsara Authority plans to study and preserve the ancient road from the front of Phnom Bakheng to the Rolous area of Prasat Bakong district, from the former capital of Yasodharapura to the former capital of Hariharalaya.
In order to implement this project, on the morning of May 15, 2023, the management of APSARA Authority led by Mr. Hang Pov, Director General of APSARA Authority signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Eben Living Solution led by Mr. Kean Kimleang, CEO of APSARA Authority. To implement a joint study project to preserve and enhance the ancient road from the front of Phnom Bakheng to Rolous area.
