8 restaurants in Koh Kong town announced not to sell wild meat dishes to customers
(Koh Kong): By promoting awareness of the value of wildlife and the legal challenges of using wild meat in detail to cook and sell to customers, eight restaurant owners in Koh Kong province have announced that Sell food made from wild meat to customers, even if customers order and pay a high price.
This was announced by Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign during the press conference on the Second Trap Zero Campaign in Koh Kong Province on the afternoon of May 15, 2023.
With the launch of the Zero Trap Campaign in Koh Kong Province, in addition to the above restaurant owners, people and the public from all walks of life have promised to bring their awareness of the benefits of natural resources and wildlife to families, relatives and Its friends, too.
To date, there are more than 86 restaurants in eight provinces: Kratie, Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Pursat, Kampong Speu and Koh Kong. Hunting and slaughtering wildlife in protected areas and wildlife conservation.
