Ms. Chea Serey encourages young people to choose sports according to their skills and passions and stay away from drugs and social inactivity
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chea Serey, Deputy Governor General of the National Bank of Cambodia and First Vice President of the Central Working Group for Santuk District, encouraged young people to choose sports according to their skills and hobbies and stay away from Drugs and inactivity in society.
Ms. Chea Serey made this remark during the opening match of the friendly football match between the youth of Prasat and Kampong Thmor communes on May 15, 2023.
District Assistance Team and Santuk District Party Youth Team Organized Friendly Football Match between Prasat and Kampong Thmor Youth to Celebrate the 32nd SEA Games Hosted by Cambodia and to Expand Youth-to-Youth Cooperation To be even better.
The friendly football match between the youths of Prasat and Kampong Thmor communes will be held on May 14, 2023. The competition will end during the fourth week of June 2023, in which for the first prize winner will receive a budget. 1 million Riel, 2nd place 700,000 Riels and 3rd place 500,000 Riels.
Mr. Long Kiseng, President of Santuk District Party, considered that the presence of Ms. Chea Serey in the opening match of the friendly football match between the youth of Prasat and Kampong Thmor communes today clearly shows the noble values of the leaders of both parties and the state, who always Connect with young people at all levels and, through this, increase trust and deep emotional connection with local youth.
