Phnom Penh Authority Holds a Meeting to Focus on Public Order Both Inside and Outside the Techo Heritage National Stadium for the Closing Day of the 32nd Asian Games
(Phnom Penh): As the opening ceremony of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games was attended by more people, both inside and outside the Techo National Stadium, Phnom Penh authorities urged further strengthening of security and order on the closing day. This sports event to make the event on May 17 run smoothly and successfully for the nation.
The promotion of the above work was held on the afternoon of May 15, 2023 in the closing meeting of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games at Phnom Penh Capital Hall chaired by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and With the participation of the 14 district authorities and the competent forces of both types.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said, "Security work is important for all of us, as the competent authorities, to pay close attention to, even though on the opening day of the Games we were successful and appreciated. "From all walks of life."
In addition, for the live broadcast of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games, the seven locations must also be better organized for people to visit. The meeting also focused on maintaining order both inside and outside the Techo Heritage National Stadium, as more people attended than the authorities and forces had to prepare in advance.
General Chev Hak, Deputy Commissioner of Phnom Penh, confirmed that on the opening day of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games and the 12th Para Games, the number of people participating in and outside the Techo Heritage National Stadium was limited by the inside. 50,000 to about 60,000 outside the stadium, another 20,000, a total of about 80,000.
But for the closing day of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games, there may be more participants than at the opening. Therefore, we must further strengthen the instructions of the Governor, both in terms of security and order, so that the event on May 17 will run smoothly and successfully for our country.
It should be noted that on May 17, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen will preside over the closing ceremony of the SEA Games.
