Traffic accident in Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province, caused 5 deaths and 3 injuries, today, the provincial governor brought gifts from Samdech Kittipritthbandit to attend the victims' festival
(Kampong Cham): On the afternoon of May 15, 2023, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, led his colleagues to visit and offer condolences to the families of five potato workers in Doun Tor village, Tuol Preah Khleang commune, Stung Trang district. Five people were killed in a traffic accident between a car and a bulldozer.
On that occasion, Mr. Un Chanda expressed his deepest condolences and condolences to the families of the five workers for the loss of their husbands, parents, dear sisters who lost their lives in this unexpected traffic accident.
The provincial governor sent a message of sympathy from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who was always concerned and considerate of the people who are vulnerable to disasters. Assign representatives to intervene, alleviate difficulties, help share grief in time, in line with the slogan "Where there is suffering, there is the Cambodian Red Cross."
With this, Mr. Un Chanda encouraged the families of the five corpses to try to control their emotions and maintain good health by working hard to earn a living to improve the family life. For the three injured people who are being treated at the provincial hospital, Mr. Un Chanda advised the hospital to take care of the treatment by the branch in charge of services and assigned the branch director to visit more.
Please note that the donation of Samdech President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the families of 5 victims, each family received: 50 kg of rice, 2 cases of pure water, 2 cases of orange juice, 20 cases of fish, 2 cases of noodles and 1,000 budget. , 000 Riels. Separately, Stung Trang District Red Cross Sub-Branch also donated 25 kg of rice, pure water, fish sauce, soy sauce and some money to each family.
