According to the NEC decision, as of May 08, 2023, the NEC has received a total of 20 applications for registration of political parties. According to the law, the NEC has seven days to review 10 documents. In accordance with Article 27 of the Law on the Election of Members of the National Assembly, all political parties have five days to fill in the missing and corrected documents after receiving the NEC's request.
A party that meets all the conditions set by the NEC is officially registered, and if any party does not meet all the conditions, the NEC decides not to register the party. In this regard, the NEC found that 15 parties had submitted sufficient and correct documents in accordance with the requirements of the law, and the NEC decided to approve the registration of these 15 parties.
Separately, a total of five parties, including the Khmer Anti-Poverty Party, the Khmer Economic Development Party, the Candlelight Party, the Women's Party for Women and the Khmer National Unity Party, received requests to complete and correct the documents. Fulfilled all the conditions, the NEC decided to recognize and register, except for the Candlelight Party, which did not do enough and the NEC decided to reject the registration of the Candlelight Party on the morning of May 15, 2023.
A statement from the NEC stated that the remaining party, the Khmer National Unity Party, which he still had due to the NEC's lack of documents and requested a supplement on May 13, 2023. . The NEC implements only one standard: the law, the law is strict, but it is the law.
During the meeting, Mr. Ith Sam Heng praised the efforts of the Czech Republic to strengthen and provide good cooperation in the field of labor, especially in the field of technical and vocational training and the National Employment Agency.
