Businesses in Indonesia, China, Thailand and Vietnam are looking to increase their revenue and profits in international markets, but the same report also showed that among respondents in Hong Kong, Malaysia and Singapore, both companies That is, there is reluctance to expand overseas.
About half of the respondents said that Singapore was the main country in Southeast Asia for business expansion, followed by Thailand (45%) and Malaysia (45%). Nearly 80% of respondents said the current business environment in the region was positive.
Meanwhile, the report shows that only one in four companies wants to expand beyond Asia.
By sector, companies in the oil and gas industry (88%) expressed strong interest in expanding overseas, followed by wholesalers, technology, media and telecommunications.
The report notes that most businesses have raised the need for more support for overseas investment due to a number of challenges, including a lack of local skilled staff, the difficulty of finding a good partner to work with. Together with the lack of compliance with laws and regulations and tax support. According to the Bangkok Post.
Eric Lian, Head of Commercial Banking at UOB, said: “Businesses in China want to connect with industry partners and have access to in-depth analysis and business data. "Companies in Southeast Asia have said they want more tax incentives and more sustainable financing options."
In that message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that from May 16, 1945 to May 16, 2023, it has been 78 years since a law enforcement body was established and Named the "National Police" under the noble handiwork of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King in order to strengthen security, public order and social security.
At the same time, I would like to send my best wishes and greetings to the National Police officers who are injured and are being treated at hospitals, health centers or homes. Unit.
