Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport is a 4E International Airport with a turnover of 3,600 meters, capable of landing all types of aircraft, equipped with the latest technology for safety and security for passengers. The airport has up to 38 airports.
When launched in October 2023, the airport will be able to handle about 7 million passengers a year. The second phase can handle up to 10 million passengers a year and the third phase can handle up to 20 million passengers a year.
