(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, May 15, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the graduation ceremony for graduates. Agriculture more than 3,000 people. The event was held at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
According to the report, the total number of graduating students from the three agricultural higher education institutions was 3,279, 1,319 of whom were female, or more than 40 percent. These successful students successfully completed their majors in 2019, 2020, 2021 and 2022. 2,433 students from the Royal University of Agriculture, 531 students from Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture and 315 students from Kampong Cham National Institute of Agriculture.
It should be noted that from 1984 to 2022, the three agricultural higher education institutions trained 30,354 human resources, 7,815 females. In the last four years, on average, the three institutions have trained more than 800 human resources per year for agriculture.
With the above results, the three higher education institutions have been implementing a series of reform programs, especially the promotion of the implementation of the new 10-year strategy 2021-2030, which was implemented by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in 2021. To promote the development of the agricultural sector in accordance with the policies and strategies of the Royal Government.
For 2030, the three institutions aim to train at least 6,000 knowledgeable, professional and productive students and develop new technologies and products that the market needs. Less than 50.
