The following is a video of the President of Khmer Mohanakor Youth Network: Understanding Business: Accelerating ASEAN Payment Connections and Promoting Local Currency Transfer to Make It Easier to Pay for Goods and Trade
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian businessmen and economists have suggested that the use of each country's local currency in QR Code payments in the ASEAN region will make it easier to pay for goods and promote trade in Cambodia. The region will enhance ASEAN prestige.
During the 42nd ASEAN Summit in Labour Bajo, Indonesia, ASEAN Leaders Agreed on Accelerating Regional Payment Connections and Promoting Domestic Currency Transfer through Enhancing Digital Payment Connectivity at Across ASEAN, the potential QR Code will be similar to the existing QR Code between Indonesia and Thailand, as well as between Indonesia and Singapore.
Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told Fresh News on May 14, 2023 that promoting the payment of individual countries or payments via QR Code in the ASEAN region is the desire of the sector. Private to facilitate payment of goods, while in the past, payments were made in US dollars, and then there are additional payments in Chinese yuan, which makes the payment time and exchange rate loss.
At the same time, he said that this type of payment method will also help promote the Khmer Riel, which encourages the use of more riel.
Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the promotion of the local currency at a time when the world is facing economic crisis due to the Kovid 19 crisis and the war between Russia and Ukraine is important for ASEAN prestige. .
"Promoting and promoting the use of the national currency for ASEAN member countries is important because we have more currents, better economic coefficients and growth," he said.
He added that the creation of QR Code is an initiative and a new mechanism that is good for people in the ASEAN region to make financial flows without having to spend a lot of time when they need cash, just pay through the App on Mobile phone without having to go to the bank or use a MasterCard.
