The NEC clarified the statements made by Comfrel's Coordinating Survey and Advocacy Coordinator, which were misleading and did not reflect the spirit of the NEC's legal performance.
* Based on the notification of the NEC No. 027, dated April 5, 2023, on the preparation of procedures for the registration of political parties and the list of candidates. The 7th legislative election in 2023, at the first point, determined that "political parties must attach a copy of the certificate of registration of political parties at the Ministry of Interior, which has been certified by the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Administration."
* Based on the Notification No. 044 of the NEC dated 26 April 2018 on the preparation of procedures for the registration of political parties and the list of candidates for the National Assembly election. 6, 2018, the first point is determined that "political parties must attach a copy of the certificate of registration of political parties at the Ministry of Interior, which has been certified by the municipal, district and Khan authorities."
Again, a copy of the certificate of registration of a political party at the Ministry of Interior required by the NEC to refer to the Prakas on registration of a political party at the Ministry of Interior, which does not specify the legality. Yes, just copy it.
The NEC has implemented the same standard since the 2018 6th National Assembly election for all political parties wishing to contest free, fair, just and fair elections.
