The following is the decision of the Ministry of Health: The temperature in Singapore reached 37 degrees Celsius, the highest daily record in 1983.
SINGAPORE: Temperatures in Singapore rose to 37 degrees Celsius on Saturday, the highest in 40 years, according to the National Environment Agency (NEA). This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Saturday, May 13, 2023.
The NEA added that locations across Singapore had temperatures above 36 degrees Celsius on Saturday. Short breaks are expected on weekends, while hot and dry weather is expected to continue until Sunday.
Two weeks ago, the agency claimed that temperatures in the country were unlikely to reach 40 degrees Celsius. The announcement was in response to an SMS aimed at warning Singaporeans of possible heat waves between 40 and 50 degrees Celsius.
