Mr. Hun Many Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for a DBST Road Nearly 8 Kilometers in Skos Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province
(Kampong Speu): Of course, rural transport infrastructure and transportation are very important in promoting socio-economic interaction between rural and urban areas. This sector is an important economic artery in linking various business activities in the region to be more active and active, which is the basis for driving the income growth of the rural population.
On the morning of May 13, 2023, Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu District, inaugurated the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of 7,800 meters of DBST Road in Kraing Tralach Village, Skod Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Yim Sokhom, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Pong Speu Province, as well as the Chairman of the Local District-Commune Working Group.
Mr. HUN Many said that normally in the process of road construction, it can be dusty and hot and dry months like this, it is even more dusty, so please be understanding when your grandparents, parents, aunts and uncles travel through the area. Construction, it must be dusty, it has some difficulties to ask you to understand the engineering team to build this road.
In particular, please be very careful when the road is completed, please do not be too fast, beware of traffic accidents eventually, because traffic accidents now occur due to people and the death rate from Kovid 19 disease is no longer a traffic accident. About 7 people a day. Accidents, however, sometimes occur due to water changes the nature (alcohol) in the body when drunk, daring to drive faster than before, only to happen in such a traffic accident.
He said that the construction, upgrading of physical infrastructure, transportation and public services has been growing rapidly everywhere, which has helped promote economic growth, employment, equity and efficiency to people everywhere, especially in the region. Rural throughout the province.
In addition, the rural road network has facilitated transportation. We are now preparing for the official inauguration of the paved and concrete roads, which is a two-step rural road improvement project with the main purpose of improving people's travel time. Reduce the cost of transporting products as well as agricultural products to the market and have easy access to various public services.
Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, expressed his deep gratitude to the Royal Government through the Ministry of Rural Development for establishing this achievement, which was implemented by the Engineering Division No. 178, Bridge-Road, Engineering Department of the Ministry of National Defense on the 7,800-kilometer road. Meters and 9 meters wide, passing through 8 villages, including 6 villages in Speu commune and 2 villages in Sen Dey commune.
And call on the people, authorities at all levels, please support and pay attention to the use and maintenance of the achievements built now for the benefit of the public, because the road is a blood vessel for traffic. As the old saying goes, "There is a road, there is hope", more specifically, to connect from one commune village to another commune village and facilitate traffic to reach local people. .
