Mr. Un Chanda said that building party members at the grassroots level is an important task, that is, to pay more attention to doing good to their party members, including the general public. Because some people, even if they do not join the CPP, does not mean that they do not vote for the CPP, so local party officials must do good deeds for them.
He added that the local party must also be prepared to propagate the party's policies to the people in the towns and also to retaliate against those who attack the CPP.
