Ministry of Health and partner organizations share experiences with pediatricians in the treatment of pediatric and infant eye diseases in a timely manner to avoid blindness
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health and partner organizations on May 12, 2023 organized a workshop on "Awareness about the health of children and infants" to educate and provide information to pediatricians, nurses and health officials about disabilities. The severity of the eye disease of children and infants that can be avoided and sent to rescue and treatment in a timely manner.
Professor Xia Huang said that over the past two decades, the Royal Government of Cambodia has continued to make great efforts to improve the quality and expand the scope of eye health under the Ministry of Health's public health equity policy through the National Eye Health Program.
"These efforts have seen an improvement in the ability to manage and prevent blindness," he said. The use of eye care services is also increasing and eye health services are being integrated into the health care system at all levels.
On that occasion, Prof. Ngy Meng also stated that the National Eye Health Program organized this workshop to set the right conditions for those who provide primary eye care services, including nurses and community health care staff who Specific training on pediatric and infant eye health is required to improve referral and pediatric eye care services.
Prof. Ngy Meng "After completing this workshop, today we will take another new step by coming together to share experiences, learn more about eye diseases, children and infants will work together to send children and infants with eye diseases. "Seriously seek treatment by ophthalmologists, children and infants in time to avoid blindness."
