Samdech stated that the watch that Samdech is trying to find has many memories from when he was a pagoda boy until Samdech was the Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen posted a photo of himself wearing a watch, which he was looking for with the following content: "Only photos! I tried to find a watch that I wore before the war in 1970 and traded it with Chea Sim in 1982. Yesterday I received from social media three photos taken in 1979. In this photo there is a watch worn on my wrist, this is the watch I am looking for.
This watch has a long history since I was a pagoda boy. Around the end of 1969 or the beginning of 1970, because the monks blamed the slow cooking, I decided to cheat the piglets and save more than 5,000 riel to buy a Titon watch.
This watch has helped me a lot so that you do not have to blame him for taking slow meals, especially serving in the army until he was Minister of Foreign Affairs 1979-1980 and Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs 1981-1982, before exchanging this watch with Brother Chea Sim in 1982. " China urges G7 countries not to conspire to intimidate and coerce economically with US
BEIJING: China is a victim of US coercive policies and economic threats, urging the G7 to stop participating in the "small circle", a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman said on Friday. Monopolize and avoid becoming an accomplice to economic coercion, according to a release by the Xinhua News Agency on Friday, May 12, 2023.
Spokesman Wang Wenbin made the remarks at a daily news conference in response to recent media reports that G7 members would announce a joint response to "economic coercion" to send a signal. Hold China.
Speaking of economic coercion, Wang said the first country to be condemned was probably the United States. He said the United States has repeatedly expanded the concept of national security, violated export controls and applied discrimination and bias against foreign companies, which seriously violates the principles of market economy and fair competition.
Citing relevant statistics on US sanctions against other countries, Wang noted that as of fiscal year 2021, more than 9,400 US sanctions have been imposed. He added that the United States has unilaterally imposed economic sanctions on nearly 40 countries around the world, affecting nearly half of the world's population.
Prek Pnov District Governor Inspects a Concrete Road Donated by the Governor of Phnom Penh and Inspected the Rehabilitation of Boeung Krachab Canal
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of May 12, 2023, Mr. THEM Sam An, Governor of Prek Pnov District, led a professional officer to inspect the construction of concrete road in Tuol Ponsaing village, Prey Snuol village, Ta Skor village to Tnaot Kphos village of Ponsaing commune.
The district governor confirmed that this road is a dirt road that Mr. Khuong Sreng, the governor of Phnom Penh, donated $ 21,400.
He added that the district fund later rebuilt the concrete road with a length of 1,200 meters. Recently, at the request of the chief of Ponsaing commune, Mr. Khuong Sreng, he decided to help build another 1,100 meters, 1.5 meters thick, with steel bones and concrete properly.
On the occasion of inspecting the concrete road, which was donated by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Ms. Chea Sinath Khuong Sreng, was also accompanied by Deputy Governor and Sangkat Chief of Ponsaing, as well as the people.
After inspecting the concrete road, Mr. Them Sam An led the officers to continue to inspect the rehabilitation of Boeung Krachab canal to release the water from Boeung Krachab from flooding and to get water for people to grow crops. The district governor confirmed that the canal, after being rehabilitated and established as a waterway infrastructure, has benefited farmers, especially those who can open the canopy.
On that occasion, the people expressed their great pleasure for helping to build this concrete road, and they promised to repay Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh by voting for all CPP. Each.
While inspecting the concrete road construction, Mr. Them Sam An also saw sick people being treated at home with compassion as children and grandchildren. He also donated $ 100 to share the hardships. He.
