The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia announced on its official Facebook page that on May 11, 2023, the Chinese Customs Administration released a list of companies registered to export Cambodian spices to China. Cambodian pepper has completed all procedures for export to China, can be exported directly to the Chinese market.
Twenty-eight pepper plantations and seven packaging plants are registered and licensed by the Chinese side for export.
To expedite the implementation of the protocol on phytosanitary requirements for pepper exports from Cambodia to China, signed jointly between China and Cambodia in November 2022, the Customs Administration of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia and the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry. And Cambodian Fisheries On April 10-11, 2023, recently inspected the location of pepper plant and pepper packing factory through Video Conference.
Pepper is the first Cambodian agricultural product to be allowed to be exported to China in 2023 and also the first spice to be allowed to be exported to the Chinese market.
