Samdech Men Sam An Recommends 7 Points to Contribute to the Promotion of Buddhism in Cambodia
(Svay Rieng): Samdech Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, presided over the dissemination ceremony of the 30th National Congress of Monks at the Hall. Svay Rieng Provincial Hall General Meeting.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, Provincial Council, Senator, Mr. and Mrs. Candidates for the 7th Legislature, Svay Rieng Province, Secretary of State, Ministry of Cult and Religion, Teachers, chiefs of 246 pagodas and relevant officials, about 517 people, including 302 monks.
Samdech Kitti Sangkhabandit also brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, and expressed his sincere appreciation to Theranu Thera: To you, ladies and gentlemen, grandparents and local authorities at all levels, who are always involved in the development of Svay Rieng.
His Excellency Dr. Men Sam An stated that the dissemination of the contents of the 30th National Congress of Priests will really help orient and respond to the challenges, especially the direction of work set out to be implemented in the field of Buddhism. To serve the public interest, to continue to reform the field of Buddhist education at all levels, and to strengthen the dharma-discipline of Buddhism.
At the same time, Samdech Kittisangha Bandith also gave the following ideas to contribute to the strengthening of Buddhism:
* 1: Priests at all levels must strictly abide by the provisions of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, relevant laws and regulations in order to become an important driving force for the promotion of Buddhism to become stronger and better. Is the state religion.
* 2: Priests at all levels must better cooperate in accordance with the rules and hierarchies in order to strengthen the unity and solidarity in Buddhist institutions.
* 3: Monks at all levels should join the Buddhist monks' movement to cooperate with the Royal Government in preventing drugs and creating conditions for respect for traffic laws by integrating the Dharma of the Buddha in sermons and education. Schools and community education programs.
* 4: The Department of Cults and Religions and the provincial hall must continue to reform the field of Buddhist education at all levels, which is the strong backbone of Buddhism, in which the primary Buddhist schools must speed up the basic curriculum and reform some subjects. In particular, Buddhist higher education must pay attention to increasing the quantity and quality of student education.
* 5: Monks of all ranks, especially chiefs, sub-clergy, and chaplains, please pay attention to encourage monks and nuns under their supervision to study and study dharma-discipline in depth and apply that moral discipline strictly, as well as establish a program of practice. Meditation and Vipassana meditation to educate the mind is important and practice as a province for a shrine to Buddhists near and far.
* 6: The Department of Cults and Religions, monks at all levels, especially the chief, please continue to strengthen the structure of local monks in all pagodas and continue to establish monks to train priests to be able to manage, lead and perform their roles. That's right.
* 7: May the Chief Bishop of the pagoda continue to pay attention to the preparation of the pagoda to be worthy, a clean, sacred temple, a place of worship, a place of discipline, a place of moral education, and a place of religious tourism, including high hygiene. Protect nature, preserve ancient buildings to contribute to the promotion of culture, tourism and social environment in accordance with the rules and development of Buddhism.
