In the past three months, the two sides have been negotiating a comprehensive Thai-UAE comprehensive economic partnership agreement, and other talks are scheduled to run from May 16 to 18 in Dubai.
According to the Bangkok Post, the meeting in Dubai will be the first between senior government officials led by the director general of the Thai Trade Negotiation Department.
The head of the Thai Trade Negotiation Department has been appointed to lead the delegation in the negotiations, with the aim of concluding an agreement within six months or later this year.
He said the products that will benefit immediately include processed foods, processed seafood, textiles, clothing, blankets, rubber products, automobile products, air conditioners, electronics and leather products.
