The ceremony is solemn and costs a lot of money, it is usually organized together with many girls and boys, just a condition if the number of children shaved must be odd. The shaving ceremony lasts for 2 days and 1 night, with many important tasks.
Archaeologist and Head of the Research and Training Department of the APSARA Authority, Mr. M. Sokrithy, said that the shaving ceremony is a transgender ceremony, a ceremony that emphasizes the important stages of the life of each person that the ancient Khmer people do for Girls, boys or adolescents are not yet mature enough to enter adulthood.
Mr. M. Sokrithy continued that this shaving ceremony is a ceremony organized by the ancient Khmer people to show the process of human life that evolved from each stage of the human cycle. It is a sign of transcendence that the Khmer tradition defines its descendants to become adult family members in society in full accordance with traditional law.
The main purpose of the shaving ceremony is to separate the sexes of girls and boys, and then the boys will go out to study for knowledge, while the girls will go into economic knowledge, family management and so on. Minister of Health pays a courtesy call and discusses with the Head of Delegation of the Czech Republic to visit Cambodia
