Kep Governor: White Horse Port Achieved About 70% Completed Soon, While Another New Port is Applying for Investment
In the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit on the morning of May 11, 2023, on "5 years of success of the Kep Provincial Administration", Mr. Som Piseth claimed that he was looking forward to the White Horse Port under construction. Another new port is also asking for private sector investment.
The governor of Kep province said, "We have built about 60 to 70 percent of the white horse port and the rest will be completed 100 percent soon." "While the port is in the process of building another port, it is also asking for investment in state public land to build another cargo port."
According to Mr. Som Piseth, the size of the investment in the new port is worth more than 1 million dollars. On behalf of the provincial administration, he asserted that he would work hard to attract real investors in order to improve the flow of goods and waterways, avoiding the use of land, which could have serious consequences.
It should be informed that the construction site of White Horse Port is located in Sangkat O Krasar, Kep City, Kep Province on an area of 8 hectares. The project is under construction, operation and transfer (BOT) for 15 years, invested by the private sector. This port will facilitate the transportation of goods and agricultural products between Kep and Kampot, especially transporting raw materials to serve factories in Kampot.
According to a letter from the Ministry of Economy and Finance dated February 15, 2021, the project will require an investment of nearly 2 million dollars and will be allowed to recoup the capital through the business of the ferry terminal (White Horse Port) during At the end of 15 years, it will continue for another 15 years from the time the railway station is completed and officially inaugurated in 2023.
Regarding the actual construction project, the representative of Mr. Ing Kov Hay, the owner of the investment company, told Fresh News that the construction of the White Horse Port project is scheduled to be completed in 2023, but the whole project has been delayed due to some obstacles such as The Kovid 19 crisis, the global economic crisis and natural disasters due to rain affected the construction process.
A representative of the White Horse Port Investment Company said that due to some impacts, the construction to be completed will be postponed until 2024, while most of the construction is now completed. The construction of the White Horse Port has been completed, including the clearing of the construction site, the filling of the port yard, the construction of the concrete port, the retaining wall, the waterway, and the office building.
However, despite some repercussions, representatives of the White Horse Port Investment Company still show a strong commitment to make efforts to complete the remaining work as soon as possible.
