Trade volume between Cambodia and international market reached more than 15 billion USD in the first 4 months of this year, Cambodia exported more than 7 billion USD
(Phnom Penh): In the first four months of 2023, the trade volume between Cambodia and international reached more than 15 billion dollars, down more than 14 percent compared to the same period in 2022, which was more than 17 billion dollars. This is according to data from the General Department of Customs and Excise.
According to the same data, from January to April 2023, Cambodia exported key goods to international markets worth more than 7.2 billion US dollars, down 4.9%, while Cambodia re-imported goods in the amount of $ 7.9 billion, down 21.1%.
Cambodia's main exports include garments worth $ 2.1 billion, machinery and electrical equipment worth $ 979 million, natural pearls or gemstones worth more than $ 300 million, and shoes worth more than $ 300 million. More than $ 436 million, along with other key commodities.
China is the number one country with the largest trade volume with Cambodia, with more than $ 3.8 billion, while the United States is the second largest country with about 2 billion dollars. $ 5,000. Vietnam is in third place, followed by Thailand, Japan, Singapore, Indonesia and other countries.
