Of the 2,825,970 migrants deported, most were on the US-Mexico border, six were in Mexico, the Interior Ministry said in a statement. Of the 10, 1,611,746 were Mexican citizens. A large portion of the other migrants expelled from the southern US border are from countries such as Guatemala, Honduras, El Salvador and Nicaragua.
In March 2020, Title 42 was issued by the administration of former US President Donald Trump, allowing the United States to quickly expel migrants from its borders during the 199 outbreak of Kovid. Recently, migrants have begun to gather in Mexico along parts of the border with the United States, while Title 42 will be canceled.
Another Agricultural Community Market in Kampong Thom Province Officially Launched to Create Market for Farmers and Increase Agricultural Production
(Kampong Thom): Chreang Svay Phleung Development Agricultural Community Market was officially inaugurated to create more markets for farmers and increase agricultural production, which contributes to improving farmers' livelihoods in Kampong Thom province.
Speaking at the inauguration ceremony on May 10, Ms. Cham Chan, Chairman of Chreang Svay Phleung Development Community Agriculture Committee, said that the establishment of Chreang Svay Phleung Agricultural Community Market was a place to gather agricultural products in the agricultural community and is a necessity. Necessary of farmers, production team.
She said that the agricultural community market, which is 15 meters long and 8 meters wide, was established with financial support from Heifer Cambodia under the project of Khmer Chicken Processing Enterprise for the National Pride of Cambodia (PPNP), UNDP and from Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs of the Republic of Korea (MAFRA) under the project to promote the use of solar energy technology for agriculture and rural development in Cambodia.
According to the chairman of the community board, as of 2022, Chreang Svay Phleung Agricultural Community has 214 members (160 women) and has the main occupations such as selling fertilizers, selling animal feed, selling chickens, meat, selling eggs, chickens, vegetables, credit. Production and credit business, buy rice, make rice and sell grilled chicken.
She said the agricultural community market will be a gathering place for agricultural products, connecting sellers and buyers in the community and outside the community, as a place to store, pack and store products to help increase the community's income and economy. Communities encourage community production groups and reduce migration.
Mr. Siv Chhoeun, Representative of the Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Thom Province, encouraged the community to organize and increase production groups to meet the needs of the market and buyers. At the same time, the community should increase communication with the market and external buyers in order for the agricultural community market to function well.
Chhum Sovanny, UNDP Representative, says UNDP projects focus on strengthening agriculture adapted to climate change, markets and solar pumps.
It should also be noted that through the project "Promoting the use of solar technology for agriculture and rural development in Cambodia", which is a joint venture between Heifer Cambodia and UNDP and supported by the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. The Republic of Korea (MAFRA) three more agricultural community markets will be officially inaugurated in Kampong Thom and Siem Reap in May 2023.
