After a joint venture between the Sam Rainsy Party and the Human Rights Party, which formed the CNRP, he ran for parliament in Takeo, and although the CNRP was dissolved, he took a break from politics for a while. Tien started working, he also joined the Candlelight Party, taking the position of Executive Vice President of the party in Takeo province.
On that occasion, Mr. Kang Leach also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party for allowing him to work with the CPP, and he also called on all members of the Candlelight Party in Takeo. Turn to support the Cambodian People's Party and vote for the Cambodian People's Party to maintain peace and national development to move forward.
Separately, Mr. Chhil Sat, Vice President of the Cambodian Independent Teachers Association and Executive Secretary of the Rain Party, Tram Kak District, Takeo Province, also said that the decision to join the CPP at this time is forced or dragged. It's from the CPP officials, that is, the decision to join on their own because of seeing injustice in the partisan and discriminating party members at the grassroots level.
