NEC: As of 11 May, the NEC has officially recognized the registration of 13 parties, while 7 more specialized units are reviewing various procedures
(Phnom Penh): As of Thursday, May 11, 2023, the National Election Committee (NEC) has officially recognized the registration of political parties and the list of 13 parties. While the other seven parties, the specialized units are reviewing and implementing various procedures.
According to a press release issued on May 11, the NEC convened a meeting chaired by NEC Chairman Prach Chan to review and decide on the registration of political parties and candidates. List of candidates from two parties.
The NEC meeting officially recognized the registration applications of two more parties: First, the Khmer National Unity Party, which has 7 capital-provincial constituencies, and second, the Local Democratic Party, which has 12 capital-constituencies. Provinces and lists of candidates of these two parties in the 7th National Assembly Election 2023.
There are still 7 political parties that the specialized unit is reviewing and following the procedures of registration of political parties and the list of candidates to submit to the NEC for review and decision, including: 1. Women's Party for Women 2. Khmer Stop Poverty Party 3. Candlelight Party 4. Khmer Economic Development Party 5. Indigenous Peoples Democratic Party of Cambodia 6. Khmer National Unity Party 7. Farmers Party
At the above meeting, the NEC revised and agreed in principle on the guidelines on the election campaign march and the distribution of leaflets in the markets of political parties for the 7th National Assembly election. 2023.
The meeting also revised and agreed in principle on the decision on the transfer of the names of voters, candidates, spouses and children in the 2022 official voter list to serve the 7th National Assembly election in 2023.
