Senior Health Officials Call on Relevant Officials and Local Authorities to Promote Community Participation for Health
Her remarks were made at a consultation workshop on a draft policy on community participation for health organized by the National Center for Health Promotion, supported by the Global Fund, on 10 May 2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel. With the participation of the Deputy Governors of the 25 capitals and provinces, representatives of partner organizations, the directors of the health departments of the 25 capitals and provinces, and representatives of other relevant ministries and institutions.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health emphasized that the development of the policy on the participation of the new community is in line with the fourth phase of the Health Strategic Plan 2022-2030, which focuses on "achieving the strengthening of the provision system. Global health care and health coverage to keep Cambodians safe and healthy. ”
She added that decentralization and deconcentration (D&D) reforms had led to significant changes in the structure and governance of Cambodia's health system, requiring an update on the policy of community participation in health center development. Exist 2003 to reflect the context of new developments and policies.
The Ministry of Health still considers community participation as a key priority in the Fourth Health Strategic Plan to ensure good governance. The Health Center Management Committee (HCMC) is an important mechanism for connecting health centers with authorities and communities, strengthening local authorities' ownership of health care management in their own areas.
"In the past, the Ministry of Health has taken care to strengthen the operation of the Health Center Management Committee by setting an important condition for evaluating the quality of health services. The functioning of the Health Center Management Committee is one of the key health indicators that we have strived to achieve with the participation of partners and civil society, ”she added.
The next step is for the Ministry of Health to develop a Community Implementation Policy Implementation Policy of the Year, which will provide a more detailed guide to the VHSG selection process, training, management, implementation, and funding.
At the same time, please pay attention to promote the operation of the Village Health Support Group (VHSG), which today plays an active role in helping to educate, promote, encourage people to receive services and facilitate various health activities in the community. (VHSG) is an indispensable component in community health development.
In addition, health work requires the participation of all institutions, cooperation and coordination between relevant institutions at the national and sub-national levels is essential to support community participation, especially in the context of decentralization, allocating additional resources and responsibilities to institutions. Sub-national governments that can provide funding opportunities to support community participation.
