Asian rice yields rise as prices rise farmers expand video (inside) (Singapore): Asian rice yields will increase this year as higher prices push farmers to expand their land and use more fertilizer. Much eased concerns about supply after production suffered its first decline in seven years in 2022. According to Reuters.
The recent harvest of rice in India and Thailand, the world's two largest exporters, has exceeded last year's level and farmers are preparing for the main growing season. Plant in the next few months.
Winter rice production in India jumped to 22.8 million tonnes, up from 18.5 million tonnes last year, as moderate rains from September to October allowed farmers to expand their cultivation. The recovery in yields has offset the decline in summer crops.
