Regional Workshop on Mine Action Data Management System to share experiences related to using IMSMA Core for mine action data management
More than 40 participants from the National Mine Action Authority of ASEAN countries affected by landmines and explosive remnants of war, as well as local and global operators / organizations on mine action, international organizations and other stakeholders. Come to this regional workshop.
A number of countries in Southeast Asia that have gone through previous wars have left landmines and explosive remnants of war (ERW) and negatively impacted the restoration of sustainable development and physical infrastructure. Such as regional peacebuilding and development.
Participants will gain knowledge on setting up IMSMA implementation processes and exchanging knowledge on implementation and data management challenges. The regional workshop also provides comprehensive insights, opportunities for sharing experiences between national authorities for mine action in the ASEAN region, as well as relevant operators. This regional workshop is funded by the Federal Government of Germany.
The implementation of the ASEAN Regional Center for Mine Action and this regional workshop contributes to strengthening cooperation between ASEAN Member States in promoting peace and security in the region, contributing to humanitarian work in dealing with landmines and national waste. Explode from the war and contribute to support the ASEAN Community in building peace and stability in the region, as stated in the ASEAN Community Security Policy-2025.
The ASEAN Regional Center for Mine Action (ARMAC) was established in accordance with a statement by the ASEAN Leaders under the initiative of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, on the establishment of the ASEAN Regional Center for Mine Action. Mine action, which was approved on November 18, 2012 and launched in 2016.
