Mr. Neth Pheaktra: We must not only remove traps in the forest, but we must eliminate all sources of traps
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Trap Zero Campaign, emphasized that "we must not only remove traps in the forest, but we must eliminate and eliminate traps sold in some locations." In a sense, the Zero Trap campaign not only provides security for wildlife, but also for people and social order.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this remark on the occasion of presiding over the opening of the second Zero Trap Campaign in Kampong Speu with the participation of Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu, partner organizations and About 500 people were involved in the morning of May 9, 2023 yesterday.
On that occasion, Mr. Neth Pheaktra asked the authorities and stakeholders to inspect some locations that continue to bring brake belts, motorcycles and some equipment that can be designed as traps to sell at locations near natural resource protection areas, which may be eliminated. The source of the trap.
In addition, Mr. Neth Pheaktra also reminded that through the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, that is, the confiscation of firearms on a voluntary basis and the principle of coercion if they do not cooperate. While recycled guns are not only dangerous for wildlife shooting, some perpetrators have also used recycled guns to shoot with the authorities.
In the two years from 2021 to 2022, 100,000 traps were removed from the forest, 1,500 recycled firearms and other illegal equipment were confiscated, the spokesman said. . Recently, in Mondulkiri province, the police cracked down on illegal hunting, confiscating six firearms, three automatic rifles and nearly 400 rounds of ammunition.
Mr. Vy Samnang also encouraged the officers to remove trapping materials from some shops near the natural resource protection area, as this location should not be for sale of brake cables, motorcycles or other cables, as well as Chainsaws that are part of creating natural resource crime and destroying wildlife.
The Governor of Kampong Speu Province urged all stakeholders to join together to eliminate traps, do not enter the forest, hunt wildlife to maintain the presence of wildlife to survive in the natural forest of Cambodia. Volunteer Doctors of Kampong Cham Province Young Scholars Association Provides Free Medical Treatment to About 500 Monks and Citizens in Veal Vong Sangkat
