The Prime Minister of East Timor accepted the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen regarding food security for the development of agriculture itself and food security. General knowledge: Which languages are spoken the most?
Russian is a language spoken by a total of 258 million people, of which 154 million are native languages. Russian is the official language of Russia, Kazakhstan, Belarus and Kyrgyzstan. Russian is also widely used in many countries of the former Yugoslavia.
Bengali is the most widely spoken language in India and Bangladesh. Bengali has a total language of about 272 million, of which 233 million are native languages. In India, this language is the most widely used language after Hindi.
Arabic is the official language of more than 20 countries in the world, mostly in the Middle East and North Africa. Arabic is also a multilingual language, with the most widely spoken language being Standard Arabic, which has an estimated 274 million speakers.
French is the official language of nearly 30 countries. The most French-speaking countries are France, Belgium, Canada and Switzerland. The language is also widely used in parts of Central and West Africa, the Caribbean and South America. There are about 280 million French speakers worldwide, but it is the native language of 80 million people.
Spanish is the fourth largest language in the world, and if we consider the number of speakers, it is the native language, which is the second largest language after Mandarin. In total, 548 million people worldwide speak Spanish, of which 474 million are native languages.
For example, countries in Africa with many different ethnic groups have decided to choose English as their standard language. The dominance of the English language around the world is due to the history of British colonization, combined with the influence of the US culture and economy of the English-speaking world.
In the United States, Spanish is the most widely spoken language after English. The United States has 40 million native speakers of Spanish, making it the second most Spanish-speaking country after Mexico and possibly Wama.
Cambodia, UK and other international countries discuss green education and training to help reduce global climate change
On May 9, 2023, the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, led a Cambodian delegation to a meeting on education and skills training in the face of global climate change to help reduce climate change. Climate through the implementation of green education programs.
Discussions on this important topic took place during the 19th World Education Forum at the Elizabeth II Center in London, UK. Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Representative of the Cambodian side, was invited by Ms. Baroness Barran, Minister of Education and Student Foundation of the United Kingdom.
Discussions on education and skills training in the face of global climate change are considered a major topic at the 19th World Education Forum and are a major global issue today.
On that occasion, Mr. Ith Sam Heng discussed with Ms. Baroness Barran, as well as the Minister of Education and Skills Training, who are all important individuals in leading the above discussion, as well as some other relevant experts, focusing on the basic role of Educate and train skills to achieve global climate change mitigation goals.
During the discussion, the UK Minister for Education and Skills shared experiences, policies / strategic plans, challenges and solutions related to education and skills training in the context of global climate change to achieve green education for All together.
Minister Baroness Barran and Minister of Education and Skills Education are committed to seeking cooperation in supporting education and skills training programs in response to global climate change and green education.
