Senior Minister Kun Kim Meets Cambodian Veterans in Kampong Cham Province
(Kampong Cham): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, together with Kampong Cham provincial leaders, met this morning, May 9, 2023, and presented medals to Cambodian veterans in Kampong Cham province. Kampong Cham Provincial Conference Hall.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim also thanked all the veterans who have actively contributed to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and achieved peace to this day. "As veterans, fighters, fighters, so we must set a good example and protect this legacy of peace for a long time to come," he added. NEC Disseminates Election Registration of Political Parties and Election Observers
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) on May 9, 2023 held a meeting with election stakeholders under the chairmanship of Mr. Mean Sati, Member of the NEC and Chairman. Meeting on the Registration of Political Parties and the List of Candidates for National and International Observers and the Code of Conduct for Observers in the 7th National Assembly Election on 23 July 2023.
Mr. Mean Sati said that until the last day of May 8, 2023, the registration of political parties to stand for election and the list of candidates of 20 political parties have applied to register with the NEC. Eleven political parties have been officially recognized by the NEC and nine others are being monitored and awaited by the NEC.
Regarding the observers, Mr. Mean Sati informed that as of May 8, 2023, the NEC has recognized a total of 10,130 national and international observers, of which 5,056 are women. The NEC has not yet received applications from international observers from any institution or country. He added that election observers include:
He added that international observers can travel anywhere in the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia without the need for permission or prior notice, except for obvious reasons related to personal security. In case of any emergency or insecurity, the observer must inform the relevant election officials and local authorities to help resolve in time.
There were questions from the participants in the meeting regarding the procedure for reviewing the registration of political parties and candidates, the withdrawal of candidates and the participation of international observers.
The NEC representative replied at the meeting that the NEC shall review the application for registration of political parties to stand for election within 7 (seven) days after receiving the application. In case the NEC agrees to register a political party to stand for election, the NEC shall issue a certificate of registration of a political party to stand for election to the political party concerned.
In the case of a candidate of a political party, the NEC requested the Ministry of Justice to confirm the re-fitness of the candidate, and the Ministry of Justice replied to the NEC that Rong Chhun was not yet qualified. Again, no. Therefore, Rong Chhun has no right to stand as a candidate for the National Assembly election.
Regarding the withdrawal from the candidates, the NEC representative stated that this case is the right of individuals and the affairs of political parties. Political parties must check and prepare the list properly before applying for registration of political parties and the list of candidates at the NEC.
Involving international observers in monitoring the election of NEC representatives is considered an important task to reflect the accuracy of the election process to some extent. However, the law does not stipulate that without the participation of election observers, the election will not be considered valid. Election observation is voluntary, however, the NEC has called on national and international observers to observe the election.
Pursat Governor Meets Cambodian Workers in Trat, Thailand
(Pursat): During a two-day study visit to Trat, from May 08-09, 2023, Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, took the opportunity to visit and check the working conditions of the children. Cambodian workers working at The Chhiv Restaurant and Resort in Koh Chang, Trat Province, Thailand.
The meeting with Cambodian workers on that occasion was also attended by Mr. Chham Nan Vitterat, Governor of Trat Province.
Mr. Khoy Rida brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, stating that both Samdech always pay attention to the well-being of workers inside. And abroad.
In fact, today, at the invitation of the Trat Provincial Administration, with the approval and support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior of Cambodia, allowed the Pursat Provincial Delegation to come. Participated in a two-day study visit to Trat, Thailand, and took the opportunity to meet with the nephews of Cambodian workers who are currently working.
He thanked the owners of the restaurants and resorts for providing employment opportunities to the children of Cambodian workers, as well as providing them with adequate food and taking good care of the health of Cambodian workers.
He praised the children of Cambodian workers who have the spirit to work hard to earn a living to increase national income. Every year, migrant workers send billions of dollars to their families, and when they return to Cambodia, they bring with them the skills and knowledge they have learned abroad and help to educate our brothers and sisters there. That basis, too.
He emphasized that the children of workers have the opportunity to work abroad now because of the correct policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has good foreign relations, cooperation and can send workers to each other. Legalized by each country.
He also advised the children of Cambodian workers to continue to take care of their own health and respect the laws of the country where they are working, as well as to participate in the election of the 7th legislature on July 23, 2023. Together as full-fledged Cambodian citizens.
