(Kampong Speu): By promoting awareness of the value of wildlife and the legal challenges of taking wildlife meat for sale to customers, seven restaurant owners in Kampong Speu have committed Absolutely do not sell food made from wild meat to customers, even if customers order and give expensive prices.
With the launch of the Zero Trap Campaign in Kampong Speu, in addition to the owners of the above seven restaurants, students and residents have promised to bring their awareness of the benefits of natural resources and wildlife to their families, relatives and friends. Also.
To date, there are more than 70 restaurants in eight provinces: Kratie, Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Pursat and Kampong Speu. And slaughter of wildlife in protected areas and wildlife conservation.
On the morning of May 9, 2023, on the occasion of the opening of the second phase of the Zero Trap Campaign in Kampong Speu Province, Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign, presented a certificate of appreciation to Restaurant owners also put up stickers advertising the importance of wildlife in restaurants.
"We should start with ourselves, not eating wild meat, not selling wild meat, because wildlife is very valuable for everyone," he said. Ask the owner of the restaurant who used to sell wild meat to cook for customers, please stop together to keep the presence of wild animals for generations to come.
"We believe that eating wild animals leads to two major problems: the destruction of natural resources and the spread of disease to humans." This is Mr. Borey's additional perception.
