Detained 6 Foreign and Cambodian Suspects in Drug Trafficking Case in Kandal Province
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Drug Department launched a crackdown on drug trafficking at a karaoke bar in Prek Soeng village, Sampov Poun commune, Koh Thom district, Kandal province, detaining suspects from Cambodia, Malaysia, Indonesia and Vietnam. A total of 6 people confiscated some drugs.
According to the report of the Third Commission of the Anti-Drug Campaign for the first four months of 2023, the police cracked down on 2,345 drug crimes, arrested 5,572 people and confiscated more than 361 kilograms of drugs.
Dr. HUN Manet Meets CPP, Khan and Sangkat Committees in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Dr. HUN Manet, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), Chairman of the Central Youth Committee of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) With the CPP Committee of the 14 Khans and the CPP Committee of the 105 Sangkats in Phnom Penh at the CPP headquarters in Phnom Penh.
Speaking on that occasion, Dr. highly appreciated and thanked all the leaders, members of the Party Committees of Khans and Sangkats in Phnom Penh for their active participation in serving the local people on a regular basis, especially in the past. When Phnom Penh was hit by the Kovid-19 epidemic, this was a clear link between the people who own the country and the officials who serve the people.
At the same time, Dr. also expressed his appreciation to the leaders and members of the Capital Party Committee and subordinate organizations at all levels who have actively contributed to the organization of the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games. In the geography of Phnom Penh, until this historic event, the opening program was successfully run and is proceeding smoothly as planned.
(Indonesia): Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, on May 9, 2023, attended the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Labour, Bajo, Republic of Indonesia.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting is one of a series of meetings leading up to the 42nd ASEAN Summit, discussing progress in the process of building the ASEAN Community as well as recent developments in ASEAN.
He said that at the summit, ASEAN will review the achievements of ASEAN in the past and its relations with foreign countries as the regional and global situation changes, geopolitical conflicts and conflicts. South China Sea, Myanmar, especially the Russia-Ukraine war, affecting the global economy.
After the plenary session, Samdech will lead a delegation to attend meetings such as meetings with the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (IPA) with ASEAN youth and meetings with other institutions.
ASEAN leaders will also discuss regional and international issues of common concern and interest, including the implementation of the five-point consensus on Myanmar and the decisions of ASEAN leaders and the implementation of the ASEAN Perspectives on the Indo-Pacific. Well.
The project receives $ 1.79 million in funding from the Global Agriculture and Food Security Program and $ 1.1 million from the CACC, aimed at improving the resilience and livelihoods of smallholder farmers through organic farming and market access.
The project also aims to promote nutrition and gender equality through social behavioral change approaches designed to stimulate the need for a healthy diet and cope with harmful social habits.
Ms. Clare Conan, WFP Country Representative in Cambodia, said: “This project is designed in the context of Kovid-19, using innovative approaches that build partnerships between the public, private and producers sectors with a focus on "The need to take advantage of private sector investment strengthens policy dialogue, ensures the necessary knowledge and supports environmentally friendly development, social and economic equity."
CACC Executive Director Kan Kunthy said the CACC will establish an organic food value chain that is environmentally friendly and encourages smallholder farmers, including women and indigenous peoples, to switch to organic farming using only fertilizers and pesticides. Natural particles and other practices that respond to climate change.
"Organic food is cheaper and more stable than traditional produce," he said. "There are high profit opportunities and stable income." He noted that small farmers in Mondulkiri mostly grow only rice, and most practice traditional shifting cultivation, which is vulnerable to weather and other crises.
Mr. Kunthy added, "Our goal is to increase the income of participating farmers by up to 20 percent compared to the profits of conventional agriculture." He also said that the CACC will facilitate market relations and farmers will be able to use their income to cope with future crises.
"Income growth will play an important role in facilitating better nutrition when their families have access to a healthy diet that can withstand the negative nutritional impact on their families," said Conan. .
She also noted that livelihoods and nutrition are very important as the target area has high levels of poverty and malnutrition.
Minister Ith Sam Heng attends the World Education Forum in the United Kingdom and takes the opportunity to build relationships with participants from around the world
(English): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, led a delegation to the 19th World Education Forum on "Cultural Cultivation, Education, Resource Building and Sustainability Promotion for Better Education". Creative, strong and courageous.
The 19th World Forum will take place from 7-10 May 2023 at the Elizabeth II Center in London, United Kingdom.
The forum aims to share experiences related to education to gain input for policy development related to resilient education, including the basics of basic education, skills development and the development of new technologies. Participation from government representatives, the private sector, education and training professionals and development partners from 118 countries around the world.
The World Education Forum is the largest gathering of education and technical education ministers in the world to discuss future education policies, share experiences and best practices, as well as to assess and find solutions to common sector challenges. Technical education and training.
In the program of this educational forum, there will also be speeches by keynote speakers, as well as discussions and exchange of views at the ministerial level. In addition, informal discussions and opportunities to build communication (Networking) between all participants.
Tycoon Lim Heng said this while leading a delegation of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to establish representative offices of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia on May 6 and 7, 2023 and met Discuss some trade issues with the President of the Government of Southeast Asia, the Government of Victoria and Australian businessmen.
Tycoon Lim Heng said that the establishment of Cambodian Chamber of Commerce representative offices in two cities in Australia will begin to expand bilateral relations between traders and traders or between the private sector and the private sector (B2B), which will speed up communication. It will be easier while Cambodia and Australia are implementing the RCEP.
He hopes that after the establishment of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in Australia will improve the relationship between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Australian Chamber of Commerce.
On the way to establish a representative office of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in Australia, the Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce also visited a number of industrial farms in Australia and held a number of business meetings in anticipation of better exports and imports between Cambodia and Australia. Up.
According to Tycoon Lim Heng, Australia is interested in importing materials and food to Cambodia, while Australia is in need of a wide range of products such as textiles, electronics, components, especially nine agricultural products such as avocados, peppers, sesame, sweet potato, mango, cashew. Palm sugar and dried banana slices studied by the Cambodia-Australia Agricultural Values Program (CAVAC), an opportunity for Cambodian traders to export to Australia.
During his visit to Australia, Duke Lim Heng also met with Laura Berk, Head of the Southeast Asian Government of Victoria at the Victoria Investment Office in Melbourne, Australia to learn about the economic situation, potential sectors of Melbourne and to explore the possibility of cooperation between the two countries. Cambodian and Australian businessmen.
She said the Victoria Investment Office would work closely with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and seek private sector to discuss expanding trade between the two countries through the RCEP agreement.
According to data from the General Department of Customs and Excise in the first three months of 2023, the trade volume between Cambodia and Australia reached more than 135 million US dollars, an increase of 7.5%, of which Cambodia exported to Australia worth 98 million US dollars. An increase of 6.7%. Australia imported 37 million US dollars to Cambodia, an increase of 9.4%.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs said that Samdech Techo and his delegation are currently in Indonesia at the invitation of Indonesian President Joko Widodo and the 2023 rotating chair of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN). This year's ASEAN Summit is held under the theme "ASEAN Importance: Core of Growth", which will be held from 10 to 11 May 2023 in Labun Bajo, Republic of Indonesia.
Accompanying Samdech Techo Prime Minister include Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, as well as senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia and some businessmen of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
During his stay in Labour Bajo, the Prime Minister will also hold bilateral meetings with his ASEAN counterparts and some ASEAN dignitaries.
