Dr. HUN Manet: Investing in education is a contribution to the cultivation of knowledge, ability, virtue and morality
(Preah Sihanouk): Dr. Hun Manet, Chairman of the Scholarship Committee for Poor Students, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, said that investing in education is a contribution to cultivating knowledge, ability and virtue. And morality is an innate quality of human beings, which is the most important asset for each nation.
Dr. Hun Many's remarks were made on the occasion of presiding over the graduation ceremony for the winners of the University of Management and Economics (UME) Sihanoukville this morning, May 7, 2023 at the Independent Hotel. Sihanoukville.
He commended UME University for its investment in education over the past 25 years, with its continuous development in six provinces across the country. Lack with the Royal Government to jointly achieve the direction of the development of education, which is the foundation of socio-economic development, as well as progress in all areas in Cambodia.
As a personal interest, this historic event, Dr. HUN Manet highlighted two important aspects: First: the leadership and organization of all activities related to hospitality and competition in a smooth, accurate, fair and consistent manner. According to the standards set by the Council of the Federation of Southeast Asian Games and secondly, Cambodia's human resource capacity in sports has been significantly improved.
In fact, in the 32nd Southeast Asian Games, the number of medals that Cambodia has won is so large that it can break its own record in history and will continue to grow. This progress is not accidental, but fruitful under the favorable environment of peace-stability and the right and comprehensive policies of the CPP-led government.
Similarly, foreign investors also have the same expectations for investment decisions in Cambodia, first: to look at the factors of peace - stability and second: the level of human resources of Cambodia to have the skills to serve. To run production in their investment projects.
