NEC: Within 15 days, 11 political parties will be officially recognized while 9 parties are under scrutiny for voting
(Phnom Penh): Preliminary results of the registration of political parties and the list of candidates for the 7th National Assembly election for 15 days from April 24 to May 8, 2023, there are political parties Twenty have applied for registration, of which 11 have been officially recognized by the NEC and nine are under review.
According to the NEC, the 11 political parties have officially decided to recognize, including:
First: Cambodian People's Party Second: Cambodian Youth Party Third: Khmer United National Party Four: Theosophical Party Fifth: Democratic Forces Party Six: Cambodian Nationality Party Seventh: One Khmer Party Eight: Khmer Conservative Party 9th: FUNCINPEC Party 10th: Beehive Social Democratic Party 11th: People's Aspiration Party
The other nine political parties are reviewing, including:
First: Khmer National Unity Party Second: Women Party for Women Third: Khmer Anti-Poverty Party Fourth: Candlelight Party Fifth: Khmer Economic Development Party Sixth: Indigenous Peoples Democratic Party of Cambodia Seventh: Local Democrat Party 8: Khmer National Unity Party 9: Farmers Party
Please be informed that the submission and receipt of the application for registration of political parties and the list of candidates for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 ends on May 8, 2023 at 5:30 PM. The process went smoothly in accordance with the calendar, regulations and procedures for the election and was attended by representatives of political parties and election observers.
