(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, affirmed that the Armed Forces standing along the border line would like to send support and encouragement to all Cambodian national team players who are struggling hard to win. Nation in the 32nd SEA Games via Remote Heart Language.
The Heart Message of the Border Guard Armed Forces was sent on May 08, 2023, on the occasion of Mr. HUN Many leading the delegation to bring some raincoats, necessary materials, which are precious gifts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen distribute to the 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 3rd Armed Forces of the 4th Army Division in Preah Vihear Province, Oddar Meanchey Province.
Mr. Hun Many stated on Facebook: "While the Kingdom of Cambodia is hosting the 32nd SEA Games as the host, we must not forget the troops who are standing guard along our border. Also. Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always consider the well-being of the Armed Forces, especially as the rainy season approaches, despite the rush.
"Despite the obligations of the Armed Forces, we would like to send our support and encouragement to the national team players who are struggling hard to win the country through the language of the heart."
Please be informed that on that occasion, Mr. HUN Many brought greetings and memories from both Samdech and expressed his gratitude and appreciation to all the Armed Forces who sacrificed their physical and mental strength to perform their duties effectively. Courage in all circumstances, especially in a peaceful country, all forces always come down to save the people.
New Zealand defense spending to reach $ 472 million (Video inside): New Zealand defense forces will receive an additional $ 472.14 million over four years as the government Try to stop the loss of military personnel and ensure its ability to conduct military operations with allies and partners. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Monday, May 8, 2023.
In the last two years, the full-time military has lost 29.8 percent of its staff, excluding those serving less than two years. That number is expected to rise to 32.6 percent by June 30 if left unaddressed. The challenge comes as competition in the Pacific escalates, climate change and New Zealand are providing assistance to Ukraine.
As of today, the NEC has officially recognized the registration of political parties and the list of candidates for 11 parties.
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) on May 08, 2023, held a meeting chaired by Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC to review and decide on the application for registration. Of political parties standing for election and the list of candidates for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023.
In other agendas, the NEC decided to issue a letter of notification to one (1) political party to make adjustments to the copy of the political party registration certificate at the Ministry of Interior in accordance with Article 27 of the Law on Election. MPs.
In another case, the NEC decided to send a letter to the Ministry of Justice requesting confirmation of the existence or non-eligibility of a political party candidate.
According to the report of the specialized unit, as of 10:00 am on May 8, 2023, 18 political parties have applied for the registration of political parties and the list of candidates at the NEC.
As of today, the NEC has officially recognized the registration of 11 political parties and the list of 11 candidates.
(Pursat): On May 08, 2023, Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Provincial Board of Governors, led a delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss with Mr. Chham Nan Vitterat, Governor of Trat Provincial Board of Governors. Remember the Trat Provincial Hall, Thailand.
The courtesy call and discussion was held during the two-day study tour of the Pursat provincial delegation at the invitation of the Trat Provincial Administration with the permission and support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. And Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior of Cambodia.
The study tour of the delegation of Pursat province is from 08-09 May 2023 at some important locations in Trat province, including:
The purpose of this study tour is to find out about the work of education, correction and development of prisoners who are about to end their detention in the industries of handicrafts, trade, agriculture, work and tourism in Trat province, to gain experience based on development in Pursat province. Lead sustainable and efficient management.
Please be informed that Pursat Province has a rocky border crossing with Trat Province, Thailand, which is one of the ports in the project to establish an international port between the two countries. Today, the leaders of the two countries have been working to promote and strengthen cooperation so that the two ports can be upgraded to international ports in the near future for the benefit of the people of the two countries.
