(Siem Reap): The Royal Government team in Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province, is committed to completing the installation of solar lights, construction and repair of houses for people damaged by rain, wind and thunder last month. Some commune villages in Banteay Srei district in Siem Reap province.
Mr. Sem Sovanny, Head of the Local Government Working Group on Banteay Srei District, expressed his commitment to complete the installation of solar lights and housing for the above people during the inspection team. Expert groups in various communes in Banteay Srei district this past weekend.
On the occasion of leading the team to inspect the main roads in Preah Dak commune, Run Ta Ek commune, Romchek commune, Tbeng commune, Khun Ream commune and Khnar Sanday commune of Banteay Srei district to install solar lights on the geographical roads of the commune. The above 6
Mr. Sem Sovanny said that the installation of solar lights is in collaboration with the Royal Government for the safety of villages and communes and make it easier for local people to travel at night.
Mr. Sem Sonny confirmed that the work of deploying solar lights and building houses should be completed by the end of May 2023, while currently more than 35 kilometers of roads equipped with solar lights and 107 houses are being Build.
Mr. Heng Thou, who has now been appointed as the Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Khnar Sanday Commune, confirmed that so far, the expert group has decided to deploy solar lights in communes throughout Banteay Srei District, including: Preah Commune. A total of 1,712 trees were laid in Khun Ream Romchek and Run Ta Ek communes over a length of more than 35 kilometers along the maze.
On the same day, Mr. Sem Sovanny also donated solar lights for lighting at Tbeng Health Center and visited new mothers who are resting in the above health center.
