Vital and the Ministry of Environment Celebrate National and World Environment Day on June 5 in Stung Treng Province, Mr. Net Pheaktra: We must all work together to preserve the planet and restore the ecosystem
National and World Environment Day, June 5, 2023, was held to coincide with the 30th anniversary of Cambodia celebrating National and World Environment Day with the aim of raising public awareness of environmental issues and encouraging Citizens and communities to become active agents, sustainable and jointly maintain, protect and develop environmentally friendly.
In addition, 2023 is an important year for nations' commitment to participating in the conservation and restoration of ecosystems and combating climate change and increasing food security, water supply and biodiversity.
* First: Services provided: Food, water, wood, medicine and energy consumption * Second: Regulatory services: Climate regulation, food chain and water purification regulation * Third: Cultural services: Beautiful areas, supernatural areas, study places Education, research and recreation areas * Fourth: Support services: nutrient production, nutrient production, soil fertilization and primary production.
Mr. Chao Monira said, "Stung Treng Province is honored to be selected by the national level to celebrate the National and World Environment Day on June 5 with great pomp and meaning and as part of the outreach to the people and students." The provinces are aware of their importance in participating in preventing negative changes in environmental issues and working together for environmental peace.
He added that with this activity, the provincial administration would like to encourage departments and units around the province to continue to spread knowledge about environmental protection to all units, stakeholders and local people.
Please note that since starting the business, Vital has prioritized its work not only to provide high quality, safe, and hygienic drinking water, to participate in social activities and to respond to the needs of society. This is another task that Vital has set as a priority.
Mr. Theav Chihan praised the organization of the SEA Games during a courtesy call and discussion with Samdech Techo at the Peace Palace on the morning of May 8, 2023.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, stated that "HE Theav Chihan congratulated Samdech Techo for organizing the SEA Games in a great and successful way."
Mr. Theav Chihan said that the athletes who came to participate in this competition were happy to receive a warm welcome.
During the meeting, Mr. Theo Chihan congratulated Samdech Techo on the successful fight against Kovid 19 and the successful leadership of the ASEAN Summit and related summits.
Mr. Theav Chihan informed Samdech Techo about his current visit to Cambodia to promote the relationship between the two countries to another level.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Government and people of Singapore for sending athletes to participate in the SEA Games in Cambodia, which made the SEA Games in Cambodia even more solemn.
He also thanked the Government of Singapore for its support to Cambodia during its chairmanship of the ASEAN Summit and related summits.
Concerned about taking relations between the two countries to the next level, Samdech Techo praised the existing cooperation between the two countries and encouraged both sides to review the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding. Already signed, especially in the energy sector and the carbon marketing sector together.
The Prime Minister also encouraged to examine the possibility of cooperation in other areas that are possible.
Mr. Hun Many called on Cambodian fans to maintain their dignity and together build more positive memories for foreign friends who come to participate in the 2023 SEA Games
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, on May 08, 2023, called on the people of Cambodia, especially those who support sports when Cambodia is hosting the 32nd SEA Games. Avoid inappropriate acts as well as comments on social media that hurt foreign sports delegates, coaches or supporters of any country.
Through Facebook, Mr. Hun Many emphasized that on behalf of the host, we should welcome and take care of foreign friends who come to Cambodia, whether players, coaches or fans, how to provide a welcome. Warm, brotherly and get good memories.
Mr. Hun Many's call came after an incident between Cambodian volleyball fans to the Thai volleyball delegation after losing to Cambodia on the night of May 7, 2023 National Olympic Stadium.
Winning or losing in the spirit of sports is common, but as hosts we should welcome and care for foreign friends who come to Cambodia, whether players, coaches or fans. A warm welcome, brotherhood and good memories while Cambodia hosts.
Stories that cause any emotional or dissatisfaction to our country like this are something that we should absolutely avoid, whether in person or in person, on social media.
We hope and believe that such incidents will not happen again as Cambodia is hosting both the SEA Games from May 5 to 17 and the ASEAN Para Games on the third day. Until June 9, 2023.
In Cambodia, we have put a lot of effort into the heads of the Royal Government, the organizing committee, the sports federations, the athletes and all the participants.
Therefore, we, the Cambodian people, must work hard to participate happily as well as build a lot of memories for ourselves and our foreign friends. Vattanac Company, the official sponsor of the Football Federation of Cambodia, would like to request General Sao Sokha to continue to be the President of the Football Federation of Cambodia to continue to lead the football sector in Cambodia to grow further.
As the official sponsor of the Football Federation of Cambodia and on behalf of the management and staff of all levels of Vattanac Brewery, we would like to express our full support and request that General Sao Sokha remain President of the Football Federation of Cambodia. Cambodia continues to lead Cambodian football to grow.
