General Sao Sokha donates money to young volunteers to help organize the football match between Cambodia and Burma, which was injured due to the intrusion of spectators
(Phnom Penh): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the National Gendarmerie and President of the Football Federation of Cambodia, on the afternoon of May 08, 2023, personally donated money to volunteer youths to help organize Order during the football match between Cambodia and Myanmar and injured due to spectators scrambling.
General Sao Sokha confirmed that the injured young volunteers, one from Siem Reap, one from Battambang, one from Pursat and one female patient were being treated at the Municipal Maternity Hospital.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that after the football match between Cambodia and Myanmar and got bad results, General Sao Sokha resigned. But after this decision, many people expressed disappointment and regret for General Sao Sokha, who led the development of Cambodian football.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister also claimed that for Samdech himself, Samdech would like to express his regret for the decision of General Sao Sokha. Samdech noted that since General Sao Sokha took office as the President of the Football Federation of Cambodia, Cambodian football has progressed steadily, although the results have not been as good as desired.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that now Cambodian football has moved away from the point where we did not have before. He added that there are many countries where football can not get good results, even though the country has a population of more than 1 billion people, hundreds of millions, their football is not strong, while Cambodia has a population of more than 17 Millions of us have achieved this level, which is very good for the Cambodian people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen appealed, "As Prime Minister, I would like to call on General Sao Sokha to continue as President of the Football Federation, and this is not my specific problem, but this is my common problem. "Representatives of the Royal Government call on General Sao Sokha to continue this role with the desire of football players and people who support football."
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, expressed the hope that General Sao Sokha, who had accompanied the prince for 46 years, would continue to accept his request. He added that 46 years have passed and he hopes that General Sao Sokha will continue to respect his request when he has no authority to order the Football Federation, but on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia for the development of sports. Football.
