Chinese mysterious spacecraft returns to Earth after 276 days in space
BEIJING: A Chinese test spacecraft returned to Earth on Monday after a total of 276 days in orbit, marking the completion of a major mission to test reusable technology. In China's space sector. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, May 8, 2023.
Official images of the spacecraft have not been released to the public. However, according to Chinese state media, the mission is a major breakthrough in China's research on reusable space technology for spacecraft, which will provide an easier and less expensive way to launch. Other space missions in the future.
