(Preah Sihanouk): Police in Preah Sihanouk province launched an operation to disperse a group of thieves, rob a motorbike and steal a car, arresting a total of 13 suspects. The suspects confessed to the authorities that they had acted seven times and some of the former subjects had been imprisoned.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin told Fresh News this morning, May 8, 2023, that on May 3, residents reported that an unidentified person had committed theft. One motorcycle at Sete point is in group 12, village 2, Sangkat 2, Sihanoukville.
Immediately after receiving this information, the light criminal police force searched and arrested one suspect and confiscated the missing motorcycle exhibits.
The 13 suspects committed aggravated theft (using a sword to rob a motorcycle, breaking a motorcycle key and breaking a car key) in a total of 7 cases. In this case, the Office of Minor Criminal Police is building a case to be sent to the Sihanoukville Provincial Court for legal action.
