This year's Royal Plowing Ceremony was held at Kampong Thom Provincial Stadium in Rong Village, Trapeang Russey Commune, Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province under the highest presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia. .
The Royal Plowing Ceremony is a proclamation to the people who are engaged in farming as the beginning of the rainy season. During this year's Royal Plowing Ceremony, Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, was approved by the King of Cambodia to be the second King of the Sky, representing him and his wife, Preah Meahua.
Please note that the Royal Plowing Ceremony is an important royal tradition, considered as one of the great culture of the people of Cambodia, which all kings have always led since ancient times.
In the past, this royal ceremony was always held at Veal Preah Meru near the Royal Palace, but in recent years, the Royal Ceremony has been allowed by His Majesty the King of Life on the Rock to be held in the provinces once again so that the Cambodian people can Participate in this important royal ceremony.
