Understand Business: Some Stuck Buildings in Sihanoukville Begin Reconstruction, Experts Consider Good Signs for Real Estate
(Phnom Penh): Real estate experts say that the start of the construction of stagnant buildings in Sihanoukville will improve the real estate sector in the province, attract investors and boost property prices. This coastal province is also reviving.
Construction of a stalemate in Sihanoukville nearly four years ago has begun a series of reconstructions, and so far 100 buildings have begun to be rebuilt and renovated.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, said that there are currently 1,006 high-rise buildings in Preah Sihanouk Province, of which 400 have been completed and operational, while another 200 have been completed but are not yet operational. No transaction. At the same time, more than 200 other buildings have been suspended, but more than 100 of them have already started construction and renovation.
According to Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, since 2019, some buildings have been stuck due to disputes between builders, landlords and landowners, the supply of construction materials and non-payment of land to landowners.
The Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province said that in order to promote the operation and construction process, the Royal Government has set up a working group under the Ministry of Economy and Finance to research and study the project. Asked in principle to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to provide some favorable work to support the construction of all the buildings so that they can continue to invest in the construction of those buildings.
Between 2016 and 2019, the influx of foreign investors rushed to invest in Sihanoukville in the presence of the construction of large buildings, especially in the hotel and casino sector, which caused the real estate prices in the province to increase sharply. . But since the end of 2019, due to the closure of online games, the spread of Kovid 19 and global issues such as the war between Russia and Ukraine, some buildings have been suspended.
However, he said that at present, property prices in Sihanoukville do not seem to have changed much because the mechanism for resolving disputes of building jams has only been short-lived, so it will take some time. It will take at least another year for property prices in the coastal province to recover.
He said that if investors come to invest through the opening of shops or other businesses and when more domestic tourists visit the province, which will increase real estate prices in the future, especially at the end of the year. 2024 and early 2025, as the number of visitors to Cambodia has now increased significantly, which is a sign that investors, especially from the country, are gradually returning to start new businesses.
According to the expert, the current price of property in Sihanoukville in the downtown area is between $ 800 and $ 1,200 per square meter and on the inner streets between $ 400 and $ 600 per square meter. Square, which is a reasonable price to develop, before the outbreak of Kovid 19, land prices in the province more than double the current price.
Oknha Sam Sok Noeun, President of the Global Real Estate Association, told Fresh News that the stalemate in the construction of buildings in Sihanoukville has affected the flow of investment in Sihanoukville, but if this problem is resolved, the buildings will start operating. Gradual reconstruction will help eradicate the bad reputation and boost the real estate sector in the province. It will also help property prices recover and attract investment flows.
