Garments are Sri Lanka's largest industrial export and will generate $ 5.95 billion in revenue in 2022, helping the country during its worst financial crisis since independence. 1948, caused by a sharp decline in foreign exchange reserves.
Reuters reports, citing data from the Central Bank of Sri Lanka that the garment industry in the first quarter of 2023 will struggle, with textile and garment exports falling 13.8 percent to 1.3 billion. Million dollars.
"Given the slump in demand that we are seeing now, a $ 1 billion drop in exports this year is reasonable," he told Reuters.
Exports to the United States, Sri Lanka's biggest buyer, fell 22 percent to $ 470 million in the first quarter, according to the latest JAAF data. Exports to the European Union fell 13 percent to $ 344 million, while exports to the United Kingdom fell 10 percent to $ 167.7 million. According to Reuters.
