Cambodia, Vietnam sign MoU to promote tourism for sustainable development, environment and resilience after Kovid 19 crisis
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Vietnam have signed a Memorandum of Understanding to jointly promote tourism towards sustainable development, environment and better resilience after the Kovid 19 crisis.
The MoU was signed on May 6, 2023, signed by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism of Cambodia and Mr. Nguyen Van Hong, Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism of Vietnam at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh. The 32nd Southeast Asian Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023 from May 5-17, 2023.
The signing of the MoU is in the spirit of a meeting between Mr. Thong Khon and Mr. Nguyen Van Hong, Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism of Vietnam on May 24, 2022 in Hanoi, Vietnam to review and update the Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation. Tourism operations signed between Cambodia and Vietnam in 2015.
The Vietnamese side congratulated the Cambodian side for hosting the 32nd Southeast Asian Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023 from May 5-17, 2023 in Phnom Penh with smoothness and greatness. Especially the lighting arrangement at the opening ceremony.
The two Ministers of Tourism provided support and continued efforts to promote tourism between the two countries in accordance with the spirit of the above Memorandum of Understanding, which focused on the following contents:
1. Jointly develop tourism packages for both countries with the participation of the private sector to develop and offer joint tourism products under the framework of "two countries, one destination" to strive to attract tourists from both countries as well. Tourists from third countries visit both countries and focus on exchanging information on tourism markets, sharing good practices and exchanging study tours of tourism officials.
2. Increase joint advertising and marketing activities more effectively and efficiently so that tourism activities between the two countries can be fully resumed through the joint organization of mutual understanding tours, increase business meetings between tour operators of the two countries. Strong and participate in tourism fairs in both countries and at various international tourism events that may have the opportunity to organize.
3. Promote the further development of human resources in tourism, based on the importance of promoting best practices in tourism training and education, including training of Vietnamese and Khmer-speaking tour guides, tourism market information and exchange programs. Of students.
4. Promoting investment in tourism through investment forums and events, raising awareness of investment opportunities and facilitating investment processes in accordance with the laws of each country.
The two tourism ministers expressed their commitment to further enhance cooperation to enhance the friendship between the two countries and fruitful tourism cooperation under the framework of bilateral cooperation and cooperation. Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam Tourism Development Triangle (CLV-DTA), as well as ASEAN and other sub-regional frameworks.
The two ministers agreed to study the possibility of direct flights between Cambodia-Vietnam tourist destinations, especially Phu Quoc to Siem Reap Angkor, and the connection of Kampot tourist port to the Vietnamese port of Fukuok in order to increase tourism. Between the two countries. The two tourism ministers also assigned technical officers to prepare and implement the work program based on the new MoU.
The Vietnamese side invited the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia to pay an official visit to Vietnam to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the two National Olympic Committees to exchange experiences on the management of the National Sports Federation and the management of sports events.
