The event was attended by Mr. Uy Ry, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, Civil Servants, Civil Servants, High and Secondary School Teachers, Contract Teachers, General Contract Officers, Police Officers, Border Police Officers, Military Police Officers A total of 1,922 retired military officers participated.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng informed the ceremony that today is a meeting with all officials, both current and retired officials in Kamrieng district, and Samdech will continue to meet with all more than tens of thousands of officials in Districts and districts throughout Battambang province as well.
On this occasion, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the civil servants, competent forces and authorities at all levels of Kamrieng district who have worked hard to fulfill their roles and responsibilities. With a high sense of responsibility, Kamrieng district has developed in all areas and contributed to the success of the Royal Government's political program.
The Prince also expressed his gratitude and gratitude to all the veterans and retirees in Kamrieng district who have worked hard and sacrificed hard to bring peace, stability, security, public order and social progress as today and for all of us as generations. Always remember the achievements and merits of veterans and retirees of all generations.
Samdech Krala Hom emphasized the achievements of the 6th term of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature and believed that the ceremony, of course, we followed the evolution of society, the complex changes of the regional and global situation, especially the consequences. Rising by war and geopolitical competition on the overall work direction of the Royal Government, including the work direction for 2023 and the direction for the next 5 years.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that while the complex situation of the regional and international situation in Cambodia, the opposition extremists and some biased circles continue to explore all means to try to cause social unrest to overthrow the government. A legitimate government that emerges from elections and uses all means to obstruct the process of social development is impossible.
In addition, Samdech Khar Lo Hom Sar Kheng stated that despite the above-mentioned crises and challenges, the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has set out policies and Measures with the support and active participation of civil servants, competent forces, authorities at all levels and people across the country, including in Kamrieng district.
He said that in the next five years, we all have a lot of work to do for the bright future of the nation and expressed optimism that based on the achievements achieved and with the support. From the people, civil servants, the armed forces and authorities at all levels, the country will continue to develop in all areas in line with the expected targets in the next five years to grow even more.
