Mr. Justin Wyatt thanked the Chairman of the NEC for taking the time to meet with him and reminded him of his mission in Cambodia to attend the 2002 Commune / Sangkat Council Election and the 2003 National Assembly Election. For 2023, the Ambassador has the opportunity once again to explore the Cambodian election.
The Ambassador was interested in the current political development and development of Cambodia. "Democratic elections are not just about election day. Democracy exists before and after elections," he said.
During the meeting, Justin White wanted to know about the registration process for political parties and the list of candidates and about the registration process. In addition, the Ambassador wanted to know about the role of election observers because Australia will not deploy election observers, but Australia will assist national observers in Cambodia.
Answering the above question, the Chairman of the NEC explained the history of elections in Cambodia since 1993, the establishment of the Constituent Assembly, the Constituent Assembly became the National Assembly and the formation of the Royal Government. So far, the NEC has held 18 independent elections, which have been recognized as fair, just and transparent.
Finally, Mr. Justin Wyatt thanked Mr. Prach Chan, President of the NEC, for informing about the election process in Cambodia went well.
