Cambodia, China jointly promote peace through slogans at regional and global sports events
(Phnom Penh): The slogan of the 32nd SEA Games, which Cambodia is hosting is "Sports for Peace", remembering that in the 2022 Beijing Winter Olympics, the slogan "Sports for Peace" . At this point, Deputy Prime Minister Tea Banh emphasized that Cambodia and China are willing to work together to promote peace through the slogans of these two events.
Samdech stated that the word "peace" has great value and is in line with the People's Republic of China to promote peace through slogans in the same sports event, Samdech considered this is very consistent.
"It means that the attention of the People's Republic of China is for the world to have complete peace, which is considered very important, very meaningful. This work is in line with the needs of mankind if there is no peace," he said. "We can not do everything because of this basis, we do our best together with the People's Republic of China to become a very important steel friend."
It should be noted that Cambodia has been hosting the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games. The event is a regional sports event organized every two years by member countries. For the first time since its inception, 64 years have passed since coming to Cambodia.
"Techo Heritage National Stadium", a Chinese grant to Cambodia, is an important sports infrastructure for the sports event that Cambodia is organizing. In addition to providing valuable assistance, China has also sent senior experts to help prepare the technology, including the opening and closing ceremonies of this great SEA Games.
After 64 years of waiting, the SEA Games, the largest sporting event in Cambodia, allows people to get free tickets while the internet is free. However, the Techo Heritage National Stadium, a new achievement of the Royal Government of Cambodia after the aid of the People's Republic of China, can only accommodate more than 60,000 people.
