Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, Phase 1, has a production capacity of 195,000 cubic meters, 100% completed
(Phnom Penh): Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, Phase 1, has the capacity to produce 195 thousand cubic meters of clean water, 100% completed, which has helped meet the water needs of the people living in the current service area, especially on the outskirts of Phnom Penh.
According to the posting on the official Facebook page of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, in response to the master plan, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has completed the construction of the first phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant with a capacity of 195,000 meters. Cubes per day is ready and will be launched to test the production and distribution of clean water from April 21, 2023.
The construction of the second phase of the Bak Kheng water treatment plant, which has a production capacity of 195,000 cubic meters per day, is now more than 70% complete and is scheduled to start operating in early 2024.
Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has confirmed that the second phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant will complement the expansion of Phnom Penh Water Supply Service to areas that do not yet have access to clean water to access clean water and pipe expansion work. Water leaders must be completed by 2025 to meet the demand for clean water for people living in the south and north of Phnom Penh.
