(Siem Reap): Dr. General Soeng Samnang, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Air Force, and his wife, Ms. Ou Sithy, inaugurated a Buddhist temple and a Buddhist temple for Buddhists in Samrong village, Khnar Po commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province. Buddhism. The ceremony was held on the morning of May 4, 2023.
The ceremony was also attended by officers of the Air Force and the wives of local authorities, districts, communes, villages and 500 people.
On that occasion, General Soeng Samnang delivered a speech and conveyed the memories of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, Samdech Akka Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, whom he always misses and cares for the well-being of the people in Nationwide.
Dr. Soeng Samnang recalled that 45 years ago, the people here were deprived of all rights and freedoms by the Khmer Rouge regime, including the right to perform rituals, the right to respect and believe in religion, to gather to celebrate religious ceremonies and to decapitate monks. Original.
"Now the people have all kinds of freedoms, as now we have all celebrated the inauguration of the school in the traditional way. Importantly, we are living in peace under the right leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. "We must change, protect peace, social stability and remember that peace is not easy to find." This is what Dr. Soeng Samnang said.
Dr. Soeng Samnang emphasized that the beginning of Cambodia is not easy. Cambodia must start from scratch, because this society has been destroyed by the genocidal regime with nothing left.
It should be informed that Kampot Multipurpose Port was inaugurated under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Denmark, Urban Planning and Construction, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on May 5, 2022.
The new international deep-sea port in Kampot province has been officially opened with a substantial investment of US $ 1.5 billion invested by Kampot Logistics and Port on an area of up to 600 Hectare is located in Changhon Village, Sangkat Prek Tnaot, Bokor City, Kampot Province.
This port is the only deep-sea port of Kampot Logistics On Port Ek Co., Ltd., which can accommodate cargo ships weighing from 60,000 tons to 100,000 tons. Convenient business operations for investors, such as importing goods into and out of the country or transit goods to third countries, which can save time and money for all types of general investors.
According to Eddie k. Abbas, an international consultant for Kampot Logistics & Portfolio Ltd., said the decision to invest in Cambodia was due to the company seeing rapid economic growth in Cambodia, despite the pressure of the disease. But economic stability is still viable, which is an important factor in attracting investors.
Eddie k. Abbas said that the company decided to invest in the transport and warehousing sector in Cambodia because the company sees that the transport and warehousing sector in Cambodia is not yet good and the company. Also want to see the transport sector in Cambodia as good as in other countries, especially to be able to compete with countries in the ASEAN region.
Please note that Kampot Logistics & Export Co., Ltd. has the only deep-sea port that facilitates natural sea transportation, such as: the deepest port, the island has an air barrier And large waves, located close to the inbound and outbound transport of goods or transit goods.
