Minister Prum Sokha donates money to Mr. Hak Seang Lay who rode his motorbike from Kratie to watch the SEA Games
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group in Kratie Province, generously donated $ 100 to Mr. Hak Seang Lay, 86 years old, who rode a motorbike by himself and alone from Snoul district, Kratie province, to watch the SEA Games chess game taking place in Phnom Penh.
The money was handed over by the Minister's team to the man who was temporarily staying in a guesthouse in Phnom Penh on the evening of May 4, 2023.
Minister Prum Sokha sent a message through the working group that on the occasion of the 15th Vesak festival, he was really excited and missed his father after seeing Fresh News published by Ta Hak. Seang Lay, 86, rides a motorbike from Kratie's Snuol district to watch the SEA Games in Phnom Penh.
The Minister said that he was excited and missed his father, Layman Prum Son, who passed away on February 4, 2010 at the age of 80. If his father is still alive today, which is the day of Vesak, then Priest Son Prumson would have the opportunity to visit the SEA Games like Grandpa Hak Seang Lay.
The Minister praised the merits of Mr. Hak Seang Lay, who is long and healthy and can ride a motorbike on his own for a long distance from Kratie province. That's why he generously donated $ 100 to his grandfather to cover the cost of returning home.
After receiving the money, Mr. Hak Seang Lay, who loves to play chess and now lives in Romduol village, Sre Char commune, Snuol district, Kratie province, also thanked Minister Prum Sokha and prayed for the sacred objects in the world. Take care of the Minister and his wife, as well as their children and grandchildren to experience the four blessings of the Buddha: age, class, happiness and strength, never to be wasted.
