TOP NEWS: Samdech Techo Hun Sen sends special message to welcome the participation of the Cambodian People's Party by the activists of the opposition party (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen sent a special message to welcome the participation of the Cambodian People's Party by the activists Opposition party, according to the voice of Samdech on the night of May 4, 2023.
Through this special audio message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered Mr. Korom Dala, former President of Student Management through the university network of the opposition party and other youth groups as Samdech's children, by expressing his satisfaction through the video message and Their letter asking to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, speaking through the remarks of Mr. Korom Dala and other youth groups, sheds more light on the atrocities of some foreigners that Mr. Korom Dala's group used to serve their policies, which wanted to create The color revolution movement destroyed the peace of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Some foreigners have tried to destroy us through their children as living witnesses, not slander by the ruling party or the Royal Government, but it is true and children are living witnesses Exactly. "I thank you for understanding this situation and for being a human resource to help maintain peace and national development in the future."
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects and believes that Mr. Korom Dala and other youth groups will become important human resources of the Cambodian People's Party and the nation, which will help Cambodia to move forward.
Samdech Techo continued that on behalf of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech would like to welcome Mr. Korom Dala and other youth groups to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party, leaving the past aside and looking to the future.
Samdech believes that because Mr. Korom Dala and his youth group used to serve foreign politics, so certainly understand the value of peace and development, so will join together to keep the peace.
