NEC: Two-Day Training Campaign Training Successfully Concluded
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), closed the training course on the 7th National Assembly Election Campaign 2023, which lasted for 2 days. Second and third, May 2023.
Mr. Prach Chan stated that in order for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 to be free, fair and just in accordance with the principles of liberal multi-party democracy, the NEC has developed a calendar and master plan and implemented it. Work in each phase, especially the approval of regulations and procedures for the 7th National Assembly election in 2023, which is an important legal document for the implementation of technical work in each phase.
The NEC chairman added that the NEC has introduced an information technology system to replace the manual implementation of election officials to be more convenient, better, more transparent and more accurate.
The NEC Chairman called on all political parties, candidates and supporters to abide by the rules, regulations and principles set out in the Law on the National Assembly Election, the Rules and Procedures for the National Assembly Election. 7th Legislature 2023 Code of Conduct for Elections Principles on Human Rights and Multiparty Liberal Democracy as enshrined in the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Regarding election observation, Mr. Prach Chan called on national and international associations and non-governmental organizations working in the Kingdom of Cambodia or foreigners to take a neutral and impartial position in the election campaign and the National Assembly election.
The Chairman of the NEC instructed all participants to pay attention to prepare materials and prepare for further training for election officials at the capital, province, commune level.
