(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, and his wife and provincial working group and all government officials on the afternoon of May 4, 2023, held a Vesak ceremony to commemorate Buddhism's birth, enlightenment and Nirvana. At Wat Indry Savor (called Wat Kampong Thom) in Kdei village, Sangkat Prey Tahou, Steung Sen city, Kampong Thom province.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Nguon Rattanak said that the celebration of Vesak is to commemorate three special events related to the Buddha: those births, enlightenment, Nirvana. He was called by many other names such as Preah Samma Samput, Preah Samanakotam, Preah Chin Srey, Preah Sakyamuni, Preah Kru Krou, Preah Sastha and so on.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak also encouraged the monks, elders, pagoda committee and all Buddhists to spread Buddhism widely from the efforts to do good deeds to get monks to the next nation and educate more children. To know how to perform rituals and save merit for a life full of Brahmanism.
