Gunmen kill six Pakistani soldiers in a shootout near Afghanistan (Video inside) (Islamabad): The Pakistani army said Thursday that gunmen killed six Pakistani soldiers in a shootout. One in the northwestern tribal region on the border with Afghanistan. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, May 4, 2023.
The Islamabad government has said that militants seeking to establish strict Islamic law in Pakistan have a safe haven in Afghanistan to plan and carry out attacks.
"Mutual shelling took place between the terrorists and our forces," the army said in a statement.
The statement added that three "terrorists" were also killed when the army clashed with them, stating that it was conducting research to determine if other attackers were hiding.
However, no militant group has claimed responsibility for the bloodshed after Pakistan declared war on militants following a series of attacks, including a bomb blast at a mosque. Islam in February, which killed more than 100 people.
