Kien Ponlok, a high school history teacher in Takeo province, joined the former CNRP in 2013 and was elected head of the party's training office. He later became a member of the Cambodian Independent Teachers Association and was the secretary general of the Cambodian Intellectual Students Federation.
Kien Ponlok has been vocal about political and social events in Cambodia with Radio Free Asia and The Cambodia Daily.
Mr. Ponlok emphasized that since 2019, he has expressed his views on the above radio no less than 100 times. He said that every time he expressed his views, the association and the leaders of the former CNRP, including Ms. Mu Sochua and Mr. Eng Chhay Eang, ordered to attack and slander the government and guarantee to go abroad if there is. Any threat from the Royal Government.
Mr. Ponlok further revealed that every time he appeared on the stage with the opposition radio, he was required to say only the bad things of the Royal Government. Even if it is a positive thing, it must be turned into a negative thing.
Mr. Kien Ponlok added, "Indeed, every topic is a negative attack on the government. In fact, no matter how well the Royal Government does that, let us highlight that it is not good.
