"Even though we have been successful with such excellent results, we must not forget ourselves, so we must continue our hard work and determination," a senior health ministry official said. "We need to do more to achieve the goal of ending the TB epidemic by 2030."
He highlighted that the National Strategic Plan for TB Response is a national guideline or guideline that focuses on strategic interventions and actions, along with specific investment frameworks for TB response for 10 years from 2021 to 2030. The strategic plan clearly emphasizes the role and participation of TB patients in responding at both the national and sub-national levels.
