Dr. Thongloun Sisoulit's state visit to Cambodia will further strengthen the existing good relations, good neighborliness, brotherhood and comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership for the benefit of the people. Both.
The following is a brief history of Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit:
Thongloun Sisoulit is a Lao politician who has served as Prime Minister and is currently the President or President of the Lao PDR. He is also the fourth member of the Politburo of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party.
Sisoulit became Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of Laos in 1987 and later served as Minister of Labor and Social Welfare and Chairman of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the Lao National Assembly.
From 2001 to 2006, Sisoulit served as Deputy Prime Minister of Laos and Chairman of the State Planning Committee. From 2006 to early 2016, he served as Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs, and until April 2016, Mr. Sisoulit became Prime Minister of Laos until 2021. In March 2021, he was elected President of Laos.
