NEC Releases Press Release on the Opening of Training Course on the 7th National Assembly Election Campaign
Mr. Tep Nytha, Secretary General of the NEC, presided over the opening ceremony of the training course and said that from one election to another, Cambodia has continuously improved and reformed the election, especially after the 2013 election. Cambodia is taking a deeper level of reform, both legally, technically and electorally.
He said that through this reform, in 2014, the National Assembly amended the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia by incorporating the NEC into the new Chapter 15 (two) and later the Law on the Organization and Functioning. The Law on the Election of Members of the National Assembly and the Law on the Election of Commune / Sangkat Councils have been approved and promulgated.
He added that in accordance with the new election law and the law on the amendment of the election law since 2016, the NEC has organized and managed the work of voter registration and the election was successful and successful. Highly professional to promote multi-party liberal democracy in Cambodia.
The Secretary General of the NEC stated that in addition to improving the technical work of the election, the training and capacity building of NEC officials at all levels to carry out the upcoming election is necessary. . That is why the NEC always pays attention to organize training courses for election officials and all stakeholders on laws, regulations and election procedures at all stages of the election.
Please be informed that the training course on the 7th National Assembly Election Campaign 2023 lasts for 2 days, on the 2nd and 3rd of May 2023.
