Wang Yi, China's former foreign minister, visited Myanmar in July 2022 and met with his Myanmar counterpart but did not meet with the head of the military government. In December of the same year, China appointed a special envoy to Myanmar, who met twice with military leader Min Aung Lan and also with the leaders of Myanmar's ethnic armed groups.
