United States announces end of Kovid 19 vaccination obligation on May 11
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States will end its Kovid 19 vaccination requirement on international travelers and federal staff on May 11, the day the Kovid 19 public health emergency ends. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, May 2, 2023.
The Biden administration announced the vaccination obligation in September 2021, with strict enforcement by federal staff who refuse to vaccinate and face dismissal or other penalties.
