Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of receiving the honorary title of "Buddha Governor" and the honorary doctorate degree "Humanities and Solidarity"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, May 13, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen received the honorary title of "Buddha Governor" and the honorary doctorate degree. "Humanities and Solidarity" The ceremony was held at the cultural and historical site of Wat Phnom.
On the occasion of receiving the honorary degree and honorary doctorate degree, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech with the following main contents:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen would like to thank all the committees and relevant authorities for organizing the grand ceremony and express their gratitude to the World Buddhist Organization and the National University of Niger Padang of the Republic of Indonesia for choosing this sacred day. This is to confer the title of "Buddha of the World Buddhist Organization" and to confer the title of "Honorary Doctor of Humanities" on Samdech.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech was very grateful and respectful for this noble gesture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that today's awarding of honors and degrees is due to the participation of Mr. Morita, who has fulfilled many roles as one of Asia's deans. Morita was the first person from the Asian Development Bank to visit Cambodia to discuss Cambodia's participation in the Greater Mekong Subregion Economic Cooperation Program.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Morita's tireless participation in the reconstruction and reconstruction of Cambodia deserves to be appreciated and respected by all. In fact, Morita is not only the most visited Preah Vihear temple, but also the one that has helped accelerate the success of many of the cooperation initiatives to develop and build peace between Cambodia. And Thailand.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that the awarding of honorary degrees and honors today is a great honor for Samdech and all Cambodians and shows the invaluable relationship between Buddhism, peace, development and peace. Positive, harmonious of humanity.
* Samdech Techo stated that this offer is truly a symbol of the Buddha's teachings that have penetrated into human life in terms of society, culture, politics and economy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia has adopted Buddhism as the state religion in the 1993 Constitution, which represents the unique spirit and philosophy of Cambodia. Samdech is proud to say that Buddhism is the basis for peace building, national unification, post-conflict reconstruction, as well as our constructive participation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the extraordinary achievements and great efforts of the World Buddhist Organization in promoting the teachings of the Buddha, promoting the values of Buddhism and connecting Buddhists around the world for the noble cause of peace. For the whole of humanity.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wholeheartedly supports the mission and vision of the World Buddhist Organization in promoting further interfaith propaganda to serve the interests of humanity and our planet. Samdech would also like to take this opportunity to commend Islam and other religions that have contributed to peace building, peacekeeping and development of Cambodia in the past and present.
* Samdech Techo spoke in recognition of the Asian Cultural Council's efforts with the support of the Asian Vision Institute in promoting cultural, religious and civilized corridors connecting the Mekong-Asia-Pacific region and Many other areas. Based on all this progress, Samdech would like to share some personal views as follows:
First. Encourage the development of more initiatives linking Buddhist civilization around the world to promote education, dissemination and publication of the Buddha's teachings for institutional-think tanks. ) Buddhist institutes or universities can incorporate these values into education and research programs.
Second. We need to push for closer practical cooperation among Buddhist countries in the Mekong region and around the world to cultivate Buddhist values and philosophies that lead to justice, unity, mutual respect, tolerance and The peaceful coexistence of humanity.
Fourth. With respect to Buddhism, the state religion, we must not forget the harmonization of race and religion present in Cambodia, especially Islam, Islam and Christianity, which are the strengths of Cambodia in the past and present.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reaffirms that Cambodia will continue to uphold the values, virtues and philosophy of Buddhism, and that all Cambodians will continue to enjoy religious freedom as enshrined in our Constitution.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on the World Buddhist Organization, the Asian Cultural Council and the Cambodian and international Buddhist communities from all denominations to work together with UNESCO and other UN agencies to further promote interfaith harmony to achieve Achieving our common goal is peace and stability.
