(Oddar Meanchey): Residents of Anlong Veng district have the opportunity to gather to watch the live broadcast of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games at the former Ta Mok House Museum from April 29 until Until May 16, 2023, while Cambodia is hosting the Games. This is according to Mr. Ly Sok Kheang, Director of Anlong Veng Peace Center.
Many former members of the Khmer Rouge considered this to be their happiest time. The live broadcasts have created an atmosphere that often attracts tourists from other provinces to sit together. When the game started on screen, all the spectators had a chance to converse and create a happy mood.
Located about 450 km from the Moradok Techo National Stadium, the event is being organized by the Anlong Veng District Administration, a district in northern Cambodia along the Cambodian-Thai border in collaboration with the Anlong Veng Peace Center. Two live screens that can receive images from digital TV devices.
Mr. Huon Phat, 52 years old, and Mr. Long Loueur, 44 years old, attended the event at Ta Mok House Museum and expressed their happiness with the live broadcast.
Phat, a former Khmer Rouge soldier, said: "I'm very happy to be able to watch live sports events hosted by Cambodia, compared to before 1998, the war is still going on. "
