General knowledge: What do the five legions of the Olympics mean?
(Phnom Penh): The Olympics is an international sporting event that is attended by athletes from all over the world and is usually held every four years. You may have noticed that the symbol of the Olympics is the five contiguous armies.
Each of the five colors, including blue, yellow, black, green, and red, along with the white surface of the Olympic flag, represents the colors on the flags of the countries from which they were created. Became the official symbol of the Olympics in 1915. Tell loved ones the dangers of drugs! Nationwide drug crackdown for May 1: 12 cases cracked, 31 arrested
