Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Meets Cambodian Sports Delegates Before Participating in SEA Games
(Phnom Penh): On the evening of Monday, May 1, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with a delegation of Cambodian sports before They participated in the 32nd SEA Games held in Cambodia.
On the occasion of meeting with the Cambodian sports delegation before participating in the SEA Games, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a talk for about 1 hour, below the main content:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Peace Palace was built for high-level meetings, but today received a delegation to the SEA Games venue.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this Peace Palace was not built just for Samdech to work, but for the Royal Government of all generations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the King for giving the sport of fire in Siem Reap in the past.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Akki Victory Parade is like a national festival.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the National Committee for the SEA Games led by Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh for his efforts in organizing the competition from all angles.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the closure of a number of telephone numbers that do not fully transfer information to Samdech regarding the provision of tickets for football spectators.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia's goal in organizing the SEA Games is not for money. Cambodia's goal goes far beyond money.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the past, Cambodia was known only until the Pol Pot regime was overthrown. But now Cambodia is known through its products and the opportunity to compete in the SEA Games is known to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his happiness and satisfaction to the Cambodian national athletes who were born abroad but participated in the national representative competition. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers this activity to show the participation in promoting the nation's reputation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advises to pay attention to halal food for athletes from Muslim countries. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is too expensive and must be carefully considered, even if it costs more.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen responds to news in Malaysia that do not worry about traffic jams for sports delegates. Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the media to clarify its broadcast.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on the people to continue to maintain order and not to jump over the fence to watch the game.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech is not worried about the competition technique, but what the players have to respect is the ethics of the competition.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on various TV stations to jointly broadcast the SEA Games.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the competition does not respect the rules, rules and ethics is making us lose again.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advises athletes to avoid using drugs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reprimanded the players during the match to fight back, not to suffer.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded athletes, whether they win or lose, must make friends with their partners. Samdech Techo expects athletes to build as many friendships as possible.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks Chinese President Xi Jinping for helping build the Techo Heritage National Stadium worth about $ 150 million.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is fortunate that Cambodia has successfully managed 19 cases of Kovid, making it possible for Cambodia to host the SEA Games.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if Cambodia has a prosperous economy, Samdech will provide more aid to other countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen sponsors $ 500 for each SEA Games delegation.
