Seven political parties officially recognized for candidate registration
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has confirmed that seven of the eight political parties have been officially recognized on the registration of candidates for the National Assembly election. Seventh, 2023.
The recognition of these seven political parties was made after a meeting to review and decide on the application for registration of political parties and the list of candidates under the chairmanship of Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC on the morning of the 1st. This May 2023.
After reviewing and discussing the documents of each political party in detail, the NEC meeting decided to officially recognize the application for registration of political parties and the list of candidates (seven). As follows:
* First, officially recognize the registration application of the Cambodian People's Party, which has 25 constituencies, capitals and provinces, and the list of candidates for the election.
* Second: Officially recognize the registration application of the Cambodian Youth Party, which has 25 constituencies, capitals and provinces and the list of candidates for the election.
* Third: Officially recognize the application form for registration of the Khmer United National Party, which has 25 constituencies in the capital and provinces and the list of candidates for the election.
* Fourth: Officially recognize the application for registration of the Theosophical Party, which has 25 constituencies in the capital and provinces and the list of candidates for the election.
