Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Cambodia is the first country to support Japan's "Free and Open Indo-Pacific Initiative", all initiatives that want Cambodia to support must guarantee three points (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia "Cambodia is the first country to support Japan's free and open Indo-Pacific Initiative," he said, adding that any initiative that Cambodia wants to support must guarantee three principles.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks were made on the occasion of the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a new container port worth nearly 1 billion dollars at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port this morning, May 1, 2023.
"Some Japanese initiatives have been supported by Cambodia, such as the 'Indo-Pacific Free and Open' Cambodia, the first country to support Japan on this issue, based on three principles, not just Japan, but all countries. " This is the confirmation of Samdech Techo.
Samdech added that the three principles are: 1. Any initiative must serve peace and development, 2. The initiative must not be against any country or group; and third. The initiative must respect ASEAN's middle ground and ASEAN's Indo-Pacific concept.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen declares that he does not support any initiative that leads to war or opposition to any other country, and adds that Cambodia's foreign policy is an independent foreign policy based on the rule of law. Therefore, any initiative that guarantees the above three points can not be, Cambodia will not participate.
The Prime Minister further stated that Cambodia will not play with it if the initiative is against others or to curb the influence of other countries.
