Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Groundbreaking Ceremony for the Construction of a New Container Terminal at Nearly $ 1 Billion at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, May 1, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a new container terminal at the port. Sihanoukville Autonomous Region. The construction of the new port, which will cost nearly 1 billion US dollars, is to further expand the capacity of sea freight to meet Cambodia's economic and trade growth.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen gave a speech for more than an hour, the following are the main contents of Samdech:
* As a start to the conversation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that three years ago at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, Cambodia helped the ship West Dam, which is a large humanitarian body.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in December 2023, the Westster Dam will return to Cambodia again. With the return of the Westster, it will be a symbol of Cambodia's concern for the right to life and liberty.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects that some people who were stranded on the Westster ship will return to Cambodia again.
* Today is International Labor Day, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the workers across the country for their contribution to building the society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on the country to give money to Naga workers to protest, to withdraw and not to be internationalized in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if Samdech did not act, the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port would become a private port.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that if the port becomes private, do not expect Japan to provide development assistance.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the story at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port is very complicated.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech is a complex surgeon at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Japan is a leading country in providing assistance and loans for development in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks Japan for having a way to pay off the debts of the old government to enable Cambodia to get new loans to develop the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants to see lenders use Japanese methods to pay off Cambodia's debts.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that every time Samdech met with the Prime Minister of Japan, he always asked Japan to help expand Cambodia's deep-sea port as soon as possible.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the construction of a deep-water port will reduce operating costs on trade.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the construction of a deep-sea port will reduce the transaction costs of trade and make Cambodia able to receive ships from 18 percent to more than 90 percent.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked to ask Japan about the accusation that the Royal Government was corrupt and used Japanese loans for development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen supports Japan for integration between the SEZ and the port of Sihanoukville.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that at this time, Samdech can proudly say that Cambodia-Japan relations have reached a new stage, a comprehensive strategic partnership.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is the first country to support a free and open Indo-Pacific policy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all international initiatives that Cambodia wants to support must serve three principles, including: to serve peace and development, not to oppose other countries, and to respect ASEAN's middle ground and ASEAN's Indo-Pacific vision. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in 2022, the trade volume between Cambodia and Japan will reach 1.948 million US dollars. Of that, Cambodia exported $ 1.170 million to Japan and Japan imported $ 774 million to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the past 33 years, Samdech Techo has never had a headache after receiving Japanese artificial eyes. Before wearing Japanese glasses, Samdech always carried a headache medicine with him.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs national and private television to broadcast live SEA Games events.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the national income was distributed to all members of the Royal Government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the remarks made by critics not to go to the King to open the SEA Games as a malicious intention to divide the King and the Royal Government. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that only Indonesia, the Philippines and Brunei have announced the opening of the SEA Games.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to clarify the reasons for not taking money for the SEA Games delegation to show the great sympathy and enthusiasm of Cambodia.
