By: Mr. Ouch Leang, Researcher of the Department of Asian, African and Middle Eastern Studies of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia View Photo: Samdech Techo Hun Sen inspects the construction of the third wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): On Sunday morning, April 30, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, inspected the construction process of the third wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville. The third wastewater treatment plant is located in Village 4, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville.
A strong young architect, Mr. Ly Raksmey, said that compared to the two wastewater treatment plants in Sihanoukville, which were launched two years ago, showed that MABR technology is highly efficient, no sound. Noise, odorless, affecting the surrounding residents, stable and energy-saving results.
Mr. Ly Raksmey also said that the third wastewater treatment plant has the capacity to filter about 20,000 cubic meters of wastewater per day. Affected by wastewater from Zone 5 and Zone 6, which covers an area of 2,690 hectares in Sangkat 4.
The third wastewater treatment plant was built on October 1, 2020 and is scheduled to be completed by the end of June 2023. As of April 24, 2023, it has achieved about 89 percent. The third wastewater treatment plant is built on an area of only 1 hectare.
Please note that the wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville is an achievement born of the consideration of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and relevant authorities to protect the environment. In particular, protect the environment, such as beaches and biodiversity in the sea, not to be affected by sewage from homes, restaurants, hotels and other locations.
The wastewater treatment plant serves to filter the wastewater before discharging it into the sea or into the sea.
Wastewater treatment plant construction began at the same time as the construction of all 37 roads in Sihanoukville. Two treatment plants have been launched in the past.
The first wastewater treatment plant has a treatment capacity of 5,200 cubic meters per day. The first station is affected by wastewater from the third area, which covers an area of 364 hectares in Sangkat 3.
The second wastewater treatment plant has a treatment capacity of 7,200 cubic meters per day. The second station is affected by wastewater from the fourth area, which covers an area of 486 hectares in Sangkat 3.
In addition to the above three wastewater treatment plants, Sihanoukville has seven other wastewater pumping stations, four of which were built by the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia and three by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. To pump wastewater to the wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville (16 hectares).
