Mr. Hong Sochua raised these signs, noting that to this day, there are still some people who shoot scammers who have set up investment projects in order to defraud the people. Although the perpetrators have been arrested, there are still a number of scams.
Recently, thousands of families in Kampot province lost almost $ 40 million after believing in scammers and drowning to borrow money from banking and microfinance institutions, including their own money to buy the land of Duke Chea Saran. .
To avoid being scammed in any investment project, Mr. Hong Sohua gave five tips to identify as a real investment project or a fraudulent investment project for the purpose of deciding before investing in any project:
1: Promise high profits
Mr. Hong Sohour explained that before making an investment, we need to notice that when someone comes to guide us on an investment project, how much profit is guaranteed? He said that if the investment project Higher profitability is a more dubious project because real investment projects can not be too profitable.
2: Profit too regular
Mr. Hong Sohour stated that this is also a dubious project because the project that actually invested can not be profitable too regularly. Real investment projects can sometimes be quick to make a profit, sometimes not easy to make a profit and sometimes a loss.
3: Secret formula
Mr. Hong Sohour also said that this point also needs to see if the staff who come to introduce an investment project, they have explained to us how to make a profit. If they are secretive, saying that this is a secret or that their explanation is messy, we do not understand, this is also a sign of deception.
4: Difficult to receive official documents
Before deciding to invest, you should carefully consider the official documents or financial statements. We need to see how easy it is to review documents related to various investments, if it is difficult to request such documents, it can also be a dubious project.
5: Difficult to withdraw money
