Cambodia asks Thailand to stop handcuffing Cambodian workers who cross the border illegally because they are not criminals
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia, through a representative of the Thai Ministry of Foreign Affairs, has asked the Thai side to stop handcuffing Cambodian workers who illegally cross the border to work in Thailand because they are not criminals.
The request of the Cambodian Embassy in Thailand came after Thai authorities on April 20, 2023, arrested 14 Cambodian workers who had illegally crossed the border to work in Thailand in Samut Prakan province.
An Sok Khoeun, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, said that after receiving the above information, the Cambodian Embassy in Thailand and the Cambodian Consulate General in Sa Kaeo contacted the Thai authorities and visited Directly with the above Cambodian workers in Natrat area, Samut Prakan province and intervened to repatriate as well.
A Foreign Ministry spokesman said: "When they were taken to a detention center in Bangkok, the workers were handcuffed by Thai authorities for fear of escaping. They were released by Thai authorities when they arrived. Bang Keo Detention Center (Bangkok). According to the coordination and negotiation of the Cambodian Embassy, the Thai authorities will send the workers back to Cambodia after the interrogation and completion of documents.
The spokesman added that the Cambodian Embassy in Thailand as well as the Cambodian Consulate General in Sa Kaeo always advise all Cambodian workers to work legally in Thailand to avoid any consequences.
