The decree was officially posted on the Kremlin website, and an increase in the conviction for treason from 20 years to life in prison has already been approved by the Russian parliament. Russia's parliament has also approved an increase in the maximum penalty for committing acts of terrorism that destabilize and destabilize Russia from 15 to 20 years in prison.
Those found guilty of vandalism could face up to 20 years in prison (previously 15 years), while those convicted of international terrorism could face up to life in prison. Previously sentenced to 12 years in prison. But the decree does not explain what international terrorism is.
Putin's signing of the decree comes as critics say Russian authorities are stepping up repression and silencing dissidents or criticizing his war in Ukraine. But the Kremlin claims that the laws are aimed at protecting the country from Ukrainian and Western intelligence agencies.
