Kun Nhem Leads a Delegation to Korea Customs Week and Memorandum of Understanding on Strengthening Cooperation
(Korea): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, led a delegation to Korea Customs Week 2023 under the theme "Global Customs and Customs Cooperation" from 26 to 28 April 2023, with the participation of leaders and delegates of the customs administrations of 75 countries, as well as international organizations, the private sector and the international network of customs universities.
The leaders of the Roundtable agreed and approved the Joint Declaration on "Global Customs Cooperation and Customs Digital", and on the last day of the meeting, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia jointly signed the Joint Declaration on "Customs Cooperation on Drug Suppression in the Asia-Pacific Region."
Separately, on April 27, 2023, the Customs Administration of Cambodia and the Customs Administration of Korea met bilaterally and signed a Memorandum of Understanding to strengthen cooperation and mutual assistance related to customs work.
This Memorandum of Understanding will be a mechanism to pave the way for (1) the further strengthening of good bilateral cooperation, (2) the contribution to the promotion of trade facilitation, and (3) the strengthening of closer ties for exchanges and cooperation. Share information to fight transnational crime; and (4) Strengthen cooperation in providing technical assistance to build the capacity of officials of the two customs administrations.
