BEIJING (Reuters) - Chinese Commerce Minister expressed concern over German export restrictions at a meeting with German economy ministers just hours after reports that Berlin was considering restrictions on trade. Exports of chemicals used to make semiconductors.
The two sides also discussed the establishment of a fair and equitable business environment, the Chinese Ministry of Commerce said in a statement.
Germany is discussing restrictions on some chemical exports to China, Bloomberg reported on Thursday, citing sources familiar with the matter. The proposal is part of a package of measures being discussed by Prime Minister Olaf Scholz's government that would cut off access to Chinese goods and services needed for the production of state-of-the-art semiconductor equipment.
