British navy says ship mysteriously attacked off the coast of Yemen
The British military says a ship was mysteriously attacked off the coast of Yemen on Friday. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, April 28, 2023.
The attack took place in the waters of Yemen's coastal city of Nishtun, which borders Oman, a British naval trading operator backing ships passing through the Middle East.
The report added that the shooting took place on an unidentified ship in the Gulf of Aden as three boats were chasing it. Details have not been reported.
The Gulf of Aden is a major route for global trade and has seen frequent attacks by Iranian-backed Houthi militants in Yemen. Most of the harassment in the area has stopped in recent years.
Nishtun is controlled by coalition forces of the internationally recognized Yemeni government and backed by a Saudi-led coalition.
