(Phnom Penh): The Union of Civil Society Organizations, a youth group of about 22 civil society organizations, issued a joint statement stating that there are six bad political cultures that have been nurtured and are being nurtured in Cambodian society through extremist politicians. Sam Rainsy that these political cultures will lead to the division of Cambodian society.
That bad political culture includes:
First, divisive politics through the use of political messages by accusing Cambodians of being Vietnamese puppets, betraying the nation, betraying the party, betraying groups, etc. This is the cultivation of extremist hatred that divides Cambodian society.
Second, doing politics by sinking criticism is not constructive criticism, this is to cultivate an unfair mindset on one side and to hinder the national development efforts of the winning party.
Third, politics destroys democracy by accusing it of betraying, selling puppets, or obstructing all means of the participation of citizens or politicians in the opposition or youth organizations, associations with the ruling party or other parties in political society.
Fourth, politics destroys peace by calling on the people's soldiers to rebel against the government to fulfill their ambitions, which is an evil act to destroy national peace, harmony, and coexistence between Cambodians and Cambodians.
Fifth, politics does not respect national and international law by violating all kinds of laws to criticize one side or to win without thinking about the rules, ethics and virtues of the society.
Sixth, politics does not think about the nation, the national economy, the unity of the Khmer nation, by saying bad things only from their own country to foreign countries for personal political gain.
Youth groups and civil society organizations see these six bad political cultures as having a serious impact on the nation now and in the future. We call on the young people who support Mr. Sam Rainsy to think long and hard about the future of the nation and to stop supporting such politics. Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration will organize live broadcasts of football matches in SEA Games in 5 cities and districts
