Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Inaugurates Sustainable Infrastructure Connectivity Project in Southeast Asia
Mr. Yong The Kim said that the International Transport Forum is a forum with a total of 64 members, including 44 countries in Europe, while in Southeast Asia, only eight countries that Cambodia joined last year. 2022.
He said that each year there are about 30-60 reports that strive to provide member countries with all the most up-to-date and rigorous information of testimony, the most comprehensive and accurate knowledge that policy makers can make. Persuade and take into account for policy formulation to improve transport connectivity.
He stressed that it is also important that we organize the annual meeting as an opportunity for the Minister of Transport, which is about 45-45 people / Ministries from countries around the world to attend this meeting. In fact, on May 24-26, 2023, we will hold our annual meeting, which will bring high benefits for the development and development of sustainable policies.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol confirmed that this International Transport Forum is a forum and Cambodia is the first ASEAN member country to become a full member in 2022.
He stressed that the forum is to discuss the transportation gap between European and Asian countries, how to improve the flow of goods to reduce shipping costs. For consumers, cheaper than now. Another is to organize green transport to reduce any pollution.
(Preah Vihear): Although the traditional Khmer New Year has passed for many days, but left a lot of fun and unforgettable memories for the people, especially all young Cambodians. At home and abroad, this is due to the peace factor throughout the country under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Ms. Penh Chanthou, a resident of Samlanh village, Tbeng Mouy commune, Sangkum Thmei district, Preah Vihear province, said this morning, April 28, 2023, that the New Year New Year has passed a few days ago. This is an unforgettable fun for Cambodians across the country.
For Wat Thaksin Kiri, also known as Wat Samlanh, located in her village, the New Year celebration was held for 7 nights and 7 days, led by a group of young people with the permission of the Chief Inspector and the pagoda committee also provided fun. To the people as well as better security.
Ms. Penh Chanthou continued that what has never happened before is that a great force of unity came from the hearts of the people by raising money to buy a speaker for 12 million Riel as a common property in the commune. Ours. She said the loudspeaker served to celebrate the New Year for seven nights and seven days without having to rent a loudspeaker from outside as every year.
In addition, Ms. Penh Chanthou said that this speaker is also for rent back to the people who organize various programs at a low price, and the income from renting the speaker is saved to supply and help people. Which is very difficult as well as for the development of pagodas, schools in the villages and communes.
Ministry of Labor Disseminates Workplace Accident Prevention Measures on World Day for Occupational Safety and Health
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training celebrates the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health 2023 under the theme "Safe Work Environment and Occupational Health is a Basic Rights and Principles in the Workplace" Introduce measures to prevent and reduce accidents at work.
This day is held on April 28, 2023, this year is the 18th time that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training organized the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health in collaboration with APHEDA and Royal Special Economic Zone. The Phnom Penh Group was chaired by Mr. Pheng Sokham, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, with a total of more than 1,300 participants.
Mr. Pheng Sokham said that the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health is an international campaign organized annually by governments, employers' associations and unions of member countries of the International Labor Organization (ILO) around the world to commemorate Workers who have lost their lives and suffered from occupational accidents and diseases in the workplace and to raise awareness on proper, safe and healthy work.
The Ambassador noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia is paying close attention to occupational health and safety, which are included in the legal and regulatory framework.
On that occasion, Secretary of State Pheng Sokham also sent some recommendations to all stakeholders to continue to implement the following measures to prevent occupational accidents in the workplace:
* Continue to pay attention to the implementation of the guidelines on strengthening fire prevention measures and improving the occupational health of workers in enterprises.
* Continue to share good practices and experiences related to occupational safety and health management of enterprises, establishments to other enterprises to improve safety and occupational health conditions from each other.
* Increase the regular assessment of occupational safety and health management systems in enterprises and establishments and put in place preventive measures to prevent and reduce occupational accidents and diseases related to the workplace.
He added that what is special is that the decision not to take money from sports delegates and athletes has made Cambodia famous to the world, especially to the International Olympic Movement.
