In its daily update on Chinese military activity in the last 24 hours, the Taiwan Defense Ministry said that a total of 19 Chinese military aircraft had entered Taiwan's ADIZ, and the most notable among That was the TB-001 fighter drone that flew around the island. It first flew across the waterway between Taiwan and the Philippines and then up to eastern Taiwan before flying back to the Chinese coast.
According to Chinese state media, the TB-001 drone is capable of carrying out high-altitude and long-range missions and has released images of it equipped with several missiles and bombs. In the past, the Chinese Air Force has flown what it calls Taiwan siege missiles using H-6 bombers capable of carrying nuclear weapons.
A mountain crocodile weighing more than 3 kg was found by the people and handed over to the park ranger to be released back into the natural canal
(Koh Kong): A mountain crocodile, one of the rarest animals in the world, weighing 3.5 kg, 1.15 meters long, was found by the people in Dong Peng commune, Sre Ambel district, Koh Kong province in the South Cardamom Mountain National Park. And handed over to the ranger of the Ministry of Environment.
The Cardamom Mountains in Cambodia provide excellent habitat for the survival of mountain crocodiles from the Osom area in Pursat province to the foothills of the Kampong Som canal system, Sre Ambel district, Koh Kong province.
Cambodia is a globally important habitat for the survival of the mountain crocodile or crocodile, which is estimated to number between 200 and 400 living in natural habitats in the country. In the world, the number of mountain crocodiles of reproductive age is no more than 1,000. Banteay Meanchey Military sends two suspects to provincial court after arrest in motorcycle theft case
(Banteay Meanchey): Poipet City Gendarmerie arrested two suspects according to the complaint of the victim in the case of motorcycle theft committed at 2:50 AM on April 23, 2023 at New building for rent in O'Chrov village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
After receiving the complaint, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie conducted a search until 5:30 PM on April 26, 2023. The target was identified and the two suspects were arrested. Both exhibits were confiscated and brought to the Municipal Gendarmerie Base for procedural action.
After being arrested and interrogated, the two suspects confessed that they had actually stolen a motorcycle from the victim. Based on the confession and the evidence, the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent the suspect to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters to proceed with the procedure.
The suspect is currently being sent to the Provincial Court by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Office on the morning of April 28, 2023 for sentencing.
