(Phnom Penh): For two days from April 25 to 27, 2023, strictly following the orders of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie. The military launched an operation to crack down on forest crime and confiscated more than 300 cubic meters of timber, and arrested 12 people.
Brigadier General Eng Hee pointed out that in the operation to crack down on forest crime, the Armed Forces also arrested 12 people involved, 7 trailers, 13 bulldozers, 1 motorcycle, 30 liters of gasoline. , 5 chainsaws and 14 chainsaws.
A spokesman for the National Gendarmerie said the operation took place in four provinces, including Kratie, Stung Treng, Kampong Thom and Preah Vihear. After the crackdown, both exhibits, materials and people involved were handed over to the Forestry Administration for further processing.
In order to implement the order of General Sao Sokha more effectively, Brigadier General Eng Hee added that this morning, April 28, 2023, Lt. Gen. Hong Vinul, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie led the task. An emergency meeting in Kratie province with relevant police forces.
