One of Two Suspects Fleeing from Detention Center at Russey Keo Police Inspectorate Arrested in Oddar Meanchey Province
(Phnom Penh): One of the two suspects who escaped from the temporary detention center at the Russey Keo District Police Inspectorate on the night of April 25, 2023, was arrested by the police and returned this morning. April 28, 2023 in Oddar Meanchey province.
Brigadier General San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News that a Cambodian suspect had been arrested by the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police and the Russey Keo District Police Inspectorate. Contact the procedure to get back.
Brigadier General San Sok Seiha also confirmed that another foreign suspect has not been arrested yet, while the specialized police force is continuing to search carefully to find the arrest.
Please be informed that two suspects escaped from the temporary detention center at the Russey Keo District Police Inspectorate on the night of April 25, 2023. The reason for the opportunity for the two suspects to escape from the detention center was due to the rain and strong winds, then suddenly there was a power outage.
When the fire broke out, a loud noise was heard in the temporary detention room, and the police entered and found a half-meter-wide wall that allowed the two suspects to crawl out.
The two suspects, one a foreigner arrested in connection with the use of violence against the same foreigner and the other a Cambodian arrested in connection with a car theft case in Banteay Meanchey province after stealing a car From the territory of Russey Keo district.
