Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates (UAE) have agreed on the terms of a bilateral Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement as the Persian Gulf states look to strengthen trade ties in the economic field. Strategies, especially in Asia. According to Reuters.
The two countries have concluded negotiations on a trade agreement called the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA) in Reuters, Reuters reported, citing a statement issued by the United Arab Emirates' WAM news agency. Six months after the start of negotiations.
When implemented, the CEPA will eliminate tariffs on Cambodia's agricultural products, leather goods and garments and footwear, while opening up new markets for the UAE's manufacturing and industrial sectors.
The CEPA program, which began in 2021 as the global economy recovers from the effects of the Kovid-19 pandemic, is a key element of the UAE's economic development strategy, which aims to double the size of the economy. $ 762 billion by 2030.
The Persian Gulf nation has signed CEPAs with India, Indonesia, Israel and Turkey and is in the process of negotiating similar agreements with other countries, including Costa Rica, Kenya and Ukraine.
The non-oil trade of the United Arab Emirates with Cambodia will exceed $ 401 million in 2022, up 31 percent from 2021, while bilateral foreign direct investment will reach nearly $ 4 million by the end of 2020.
Pen Sovicheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed to Fresh News on April 27 that the signing of a bilateral trade agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates is scheduled for the end of April. However, due to some work that has not been completed, that is to clear the text, while the law has been postponed until the end of May or the beginning of June.
"Due to the Cambodia-UAE Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, there are up to 18 chapters, equivalent to 580 pages, so it is time to clear the text as a matter of law," he said. We expect to be able to complete the remaining work, leading to the request for permission from the Royal Government to sign this agreement in late May or early June.
Please be informed that CEPA has announced the opening of the first round of negotiations on October 24-26, 2022 in Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates. The two sides then held the second round of talks on December 19-21, 2022 in Phnom Penh and the third round of talks, the last round on 20-22 February 2023 in Dubai, United Arab Emirates. The agreement was officially concluded on March 16, 2023.
