(Phnom Penh): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, reminded hospitals and clinics or private medical centers that are licensed to operate in Cambodia to continue to pay attention to the maximum. According to the rules, in terms of technical, medical, infrastructure, training, resources, use of digital systems, management and maintenance with proper professional ethics.
She said this was done to ensure that its services would receive quality and safety in line with the minimum standards for the recently launched private health facilities in response to the strategic health plan. 2023 to 2030. This statement was made by Dr. O Vandin during the official inauguration of the Sunrise Sen Sok Medical Center earlier this week at Aeon Mall.
She continued that the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has made efforts to strengthen and improve the health system to meet the needs of examination and treatment services to the people in a timely manner with more modern technology in line with the evolution of medical technology in the context of digital health. Provide more efficient and quality services.
At the same time, the Ministry of Health has allowed the establishment of modern hospitals or clinics or private medical centers to meet the needs of the health care sector, contributing to the reduction of the high cost of seeking health care abroad for Cambodians.
Dr. O Vandin stated, "Private health facilities remain a health development partner within the health care system, which requires quality improvement and must provide quality and safe services to the people of Cambodia, regardless of race. "No color or political affiliation, no matter what the circumstances."
On behalf of the Ministry of Health, she hopes that the presence of Sunrise Sen Sok Medical Center now and in the future will improve the provision of health services in Cambodia and make it easier, more efficient and more trusted by the people. "Will be able to promote the health sector in Cambodia to grow for the common benefit of the country and the people of Cambodia."
Sunrise Sensok Medical Center offers services such as: medical examination, general medicine, emergency care and minor surgery, diagnostics: medical imaging and immunization laboratories, etc. Since 2016, Sunrise Japan Phnom Penh Hospital has been committed to serving the people of Cambodia through the provision of world-class medical services. During the seven years of operation, more than 25,000 health check-ups were provided each year.
Dr. Hong Chhay, Managing Director of Sunrise Sen Sok Medical Center, also said, "Our mission for Sunrise Medical Center is to ensure that all Cambodians have access to the best medical services just one step away from home."
The new center is a state-of-the-art clinic that aims to accelerate the provision of preventive health check-ups with a variety of check-up options, he added. Special will guide people to make wise decisions according to their health needs. This initiative is to protect life and make it healthier for every citizen living in Cambodia. People will go through a wide range of health care experiences with affordable prices and a comfortable environment.
Sunrise Medical Center is committed to providing the best services to satisfy the people through 4 main points: 1- Affordable, 2- Fast service 3- High quality and 4- Comfort.
