Expansion of power transmission and distribution system in Phnom Penh and some provinces under Japanese grant has been officially launched.
(Phnom Penh): Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has officially launched a project to expand transmission and distribution systems in Phnom Penh and a project to expand the distribution network through the southern economic corridor in Koh Kong, Svay Rieng and Banteay Meanchey provinces under the Concession and Aid Framework. Grant from the Royal Government of Japan.
The official inauguration ceremony was attended by Mr. Suy Sem, Minister of Mines and Energy, Mr. You Ino Assuzi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia on the morning of April 27, 2023 at the National Olympic Stadium in Phnom Penh.
Sanui Socho, Representative of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia, said that the expansion of infrastructure and service facilities in Phnom Penh, as well as the development in rural areas, urgently required the improvement of substations and cables. Transmit electricity to continue to supply power stably.
Mr. You Ino Assuzi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, expressed his pleasure at the continuous development of Cambodia-Japan relations through assistance and cooperation, as evidenced by the inauguration of both projects. Today.
He strongly hopes that the achievements of these two power grid projects will last for many years, which will benefit the Cambodian people and boost the Cambodian economy.
Mr. Suy Sem, Minister of Mines and Energy, said that on behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, he would like to express his deep gratitude to the Royal Government and the people of Japan for providing 6,880 million yen in concessional loans and grants from the Royal Government. Government of Japan 893 million yen for project development in the energy sector in Cambodia.
The Minister stated that the transmission line infrastructure and substations built within the framework of the project that has been officially inaugurated now will make the transmission system in Phnom Penh into a network to help strengthen each other. On the other hand, for the transmission of electricity, which will help strengthen the supply, there must be quality, stability and sustainability throughout the country.
For the electricity distribution network in the project also made the supply to the industrial and commercial areas in Phnom Penh and in the economic corridors of the three provinces to be more quality, stable and sustainable in accordance with the policy of industrial development in Cambodia 2015-2025. .
The Kremlin welcomes the telephone meeting between Xi Jinping and Zelensky, but the goal of the war remains the same.
MOSCOW (Reuters) - The Kremlin on Thursday said it welcomes anything that could bring the end of the Ukraine conflict closer. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, April 27, 2023.
The Kremlin made the remarks in response to media inquiries about its views on a telephone conversation between Chinese President Xi Jinping and Ukrainian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday. On the Ukraine crisis. However, the Kremlin stressed that Russia still needs to achieve the objectives of its special military operations aimed at the war in Ukraine.
