Australia plans to overhaul immigration control system to accept skilled workers
Sydney: The Australian government on Thursday proposed improving its immigration system to expedite the admission of highly skilled workers and streamlining procedures for permanent residence. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Thursday, April 27, 2023.
Government officials from the Australian Labor Party say the current system used to recruit skilled workers by past test scores will be redesigned to better identify skilled people to meet Australia's economic needs.
