The following is the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Administration: Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon chaired a meeting to review the progress of economic diplomacy in the first quarter of 2023 and a discussion on the selection of Khmer food for foreign guests in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on April 25, 2023, chaired a meeting to review the first quarter of 2023 economic diplomacy and recruitment talks. Khmer cuisine for receiving foreign guests in Cambodia ”organized by the Economic Diplomatic Coordination Team at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation in Hybrid format.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon praised the good cooperation and support from the relevant ministries and institutions and the private sector in implementing the 2021-2023 Economic Diplomacy Strategy. The Deputy Prime Minister also stressed the importance of using food as a diplomatic tool, contributing to the promotion of trade, culture, tourism, exports of Cambodian products, as well as improving skills in the food sector.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister supported the initiative to select Khmer cuisine, which requires the participation of local stakeholders, especially from the private sector, such as hotels and restaurants, which often receive foreign guests in Cambodia to ensure national identity. As well as identifying standard flavors and ingredients and can be a new step in promoting Khmer food to foreign guests and enhance the national prestige to another level.
After the meeting, Dr. Nhim Khemara prepared a solidarity meal for the representatives of relevant ministries and institutions and the private sector to taste delicious Khmer food and learn about the ingredients as well as cooking techniques. Dr. Kao Kim Hourn Meets 12 Young Officials from Representatives of the Political Security Community, the Economic Community and the ASEAN Socio-Cultural Community of Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam
(Jakarta, Indonesia): On the morning of Thursday, April 27, 2023, at the ASEAN Secretariat in Jakarta, the Republic of Indonesia, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, met with 12 young officials from the ASEAN Security-Political Community. ASEAN Economic Community and ASEAN Socio-Cultural Community of Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam.
The students are undergoing a 12-month internship at the ASEAN Secretariat under the Japan Government-sponsored ASEAN Integration Initiative through the Japan-ASEAN Integration Fund.
On that occasion, the Secretary-General of ASEAN urged the 12 officials to work hard to increase their knowledge and understanding of ASEAN to be used in their countries at the end of this program. As of April 2023, the program has trained 99 officers from Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam.
