Sihanoukville International Port will allow cargo ships from around the world to dock from 2029 onwards
(Sihanoukville): Cambodia has ambitions to develop the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port to be able to step up with the Royal Government is developing this international port to achieve the plan from 2029 onwards, cargo ships from around the world can You can dock at this international port without any obstacles, water depth, container location or parking problems.
This was confirmed by Mr. Lou Kimchhun, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port in a press conference with the press on April 25, 2023 at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port. The press is led by the Club of Cambodian Journalists.
Mr. Luo Kimchhun, Director General, said that in addition to the daily trade activities, the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port is also busy developing container terminals, increasing the depth of waterways in response to the growth. International trade, transportation, and fulfillment of plans allow cargo ships of all sizes to dock. He confirmed that this ambition will be achieved in 2029 onwards.
He planned that in 2024, the Royal Government will implement another new port, which will increase the container capacity by 35% compared to the current time. Currently, only about 18% of large cargo ships dock at Sihanoukville Port.
He said that by 2026, the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port will have the same authority as the ports of other countries in the region and will allow about 93 percent of local cargo ships to dock, reducing shipping costs by about $ 200 per person. Containers as well as increase national trade competition and can also attract more investment to Cambodia.
He added that in 2028, Cambodia will build a new port with a depth of 16.5 meters, then the goods transported around the world, especially the United States, part of Europe as well as Asia will be able to dock. Go to Sihanoukville Autonomous Port without water depth barriers.
General Director Lou Kimchhun also stressed that in 2029, the Royal Government will build a new port with a depth of 17.5 meters to ensure that all cargo ships from around the world can Can dock at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port without any obstacles, including water depth, docking and container loading.
The Director General of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port is optimistic that once all cargo ships can dock at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, that will reduce the cost of sea freight than it is now, leading to an increase. A major challenge for the national trade sector is to increase the economic profits by hundreds of millions of dollars, he said, according to the study is up to more than 350 million dollars per year.
In addition, it will also help attract foreign investors to invest in Cambodia, as their companies will be able to easily import raw materials and export finished products without having to go through. Connected with the ports of other countries, this is a huge benefit for the nation.
