Senior official of the Ministry of Culture of Cambodia has been appointed Secretary-General for the first term of the Alliance for Asian Cultural Heritage.
(Phnom Penh): With the participation of 22 countries and 3 international organizations, the Alliance for Heritage Conference was held on April 24-25, 2023 in Xi'an, Shaanxi Province, People's Republic of China.
Mr. Kong Virak, Undersecretary of State, attended the meeting on behalf of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts of the Kingdom of Cambodia and represented the Minister. The conference has four main agendas:
* 1: Approval of the draft statute * 2: Work plan for 2023-2024 * 3: Election of the Secretary-General * and 4. Approval of the Xi'an Declaration of the Alliance for Asian Cultural Heritage.
Proud of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, Kong Virak was elected General Secretary for the first term of the Alliance for Asian Cultural Heritage in the 2023-2024 term by a majority vote.
Please note that Cambodia is one of the 10 countries that are the founders of the Alliance for Asian Cultural Heritage. The Alliance aims to establish an intergovernmental mechanism for cultural heritage cooperation among Asian countries.
