Kampot Salt, Kep Fish Sauce, Kampot Kep, Takeo Lobster are registered by the Ministry of Commerce as GI, while Battambang Coconut, Siem Reap Noodles, Grapefruit, Koh Pei and Kampong Thom are listed as collective trademarks.
Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the National Commission for the Management of Intellectual Property, stated that the registration of geographical markers and collective trademarks for these products is the head of government's intention to add value to local products and Strengthen the competitiveness of Cambodian products in the domestic market and export.
"The registration of these products is an important achievement as we have worked together to create, compile, preserve and develop local products with high added value and promote our Cambodian culture," he said. "I firmly believe that geographical brands and collective brands will drive more demand for products in national and international markets and be part of the tourism destination."
Mr. Suon Vichea, Director of the Intellectual Property Department of the Ministry of Commerce, Geographical Identification and Collective Trademarks Pride: For the development of its products and business.
He said that the success in building a geographical brand in the past has made many Cambodian products into foreign markets and very famous, such as Kampot pepper, Phnom Penh noodles and Kampong Speu palm sugar. These products not only get high prices, but also become products that contribute to promote the tourism potential of the province, culture, traditions, customs, history of the Cambodian people on the international stage.
Mr. LONG HUN, President of Koh Pi 2 Grapefruit Producers and Traders Association, said that after the two Koh Grapefruit Grape registered as a collective brand, it will boost the reputation of Koh Pi 2 Grapefruit, Tbong Khmum Province to have a better market and good support. Eat more than before. Currently, Grapefruit Island 2 only supplies markets in Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham and Phnom Penh due to the lack of recognized brands.
He said that what motivated the two islands grapefruit to register as a collective brand was because the local oranges had a delicious sweet taste, similar to the soft grapefruit from Koh Trung grapefruit in Kratie province. He hopes that after the two islands grapefruit is registered as a collective brand, the supply will be wider and the value added will be higher than now, which will make the community more prosperous while the community has been expanding its cultivated area.
Mr. Sap Sarun, President of Takeo Lobster Association, said that while Takeo Lobster was registered as a geographical indication, the association was preparing to expand the market and increase production, ie in each farm that used to produce 1 ton in One year will increase production to 2 tons per year to increase the market supply to at least 100 kilograms per day.
Minister of Information Reminds All Journalists to Disseminate Professional, Ethical and Sourced Information
(Siem Reap): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, reminded all journalists to disseminate information in a professional, ethical and clear manner. Press at Siem Reap Provincial Hall on April 26, 2023.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of the seminar on the role, duties and professional ethics of journalists, Mr. Liv Sokhon, Director of the Siem Reap Provincial Information Department, spoke about the work done by the department in the past and the management of legally registered media units. Activities in Siem Reap, as well as some challenges and suggestions.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith reminded all journalists to publish their news professionally, ethically and to have clear sources that the truth will be a shield to protect journalists from legal punishment.
"Ethics is important, it is not a matter of coercion or crime, but ethics, like the wind in the first balloon, maintains our dignity as journalists who show that we are truly professional," he said. "We went through the second learning, it shows the value of people in society as a whole."
It should be noted that any journalist who writes in accordance with professional ethics, but when published to be sued, will receive the right to defend from the volunteer lawyers of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen is responsible. Defend the journalists who work in accordance with those professional ethics.
In addition, Mr. Ung Kim Leang, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap, said that the press is a mirror of society, but some media also pollute society. He added that the workshop provided an opportunity for journalists to learn about the role, duties and professional ethics of journalists in avoiding mistakes in writing news for public dissemination in society.
