Mine Authority and German Company Host a Dinner to Welcome Participants in the First Regional Workshop on Effective Solutions for Mine and Unexploded Ordnance Detection
The regional workshop brought together experts and stakeholders from the mine action community, including mine action operators, NGOs, government agencies and international organizations, to explore the latest developments in mine and UXO detection technology. Participate in improving mine action operations and strategically accelerate progress towards Cambodia and the ASEAN region, as well as the mine-free world.
At the dinner on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mines Authority, warmly welcomed the presence of technical experts and all mine action communities from Cambodia and the ASEAN region who attended the workshop. Joint Mine Action Area and Unexploded Ordnance under a joint venture between the Mine Authority and Vallon GmbH, hosted by Cambodia.
The Senior Minister hopes that this regional workshop will share the latest knowledge, skills and technologies in the detection of landmines and unexploded ordnance in a highly effective manner with the common goal of making the world safer and more prosperous. Previously, Vallon GmbH was an indispensable partner in the production of state-of-the-art, high-tech equipment for the detection of landmines and unexploded ordnance for humanitarian purposes.
