The remains of 7 more Vietnamese volunteer soldiers will be repatriated on May 24.
(Ratanakkiri): The Ratanakkiri (Cambodia) and Yalay (Vietnam) Provincial Commission for the Search of the remains of the Ratanakkiri Province (Vietnam) held a meeting on the preparation of the repatriation program for the remains of 7 more Vietnamese volunteer soldiers and experts. During the war in Cambodia in Ratanakkiri province for the dry season 2022-2023.
The meeting was held on the morning of April 25, 2023 under the chairmanship of Mr. Sou Serey, Deputy Governor and Chairman of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Committee for Excavation and Remembrance, and Ms. Nguyen Thi Thanh Lech, Vice Chairman of the Provincial People's Committee and Chairman of the Committee. Yalai provincial excavation team.
Speaking at the meeting, Mr. Su Serey said that the search and repatriation of the remains of Vietnamese soldiers who lost their lives during the war in Ratanakkiri province is in accordance with the cooperation agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Vietnam. And between Ratanakkiri and Yalai provinces, which plan to search for the remains of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army in Ratanakkiri province.
The two commissions set May 24, 2023 at the Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Culture and Fine Arts for arranging the departure of the remains of seven Vietnamese volunteers and experts found during the 2022-2023 dry season.
