Mr. Pan Sosak defended the draft law on the approval of the border trade agreement between Cambodia and Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of April 24, 2023, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, led a delegation to defend the draft law on the approval of the border trade agreement between Cambodia and Vietnam with the Commission. 9 of the Senate.
During the meeting to discuss the draft law, Mr. Kong Sarach, Member of the Standing Committee and Chairman of the Ninth Committee of the Senate, informed the meeting that the Ninth Committee of the Senate had carefully examined the text of the draft law on the approval of the agreement. On border trade between Cambodia and Vietnam.
He added that the draft law was prepared in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution, laws and relevant legal norms. The Ninth Commission fully agreed on the procedures and procedures for requesting ratification of the above draft law.
In response, Mr. Pan Sosak clarified and informed the meeting of the objectives, content as well as the benefits that Cambodia will receive from the border trade agreement between Cambodia and Vietnam when this agreement enters into force.
The Minister also answered questions from members of the Ninth Committee of the Senate regarding the draft law.
Minister Pan Sosak hoped that the draft law on the ratification of this agreement would contribute to the implementation of strategies to further strengthen business connectivity aimed at enhancing business partnerships, providing employment opportunities and business opportunities. Promote production and family business that will help promote and improve the lives of Cambodians living along the Cambodian-Vietnamese border.
(Phnom Penh): Retaining old members plus building new party members is a strong unity force for the party to continue to lead the country to further progress, as well as make the country peaceful, social stability and development. In all areas.
Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Local Working Group of Khan Chamkar Morn and Khan Boeung Keng Kang, said this while presiding over the inauguration ceremony of 180 new members of the CPP of the Party Committee. Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov in Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh, which was held at the party office in Khan Chamkarmon.
Dr. Ith Sam Heng stated that the new and old party members have an important role to play in striving to properly implement the party's program, policies and statutes aimed at building good relations with the people and promoting the party's political programs and state laws. By maintaining unity, internal unity, helping each other, and must strive to learn and enhance the capacity of both virtues and morals to accomplish the tasks for our society.
In addition, Dr. also mentioned the history and achievements of the Cambodian People's Party, a mature party, has set out a correct political program and has built many achievements in the cause of the motherland. Has gone through all kinds of difficulties with the people until the country is completely peaceful and developed as it is today.
Yim Sinan, a representative of the newly-elected Cambodian People's Party, believes that only the Cambodian People's Party can maintain peace and bring Cambodian ships to the same level of development as other developed countries. We are very proud to have contributed as members of the Cambodian People's Party.
In order to respond to the trust of the party and participate in maintaining the victory of the party in the upcoming 7th National Assembly election on July 23, 2023, we would like to make the following commitments:
1. Commitment to fully support the decision of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, which unanimously decided to continue to support Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister and to nominate Dr. Hun Manet as the Prime Minister's candidate for the future.
2. Commitment to the absolute protection of peace, political stability, security, social order and to prevent any attempts by the opposition and the biased environment to ensure the peaceful life of the people.
3. Commitment to serve the CPP faithfully.
