Mr. Tum Nero made this statement at a press conference on "Success of the past 5 years of Stung Treng Provincial Administration" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government at the Office of the Council of Ministers on April 24, 2023.
He pointed out that although Stung Treng is not a potential province for rice cultivation, it is a potential area for agro-industrial crops such as cashew, cassava, rubber and mango.
He said that in the last five years, cashews have produced about 90,000 to 100,000 tons and generated more than $ 100 million in revenue. The cassava crop has grown significantly by 2022, covering more than 25,000 hectares and producing more than 1.6 million tons, providing more than $ 200 million over the next five years. Inject into the economy of Stung Treng province.
At the same time, the rubber crop has also grown significantly, with more than 20,000 tons of rubber being harvested each year and earning more than $ 20 million, while mango production of more than 100,000 tons, which generates more than 30 tons. Million dollars in 5 years.
Livestock, on the other hand, generates about $ 200 million in revenue, and the fisheries sector yields about 4,000 tons per year and about $ 150 million over the next five years.
