Foreigners rush to evacuate their citizens from Sudan as the situation worsens
(Khartoum): Foreigners rush to evacuate their citizens from Sudan, torn apart by anarchy, where fighting intensified as fighting lasted for ten days between forces loyal to two generals. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, April 24, 2023.
With renewed clashes between the army and the armed forces in Khartoum and across the country, the United Nations says panicked Sudanese are short of water, food, medicine and fuel, as well as power cuts. And the Internet as well.
At least 427 people have been killed and more than 3,700 injured, according to the UN agency, which also reports that Sudanese civilians are "fleeing the fighting." "Hold neighboring countries such as Chad, Egypt and South Sudan."
The United States and several countries in Europe, the Middle East, Africa and Asia have launched emergency missions to evacuate embassy staff and residents of Sudan by land, air and sea.
U.S. Special Forces intervened by helicopter to rescue diplomats and their families on Sunday as Britain launched a similar rescue mission involving more than 1,000 troops. .
