(Pursat): Mr. Keo Sothea, the owner of Veal Sre Duong Chet restaurant in Veal Veng district, Pursat province, said that as a responsible restaurant owner, I know that selling wild meat to my customers can cause many diseases. "Type and will put them at risk."
“Veal Veng district has a lot of potential. We can protect our forests and wildlife and we will continue to grow. "We can farm and promote our district to national and international tourists, and we continue to educate community members, relatives, families and children to protect our environment now."
He also expressed his confidence and support for the Zero Trap Campaign to Stop Wildlife Trafficking. He will continue to protect forests and wildlife and help his community understand the importance of our natural resources.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that 19 restaurants in Veal Veng district and in Pursat town were declared non-vegetarian restaurants to their customers. 10 in Veal Veng district and 9 in Pursat provincial town.
"As of now, there are a total of 71 restaurants and eateries in the target provinces of the Zero Trap campaign, which have announced that they will not sell wild game to their customers," said Neth Pheaktra.
Mr. Net Pheaktra emphasized: "We believe that the owners of restaurants and eateries will participate and change the attitude of not eating wild animals and turn to participate in the protection and conservation of wildlife, which is our natural resources for human survival. The next generation. "There is no demand, no supply, trapping and hunting will decrease. Please join us."
