This is according to Mr. Tum Niro, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Stung Treng Province on the morning of April 24, 2023 in the press conference of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on "Five years of success of Stung Treng Provincial Administration. "
Mr. Tum Niro claimed that this giant trout, which is more than 2 meters long and weighs up to 300 kilograms, is unprecedented in the world, having just been spotted by fishermen in Stung Treng province. Seeing this rarity, officials installed self-monitoring devices before returning to the water to monitor their progress and daily life.
The official also thanked the people who obeyed the authorities' instructions to release the giant trout back into the river, as this is a rare species in the world. He further explained that if the fishermen traded the giant trout, they would not be able to become rich, and if they ate, they would not be able to have immortality, but if the giant trout survived, they would have left a good reputation. To Cambodia.
However, he has not yet been able to confirm the actual number of large trout, as the installation of the tracking device will help professional officers to learn more.
Recall that a giant trout weighing about 300 kg was found in the Mekong River in Stung Treng province in June 2022, and this giant trout broke the world record for the largest freshwater fish. This giant trout weighs about 300 kilograms, is 2 meters wide and almost 4 meters long from head to tail.
