(Pursat): The community of Protected Area Village, Page of Phnom Samkos Protected Area in Pramoy Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province, has set up a cardamom nursery to plant in the forest so that it will not be lost.
Currently, cardamom, young plants and seeds are in high demand, while young cardamom is used as a vegetable and its fruit is used as a medicine to treat various diseases.
Cardamom is a type of balm that many communities use to lower blood pressure, lower blood sugar and fat, facilitate breathing, lose weight and so on. This plant grows naturally in Pursat and Battambang provinces in the Cardamom and Samkos wildlife sanctuaries.
The community usually collects cardamom at the end of the rainy season to dry, use as a household medicine and sell to the market. Cardamom can also be used as a hot tea and as a food ingredient. Cardamom is used as a vegetable, such as onlak or fried with snail oil, beef, etc., because it tastes delicious and slightly spicy.
Mr. Ros Chhor, Director of the Department of Community Livelihood of the Ministry of Environment, confirmed that natural cardamom varieties grown in streams and cardamom mountains have been increasing cultivation, with 13 communities expanding their plantations to meet demand. The current market price for a kilogram of cardamom is 20,000 riels.
Mr. Ros Chhor highlighted: "Cardamom nursery, because there is a project, he helped to provide reserves, how can the Ministry of Environment consider the need, if the Ministry does not consider, the cardamom will be reduced, the Ministry of Environment will lose. High attention, especially HE Say Sam Al.
He said that for unripe cardamom sells for 1 kg 10,000 riel, while dried cardamom costs from 40 to 50,000 riel. He said that cardamom harvesting is difficult because the location is rich in cardamom is on a distant mountain, so people who go out to collect cardamom need to rest on a mountain.
He said: "The Royal Government of Cambodia has designated a sub-decree on the genus of cardamom species on an area of more than 500 hectares in O'Som commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province to be an area to protect and preserve plants. Cardamom.
According to documents from the Ministry of Environment, cardamom bears good fruit at the age of 4 to 5 years and continues to bear fruit every year until the age of 50. Studies have shown that planting cardamom properly with cardamom can produce a lot of fruit. Its bells can be harvested in the rainy season.
