Citizens claim no illegal wildlife sale after Batheay district authorities' instructions and regular patrols
(Kampong Cham): People who sell at Spean Tros in Batheay commune, Batheay district on April 24, 2023, claim that there is no more illegal sale of wildlife after frequent instructions from Batheay district authorities and Regular patrols as well.
Hum Panh, 55, said she had been selling at the bridge for more than 25 years, selling smoked fish, gasoline and other small items. As for illegal wildlife, he does not have it for sale, so the Batheay district authorities have banned and instructed it regularly.
The woman confirmed that in the area some time ago, some wildlife was sold and the police cracked down. However, in 2022-2023, there will be no illegal wildlife sellers and residents in this area because the local authorities have issued a ban on wildlife sales and there will be regular patrols.
Residents living nearby and passing through the area frequently stated that despite local authorities' efforts to curb the illegal wildlife trade, there were still opportunists. From other areas, a small amount of wild animals were stolen and sold in this area during the time when the authorities were not there, that is, when the authorities were busy protecting security and order during various national festivals.
In relation to the above case, Mr. Oum Sarin, Officer in charge of Production and Health of Batheay District, said that in the case of illegal wildlife sales in Spean Tros area, he led the patrols regularly and often advised To the people in this area not to sell wildlife illegally. If the authorities find out, they will be punished according to the law and dismantle the stalls and stop selling here.
Mr. Oum Sarin confirmed that the real vendors have only 8 valid stalls, besides that there are people in other districts who cheat animals to sell.
The same official said that in connection with this crime, Batheay district authorities had recently cracked down on wildlife smugglers from other districts and arrested the perpetrators along with evidence to make a contract to stop the sale of wildlife. . Meanwhile, Batheay district authorities also regularly patrol the area.
