(Pursat): Scientists recently researched and found some rare species of animals and plants in the Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary in Veal Veng District, Pursat Province.
According to Neang Thy, Director of the Inland Biodiversity Conservation Division of the Wildlife and Nature Coalition, the species and biodiversity include: frogs, cardamom, legless animals, snakes, wolves, snakes. Cambodian gold beads, rattan plants, canals, cups on Phnom Samkos and ant tube plants on Phnom Tum.
Ms. Thy said that in addition to the recent species, researchers also found a number of geckos also found on the Dalai Lama and Phnom Samkos.
The researcher said that many species of plants and plants found on Phnom Samkos and some of the mountains in the Cardamom Mountains have not been found in other areas.
The recent discovery of rare animals and plant species is an indicator that the Phnom Samkos area needs to study and research more species and biodiversity, while many other biodiversity species have not been studied. Research yet.
