Ministry of Economy opens training course on technical skills, certification level, position 2023
(Phnom Penh): On April 24, 2023, the Ministry of Economy and Finance officially organized the opening ceremony of the training course on "Technical Skills at the Certificate Level Association 2023" for 300 trainees who are public finance officers. From the 25 Ministries-Institutions and Departments of Economy and Finance of the Capital-Provinces.
The purpose of this program is to promote the importance of highly skilled financial officers and the continuous capacity building to fully contribute to the support and implementation of the public financial management reform program, especially the fourth phase to achieve success. Effectively and sustainably.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hean Sahip, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and attended by leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Delegation of the European Union to Cambodia. , Representatives of relevant development partners as well as trainers and trainees from relevant units.
Professional qualifications by type of position shall be determined by sub-decree as proposed by the Minister of Economy and Finance and the regulations in force. This, in turn, makes training and capacity building skills related to public financial management an obligation for public finance officers to perform their duties to contribute to improving productivity and efficiency.
Speaking at the ceremony, Dr. Hean Sahip added that the training course on technical skills at the certification level was first implemented in 2018 and has been continued until now to meet the needs of the promotion. Step by step steps of the Royal Government's Public Financial Management Reform Program.
This training program is part of the professional development of each type of position for public finance officers who need to successfully attend training and obtain a certificate from the Ministry of Economy and Finance for the appointment or assignment of relevant duties. Public financial management.
He also reminded that the fourth phase of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, which focuses on "performance accountability" through the implementation of budgets, information, achievements and performance agreements, including authority, ownership and access. More responsibilities have been transferred to ministries and institutions and specialized units, including sub-national administrations, to prepare and implement full program budgets and budget units.
