(Pursat): The Ministry of Environment, partner organizations and authorities continued to launch the second phase of the zero trapping campaign in Veal Veng district, Pursat province under the theme "Together we end the crisis of trapping and wildlife trade in Cambodia" on 22 May. 2023.
The campaign brings together large numbers of government institutions, the private sector, civil society, students and citizens to end the crisis in protected areas and illegal wildlife trafficking in Cambodia. The campaign is led by Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign.
Regarding this activity, Mr. Vong Eng, Governor of Veal Veng District, told Fresh News that the Zero Trap Campaign was very good for Veal Veng District as well as Pursat Province because Veal Veng District is full of natural resource potential. Especially the presence of many rare wildlife.
The district governor said that for his district, there are always hunters from other districts or provinces who come to hunt wild animals, so through the zero trap campaign initiated by the Ministry of Environment and partner organizations is really good. As an authority, he announced his support for the Zero Trap campaign.
Mr. Vong Eng expressed his belief that this campaign will bring more benefits to Veal Veng district through various advertisements that raise awareness to the people to better understand the invaluable importance of natural resources and animals. The forest at these points will attract more and more national and international tourists to visit Veal Veng district to increase employment opportunities for local people.
Separately, Brigadier General Hun Rem, Chief of Post Pramoy, said that as a local authority, he always led his forces to spread the law and the importance of forests and wildlife. As the second Trap Zero Campaign, initiated by the Ministry of Environment and NGOs, moves towards Veal Veng district, this is a very important message for the protection of wildlife living in the mountainous areas of Veal Veng district of Pursat province.
Mr. Suong Sang, Head of the Community Protected Area, Phchek Chrum Chheuteal Chrum Village, Pramoy Commune, said that the Zero Trap Campaign, which is now marching towards his base, is very important in eliminating the traps set by hunters. Animals, in particular, have become a message to awaken people to love the forest and wildlife.
The community leader said that for his community, many species of wildlife are present in the natural forest, in fact, the Cardamom Mountains are also home to Asian wild elephants. So when we preserve forests and wildlife, communities will benefit more from natural resources.
According to Bun Thoeun Phany and San Srey Nea, 12th grade students at Pramoy High School, after listening to the message about the importance of natural resources and wildlife through this zero trapping campaign, they became more aware of the value. Of it. Forests and wildlife are very important to everyone on earth.
These young people claim that they will spread the importance of forests and wildlife to family and friends to better understand the value of this biodiversity for generations.
