(Pursat): Experts from the Natural Resources Conservation Organization, which is active in protecting wildlife and biodiversity conservation in Cambodia, have expressed similar views, wanting to see years of legal punishment for those who remain. Unauthorized persons who continue to hunt and trade in wildlife illegally as a warning to those who continue to secretly commit this crime.
Mr. Seng Teak said that according to the report of the Ministry of Environment in 2022, the number of traps that the perpetrators have set in all protected areas to catch wild animals across the country is 35,193 traps. Compared to the traps caught in 2021 before the Zero Trap campaign, there were more than 60,000 traps, down to more than 30,000 traps, a decrease of about 40 percent.
In connection with the Zero Trap Campaign, he expressed the hope that with the efforts of state institutions and partner organizations, as well as the visit of park officials and communities in the natural resource protection area to break the trap of resource crime. Nature effectively and strictly enforced the law against the perpetrators.
"Legal measures must be taken strictly against those who kill wildlife and trade in wildlife. At this point, the zero trapping campaign is decided. We need to look at special policies and laws, fines and penalties," he said. "Punishment."
At the same time, Mr. Seng Teak also requested to review and amend some articles related to the ban on killing and capturing wild animals. Currently, those who catch and kill wild animals are only contracted and fined from 1 million to 10 million riels, which is the smallest point for the perpetrators.
According to Tuy Serey Vathan, Program Director of the Wildlife and Nature Coalition, "If there is a discussion (the law punishes natural resource offenders), he will participate, but will have to go through a little closer discussion because it takes time. In a short time, lest the behavior of our people, you do not catch up so fast.
He expressed hope that through the zero trapping campaign will soon lead to the creation of a law to punish those who still do not spy on hunting wild animals for business.
Mr. Lou Vanny, Representative of FFI in Cambodia, suggested that if possible, the law should highlight the law on punishment and education so that people can better understand the law on wildlife, especially legal challenges. For committing a crime.
Mr. Lou Vanny said that this education is very important for the people to understand, especially the perpetrators who used to set traps to hunt wild animals to sell to traders to distribute for them to eat to turn to participate. This business easily comes to protect and conserve wildlife for future generations. Students who want to get a scholarship to study in China can contact PPSA, unlimited scholarships!
(Phnom Penh): For students in Cambodia who want to get a scholarship to study in China can contact the Student Association in the provinces in Phnom Penh (PPSA), which has partnerships with many schools and universities abroad, especially China, on the other hand, there is no limit on the number of scholarships.
Speaking to the media, Ms. Samrith Thida, Vice President of PPSA, said that the scholarship and study fair was attended by about 30 universities from China, which will provide scholarships to Cambodian students while the number of scholarships. There is no limit to that, as long as the students are willing to continue their studies and meet the requirements properly and pass the test according to the program submitted.
"The PPSA receives such operations from many partner universities abroad, especially in China, every year," she said. There are more than 40 majors, such as engineering, medicine, health, agriculture, technology.
Ms. Samrit Thida appealed to parents of students who want their children to study abroad or students who wish to study through scholarships in China, please contact PPSA directly to know about Information.
"Anyone can go as long as they really want to go to school," she said. "Our association's expert committee will help disseminate information on how to stay and study, as well as other tips when they go to study in China, in general, to facilitate the completion of the beginning of their study mission."
Ms. Samreth Thida also briefly mentioned the most important conditions for applying to study in China: Students must be good students in the school, have a real willingness to study Chinese to a level called HSK 4 and pass Pre-testing. If you do not pass the test, the association will help train additional candidates to be able to respond to the next test.
According to the Vice President, the vision of the Provincial Students Association in Phnom Penh (PPSA) is to give Cambodian students the opportunity to study abroad, such as China and other countries to bring full knowledge and skills. Participate in the development of the nation because the motherland of Cambodia has many opportunities for young people and modern human resources.
It should be informed that in addition to the scholarship program abroad, the Provincial Students Association in Phnom Penh (PPSA) also has cooperation on scholarship programs with local universities. In the future, the association will also organize such scholarship and study fairs with partner schools and universities to provide more scholarship opportunities for students.
