(Phnom Penh): On Monday morning, April 24, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the boundary of Preah Vihear Buddha Phisek and the achievements in the pagoda. Preah Barami Vongkot Borey is located in Sangkat Teuk Thla, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
Wat Preah Barami Vongkot Borey, also known as Wat Tuol Krasaing, was originally a hill rich in small and large Krasaing trees, and in the rainy season this hill is not flooded. When the country fell into disarray between 1973 and 1975, the hill became a haven for people fleeing from Kandal and Kampong Speu provinces, as well as for monks. .
Due to the observance of Buddhism as much as possible, the people at that time initiated the idea of organizing this hill to have a school called "Sala Chhean Tuol Krasang" in 1973. But during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, the site was destroyed, leaving only a small throne.
In addition to the new church, there are also a number of physical infrastructures that have been built in Wat Barami Vongkot Borey, including: arranging the lighting system in the temple, painting the temple and doors, repairing the flagpole, building the Buddha image, copper and the throne, and building the room. Water and cleaning to improve the beauty of the whole pagoda, the total construction cost is 1,002,301 USD.
(Prey Veng): Prey Veng provincial authorities, as well as the Prey Veng Old Market Commission, on the morning of April 23, 2023, called on traders who have not yet transferred their sales on the road south of the market and east of the Old Market to hurry up and sell at Phsar Thmey Prey Veng as soon as possible because the authorities will arrange the streets around the market to be in order in the city.
He added that after the notification from the authorities as well as the Old Market Commission, some street vendors around the Old Market decided to go to Prey Veng Central Market about 85 percent, but more than 20 other traders refused to go. This morning, the provincial authorities invited more than 20 vendors who were selling on the street to solve the problem.
Mr. Lahn Virak said that on behalf of the representative of the Old Market Committee and the Prey Veng Central Market, he always did what the authorities decided, and the establishment of the Prey Veng Central Market was due to the congestion of the Old Market, which led to traders selling on State-owned roads lead to the loss of public order and old buildings, which pose a risk to shopkeepers, will also require repairs.
He stated that Phsar Thmei and Old Market Prey Veng is a state market, so traders should not be confused as a private market on behalf of the Prey Veng City Market Commission also provides opportunities for traders who can not afford to rent stalls on the Central Market. Will help as much as possible for traders, especially the Central Market Commission has already provided 60 stalls selling vegetables, fish, meat to the poor who can not afford to buy stalls to sell for life for free.
In addition, the vendors in the Old Market who transferred to sell in Phsar Thmei in Prey Veng expressed their happiness and said that in the area of Phsar Thmei where he came to sell is fresh, cool air and beautiful. There is a large building, convenient for the people who come to shop in this market, unlike before, selling on the state road under a hot umbrella, rain, wind, which is very dangerous for health and life.
(Phnom Penh): Hundreds of families living in Snoul Khpos village, Sangkat Kambol, Khan Kambol, on April 23, 2023, continued to request the Ministry of Public Works and Phnom Penh Capital Hall to facilitate the construction of a road to the village at the bridge crossing the expressway. Fast and easy because the road down from the bridge into the village is now difficult to travel, when turning and getting on the bridge.
The people also requested the local authorities as well as the Ministry, especially the Phnom Penh Capital Hall, to facilitate this road to make it easier to travel, so that it can be as small as 12 meters, because the old road is 15 meters in size. M.
Residents also mentioned the hardships of commuters, especially young children, when riding bicycles and motorbikes to school, they are worried about safety while there are cars coming down from the bridge at high speed for fear of accidents. . If it rains, some of the students do not make it to school because sometimes they slip and fall back home.
Residents said that this is the third meeting to request the Phnom Penh authorities and the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to help as soon as possible because people continue to suffer due to narrow roads. That the authorities have a solution only to put the receipts and light poles, while the problem of turning into the village is still difficult.
However, the people would like to request the local authorities to help speed up the preparation of this road as soon as possible to facilitate the travel of people more safely.
