Senior Myanmar Election Commission official shot dead by gunmen
Nay Pyi Taw: A deputy chairman of the Myanmar Military-appointed Election Commission has been shot dead by rebels in Yangon, the latest in a series of assassinations of high-ranking officials linked to the current military regime. This was confirmed by the Myanmar authorities, quoted by the AFP news agency on Sunday, April 23, 2023.
The People's Defense Force was formed and armed by the shadow government of Myanmar to fight the military regime that seized power through a coup to overthrow Aung San Suu Kyi's government in February 2021. In April 2022, the deputy governor of the Central Bank of Myanmar, appointed by the military regime, was also shot dead by gunmen at her home in Yangon.
