MOSCOW (Reuters) - German authorities decided to expel a large number of Russian diplomats on Saturday, meaning the city of Berlin is continuing to destroy all Russian-German relations, the Russian Foreign Ministry said on Saturday. This is according to the publication by the Russian newspaper TASS on Saturday, April 22, 2023.
"We strongly condemn Berlin's decision to continue to damage Russia-Germany relations as a whole," the Russian Foreign Ministry said in a statement.
The Russian Foreign Ministry added that "in response to this hostile action, Russia has also decided to expel German diplomats from its country and to reset the maximum number of staff in the embassy."
Russia's Foreign Ministry officially notified the German ambassador to Moscow on April 5, 2023.
