This April, parts of Asia as a whole have been reporting extreme warming, with some countries recording record-breaking temperatures. In Bangladesh and India, the heatwave has fueled demand for energy, leading to power outages and power shortages for millions.
In Bangkok, temperatures reached 54 degrees Celsius in Bangna on Saturday, and authorities urged residents to refrain from outdoor activities and to protect themselves from the dangers of heatstroke. According to Thai authorities, temperatures will exceed 40 degrees Celsius in at least 28 provinces on Saturday.
According to a Thai government spokesman, due to the recent hot weather, electricity consumption has risen to a record high of more than 39,000 megawatts. April compared with the previous record of 32,000 megawatts in April last year. Dr. HUN Manet Visits Lieutenant General Hem Kuy, Deputy Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF)
