Mr. You Serey Vuth also called on workers to maintain peace, which is covering the whole country under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister to have jobs and earn a living. Ministry of Environment and partner organizations continue to actively show the benefits of wildlife to the people in Veal Veng district as a place for biodiversity
(Pursat): Officials from the Ministry of Environment, civil society organizations and journalists, as well as Pursat Provincial Administration and more than 300 relevant departments, continued the march to open the second zero trap campaign in Vol Veng district town, Pursat province on April 22. This year 2023. This ceremony also takes place on Earth Day.
The second Trap Zero Campaign in Veal Veng District aims to reduce and prevent the number of traps in protected areas in Pursat province as well as in protected areas in Cambodia and to cultivate a greater love for wildlife among Public.
The second Zero Trap campaign, which reached the Cardamom Mountains province after the successful results of the first phase Zero Trap campaign, took place in Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Kampong Thom and Ratanakkiri provinces in 2022, Ministry of Environment Collaborated with conservation partners and relevant provincial administrations.
The Secretary of State stated that the Cardamom Mountains are the area with the most traps because it is rich in wildlife such as elephants, lizards, wild boar, etc.
In this regard, Mr. Net Pheaktra added, "This campaign is to save the life of wildlife that is declining, which for 70 years, the decline of wildlife and research is about 60 percent."
He said the decline was due to traps being hunted in the forest to catch prey. Importantly, this second Zero Trap Campaign to educate people to understand the risks of wildlife loss to join the conservation of wildlife in Cambodia.
Mr. Kong Puthira, Director of Pursat Provincial Department of Environment, said that after launching the first campaign, people have become more aware of the value of wildlife, and now they see that the market used to sell wild meat. This decrease is due to the fact that people are more aware of the benefits of wildlife and aware of the disadvantages of eating wild meat.
In this regard, Mr. Nguon Bunnara, Director of Pursat Provincial Forestry Administration, emphasized that the Forestry Administration has always instructed all vendors and restaurants in Pursat province not to display food on the list of wildlife.
He said that the Forestry Administration has also cooperated with relevant partners to ban and educate local people about the pros and cons of eating wild animals.
It should be noted that Pursat province, according to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, has 6 protected areas: South Cardamom Mountain National Park, Central Cardamom Mountain National Park, Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary, Oral Mountain Wildlife Sanctuary. In many cases, the Tonle Sap Lake and the Biodiversity Conservation Corridor system have a total area of 689,297.
Joint Special Forces Training Between 70th Brigade and Counter-Terrorism Special Forces Completed
(Phnom Penh): The Joint Special Forces Training Course between the 70th Counter-Terrorism Special Battalion and the National Anti-Terrorism Special Forces Command by the Special Warfare Command of the Army of the Republic of Korea has been successfully concluded. .
