Deputy Director General of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, who pulled out a gun while driving a young man, has been remanded in custody.
(Phnom Penh): A person named Bel Van Det, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Administration and General Affairs of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, who withdrew his firearm, was remanded in custody on the afternoon of April 21, 2023. Police forces arrest and send to court.
It should be noted that the operation to arrest this person was carried out by the Central Security Force of the General Commission of National Police, Phnom Penh Municipal Police and Russey Keo District Police Inspectorate, led by Major General Bun Sosika, Deputy Commissioner for Security Planning.
Please be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has decided to terminate the position of this civil aviation official because of the withdrawal of firearms by others over car horns. The civil aviation official who was terminated by Samdech Techo is Bel Van Det, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Administration and General Affairs of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister posted a sub-decree to end his position with such confirmation: "If the court does not take legal action, let me discipline the state first. "The pool has the power to use weapons to threaten the weak." Samdech Techo added, "This is a warning message to all officials, do not use your power to harm the weak, especially not to use illegal weapons."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the Minister of Justice to work with the court not to allow perpetrators to use illegal weapons on bail before trial, as they may be threatening others.
