(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, met with 368 female coaches, assistant coaches and athletes of the Cambodian national team who will participate in sports competitions. The 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023, hosted by Cambodia.
The ceremony took place on Friday afternoon, April 21, 2023.
Taking this special opportunity, Samdech Kitti Sangkhabandit sent a message of greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all members of the ceremony with nostalgia and condolences. Well.
"Under the honorable leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the war-torn country has become a prosperous and developed country in all areas under the shadow of peace," he said. At the same time, the sport has also made remarkable progress. In the past, our athletes have won many medals for the motherland and made us famous in the region and the world. "Mr.
The purpose of this event is to encourage more athletes to train hard to build a strong will and commitment to the competition based on the spirit of national and international solidarity to achieve success and honor for the country.
The 32nd SEA Games will be held on May 5, 2023 and the ASEAN Para Games will be held from June 3 to 9, 2023. The hosting of the SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games is a source of pride and honor for the country and the people of Cambodia as a whole for 64 years.
