Chinese Foreign Minister: Both sides of the Taiwan Strait belong to China
Chin made the remarks during a forum in Shanghai, where he raised issues ranging from global economic debt to Taiwan. "Recently, there have been extreme allegations that China is trying to change the status quo and undermine peace and stability in the Taiwan Straits," he added. "Such a perception is irrational and extremely dangerous."
"It is not China, but the separatist movement that wants independence in Taiwan, along with a small number of countries that are trying to destroy the status quo," he said. "Those who play with the Taiwan issue will eventually burn themselves." According to Chhin, those who are truthful can clearly see who is causing the trouble and who is the first to blame.
(Koh Kong): On the afternoon of April 19, 2023, Major General Mandavit, Chief of Staff of the Koh Kong Provincial Gendarmerie Command, held an official meeting with the guidance of Brigadier General, Commander of the Koh Kong Provincial Gendarmerie. Implementation of modern digital presence in all units under the Koh Kong Provincial Gendarmerie Command.
The meeting was attended by the Deputy Chief of Staff, the Chief of the Deputy Chief of the Department, the Deputy Chief of the Office, the Chief of the Municipal, District Security Office and the Assistant Team.
The recruitment of soldiers through this modern digital system is a testament to the technological capabilities of the soldiers of the Koh Kong Provincial Gendarmerie, which is up-to-date in society, which is the age of technology.
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority will start testing the first phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant on the night of April 21, 2023. This is according to the announcement of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority on April 21, 2023.
The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA) has confirmed that during the pilot operation, the water supply company will send clean water to supply in Chroy Changvar district, and this may lead to water shortage in the short term.
Mr. Som Sovann, Director of Business Department of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, said that this is a pilot test to add water to pipes in the area around Prek Leap, and from April 28 to 29, the Water Supply Authority will start. Testing of water transmission to the west bank of the river before it is officially launched in early May 2023.
Mr. Long Naro, Director General of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, said that after the opening of the Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, the first step will be able to supply enough water to the connected network.
Please be informed that the first phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant project has the capacity to produce 195,000 cubic meters of clean water per day.
