According to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the second expressway in Cambodia will be presided over by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the expressway is about 138 kilometers long and will be a long bridge across the Mekong River. Including the bridge and the connecting road, it is about 5 kilometers long.
The senior minister said that the planned budget is about $ 1.638 million, which is less than Sihanoukville, but the length of the road is also shorter than the Sihanoukville Expressway. According to the senior minister, this road is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2026 or the beginning of 2027.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the expressway is very important in connecting China from Burma to Thailand to Cambodia and Vietnam.
