North Korea tells G7 it will continue to strengthen military capabilities until US threat is eliminated
SEOUL: North Korea's state-run media (KCNA) on Friday said that North Korea's position as a nuclear-armed state is indisputable and will continue to strengthen its military capabilities until the military threat from The United States and its allies were eliminated. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, April 21, 2023.
The KCNA made the report based on quotes from North Korean Foreign Minister Choe Son Hui, who accused the United States and other G7 members of interfering in Korea's internal affairs. The North illegally with the warning that Pyongyang will take strong action in the event of any threat to its sovereignty and core interests.
North Korea's reaction comes after the G7 foreign ministers condemned the April 13 missile test, which Pyongyang called an ICBM intercontinental ballistic missile test. Uses solid fuel technology. The ministers also called for denuclearization at the end of a meeting in Japan on Tuesday.
