The Kremlin has responded that South Korea's resumption of arms supplies to Ukraine would mean "relevant action" in the Ukraine conflict. Russia has threatened to return weapons to North Korea if South Korea dares to supply weapons to Ukraine.
On the battlefield, the clashes between Russia and Ukraine, which used foreign military aid, differed from those of the host countries. The use of NATO-backed weapons was previously banned on Russian soil, but in the wake of the clashes, US-backed weapons were reportedly fired on Russian territory. .
Meanwhile, German Chancellor Olaf Scholz has been pressuring Switzerland to maintain its central position to provide aid to Ukraine as the Swiss president visits Germany this week.
Switzerland, a neutral country, has yet to offer anything to help Ukraine in its fight against Russia. Swiss President Alain Berset stated at a conference on the position of Switzerland: "We have approved an agreement set out in our law." But when the situation changes so much, you can not ask us Do not violate our laws.
In addition, the United States has announced a $ 325 million military aid package for Ukraine, including HIMARS, ballistic missiles and anti-tank mines. This is the 36th military aid package provided to Ukraine since the February 24, 2022 attacks.
Also this week, amid reports of spring war preparations, Russian and Ukrainian leaders traveled to the front lines, encouraging their respective forces ahead of a large-scale offensive. Starting in the near future.
