General Hun Manet: Those who are good at wondering about the law and the army's practice in appointing, changing or promoting military ranks, please continue to wonder and hesitate, I do not have time to explain
(Phnom Penh): General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Army, has responded to those who are good at questioning the law and the practice of appointing, changing or promoting military ranks.
He briefly stated that those who are good at wondering, please continue to wonder and continue to argue according to their merits, he did not have time to explain the rules and habits to them, because he has to spend on things that are useful for the nation.
General Hun Manet's message came after analysts Seng Sary expressed skepticism about the appointment of Dr. Hun Manet to the rank of "General" after the King issued a royal decree promoting him.
Through social media, General Hun Manet said:
I would like to take this opportunity to sincerely thank my grandparents, aunts, uncles, aunts and uncles for sending me a congratulatory message on the occasion of being promoted to the rank of General today.
For those of you who are good at wondering about the rules and practices of the army in appointing, changing or promoting the military, and for those who are skeptical about the promotion for me, please continue to wonder and continue to ask as you should, if all He has a lot of time and nothing else to do. I do not have time to explain or respond with you 😅 because my time is spent on something useful.
In fact, I am now traveling hundreds of kilometers to continue to meet and work with the military units stationed along the border to strengthen the army's ability to prepare to defend our territorial integrity. "This work is more beneficial to the motherland than to spend time responding to your questions or insults, I honestly do not get angry."
