Minister of Labor: Promoting quality enterprise medical services contributes to the prevention and control of occupational accidents and diseases in the workplace
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, stated that the promotion of quality and efficient enterprise medical services is an important part of contributing to the prevention and control of occupational accidents and diseases. Occupation in the workplace.
On that occasion, Mr. Ith Sam Heng recommended and reminded the officers under the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to encourage employers, doctors, enterprises and health professionals in all factories to go through safety and health training. Pre-professional job as an enterprise doctor in the Department of Occupational Medicine.
He went on to recommend that an application for a doctor's license be issued every two years issued by the Department of Labor Medicine. Must be registered in the Health Professions Committee according to each specialty in order to be eligible to work as a doctor in a factory in accordance with Joint Proclamation No. 139 on the Terms and Conditions of Enterprise Medical Services.
He said that in 2022, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training promoted the implementation of labor laws and regulations through the labor inspection mechanism, including a total of 2,311 labor inspections, with 1,952 ordinary labor inspections. Conducted 25 follow-up inspections and 361 special labor inspections.
In addition, there is a proclamation and introduction of a guidebook on the establishment of hospital establishments and establishments as a tool to guide and indicate how to set up an enterprise hospital establishments to those directly involved with the work of health services in the workplace.
There are also 3 training sessions for enterprise doctors with the participation of 335 enterprise doctors.
In addition, the Ministry has issued 330 business licenses to enterprise doctors who have received training on the basics of occupational safety and health for enterprise doctors.
Respiratory problems, along with dermatitis, sore throats and sore throats, are among the most common health problems patients suffer from air pollution in Thailand. Thai authorities have advised people to use high-quality N95 masks to prevent pollution and not to open doors and windows, as well as to reduce time spent outside unnecessarily.
According to experts, air pollution in parts of Thailand is mainly caused by smoke from wildfires and burning of agricultural waste. Thailand has a population of more than 70 million and air quality issues have become a hot topic in the run-up to the ASEAN general election on May 14, while the current Thai government is Accused of not doing enough to resolve the issue.
