4-day-old male dolphin dies in Kratie province's Prek Prosop district
According to a press release from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the dead dolphin weighed 10 kilograms and was 0.87 meters long and 4 days old. And broken both sides. Through an autopsy, the team concluded that the baby dolphin had died from a mosquito net.
Meanwhile, last March, male dolphins died from the same nets in Stung Treng province. In 2022, 11 dolphins died, including 5 adult dolphins, 4 young dolphins, 1 adult and 1 adult.
At the same time, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in cooperation with the Kratie, Stung Treng Provincial Administration and relevant partner organizations, has been continuously strengthening the protection in the areas where dolphins live, as well as continuing to educate local people about universal values that are not. The cost of this Mekong dolphin.
As a result, the use of nets, hooks and electric devices has been reduced by about 50 to 60%. However, the use of fishing nets and the theft of electric devices have occurred in some places, resulting in the death of dolphins.
