According to Mr. Cheam Chansophorn, there are currently 292 enterprises in Tbong Khmum province employing 17,060 people. Separately, two garment enterprises employ 1,039 people, including in Suong and Ou Raing Ov districts. Five rubber plantations employ 8,888 people, 43 bricklayers employ 629 people.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan made the remarks at a press conference on "Success of the past 5 years of Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government at the Office of the Council of Ministers on April 20, 2023 .
He said that currently in Tbong Khmum province, there are more than 80,000 hectares of rubber plantations, of which more than 30,000 hectares are company plantations and more than 55,000 hectares are family plantations, with a total yield of about 80 hectares. 975 tons with a revenue of 120,554.711 million US dollars.
He added that currently in Tbong Khmum province, there are five rubber processing companies that are processing rubber for export.
Other potential crops for the province, such as cassava, cashew, red corn, pepper, mango, turmeric, generate more than $ 270 million.
At the same time, the provincial administration has set up two cashew processing factories and handicrafts, exporting more than 3,000 tons of processed cashew nuts each year.
