Prey Veng Provincial Court Detains 4 People for Forging and Using False Documents, Not Involved in Politics
(Prey Veng): Four people were arrested in a row and the Prey Veng Provincial Court decided to detain them in two separate cases. In this case, the court claims that it is not involved in politics.
Prey Veng Provincial Court on April 20, 2023 issued a press release stating that there were a total of four defendants: Ieng Chea, Heng Sam Oeun. The two defendants were remanded in custody by the Investigating Judge of Prey Veng Provincial Court on 13 April 2023 on charges of forgery, use of forged documents and conspiracy to commit fraud under Articles 204 and 205 of the Penal Code.
The other two defendants, Seng Visal (aka Touch), a female, and Bin Chong, 62, were remanded in custody by an investigating judge of the Prey Veng Provincial Court. On April 19, 2023, he was charged with forgery using a forged letter and conspiracy to commit a forgery under Articles 204 and 205 of the Penal Code.
According to Mr. Chan Vannak, Deputy Prosecutor and Spokesperson of the Prey Veng Provincial Prosecutor's Office, all procedures for the indictment and detention of the four accused are not politically motivated. That is, they commit crimes themselves.
