(Siem Reap): The humanitarian donation of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, was distributed by the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Siem Reap to 141 families affected by the typhoon in Chi Kreng District, Siem Reap Province.
These charitable donations were handed over to the families of the victims on the morning of April 20, 2023 through Mrs. Teang Eng Tea Seiha, in the presence of Mr. Sum Sam On, Director of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Siem Reap and members of the Red Cross Delegation. Siem Reap Local Authority.
Mrs. Teang Eng Tea Seiha brought greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen as well as Mr. Tea Seiha, Chairman of the Siem Reap Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always cares about the well-being of all citizens. No caste, creed, religion, or political affiliation, as the saying goes, "The Cambodian Red Cross is everywhere for everyone, leaving no one behind."
She also encouraged people to continue to grow mixed crops near their homes to support their families, and asked all people to continue to be careful this coming summer and to take care of their health, especially young children. If children are not comfortable, they should be rushed to the nearest health center.
For the gifts distributed, for one family that collapsed, one family received 30 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 box of fish, 1 portable mat, 1 mosquito net, 1 sarong, 1 scarf, 16 sheets of zinc and 150,000 Riels and materials Some groceries as well.
