Club of Cambodian Journalists hosts forum to "strengthen ethics of journalism" this weekend
(Phnom Penh): The Club of Cambodian Journalists (CCJ) will hold another gathering of more than 500 members on April 21, 2023 to promote the ethics of its journalism profession. The initiative for the current press conference was also held in the context of the celebration of World Press Freedom Day on May 3.
The meeting will take place at the National Institute of Education and is divided into three sessions:
* Session 2: From 5 to 6 pm is a forum for HE Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information with members of the Club of Cambodian Journalists.
* Session 3: A solidarity dinner that comes with lots of prizes supported by the private sector and philanthropists who support and promote the Cambodian media.
Puy Kea, President of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, said: "This is a great forum in the history of journalism that opens up a debate on the ethics of the journalism profession, a hot topic in the digital age. " He added: "I am confident that this forum will help strengthen the capacity of journalists, especially the ethics and professionalism, which is a shield to protect journalists from criticism and lawsuits."
