Speaking to Fresh News on April 19, 2023, Ms. M. Rachana, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, confirmed that the export of fresh longan fruit to the Chinese market is still ongoing. In fact, in the first three months of 2023, Cambodia exported 3,400 tons of fresh longan to China, and since the opening of the longan export market to Cambodia has exported more than 6,000 tons of fresh longan.
The spokesman added that the Ministry of Agriculture hopes that the export of fresh longan fruit will continue to grow because after opening the market to export fresh longan fruit from Cambodia to China, the Chinese side has not only sold Longan is not only marketed but also more popular in the Chinese market.
She added that in order to promote better exports, the Ministry of Agriculture, the General Department of Agriculture, which is a professional institution, will continue to work with farmers who grow fresh lentils to ensure that they comply with hygiene and phytosanitary principles. Hygiene is consistent because the export of fresh longan to China is possible only if the fresh longan fruit of Cambodia meets the standards set by China.
Mr. Phok Sophanborey, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Pich Chenda, a company that cleans, processes and packs agricultural products, said that after the first trial of exporting fresh lentils to China, the company plans to make large-scale exports. In September 2023, more.
Please be informed that Cambodia's fresh longan was officially exported to China in October 2022 with the first export of more than 1,000 tons. As for Chamkar Mean, it has been officially registered to export 74 fruits to the Chinese market, 40 in Pailin province, 28 in Battambang and 6 in Banteay Meanchey.
