Strikes in some European countries could affect more flights during the summer of this year
(Europe): Strikes in some European countries have led to an increase in flight cancellations, flight delays, as data from tour operators show bookings to cities such as Paris. Has declined despite efforts by airlines to avoid another disruption like in 2022. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, April 19, 2023.
In the UK, strikes at airports and ports have also disrupted airport operations across the country, with London airport facing the biggest delay, AirHelp said. In Germany, however, Hamburg Airport canceled all flights for Thursday and Friday this week due to strikes by security guards.
Under European passenger rights law, airline customers who are delayed for several hours are entitled to compensation, which is a difficult issue for airlines that are already in dire straits. The airline also said that the airport and other stakeholders must also be involved in compensating customers so that the burden is not too heavy on them.
Through this voicemail, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to waive some additional obligations, especially the obligation to wear a mask for gatherings, but individuals can wear a mask of their choice.
In addition, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also decided to waive the duty of rapid test for all types of meetings, but individuals can test quickly according to their choice.
However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen still calls on people to continue to keep clean by washing their hands often with soap or alcohol. Samdech Techo advised the Ministry of Health to continue to monitor and evaluate the status of Kovid 19 in collaboration with the World Health Organization in Cambodia.
In addition, the prince encouraged individuals with doubts to adhere to the "3 prevent and 3 do not" measures and quick test for Kovid 19 virus and monitor health properly.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Royal Government is still maintaining protective measures to be vigilant in response to the situation that will arise, especially the Ministry of Health must closely monitor and take measures for the upcoming SEA Games.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that if the test measures continue to open the SEA Games or watch the SEA Games, it will create serious problems for families and people waiting for the test, but we will drop this problem. Individuals in case of doubt should test themselves and do not have to attend to avoid creating problems for others.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen sees that the reduction of the above two measures will facilitate the cost of people to buy masks and reduce costs and time, as well as doctors for quick tests and PCR. And so on.
At the same time, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, thanked for the participation of all compatriots who made Cambodia travel to this day, which is a successful journey on the Battle of Kovid 19.
