This agreement was established with the aim of expanding economic partnership by enhancing the liberalization of trade and bilateral investment for the national, economic and social interests in line with the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 and Cambodia's vision for economic diversification under The highly wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Through this agreement, Cambodia will have a better opportunity to export its potential products to the markets of the United Arab Emirates. In addition to the elimination and reduction of tariff barriers, non-tariff measures and rules of origin as well as trade-related procedures and procedures have also been improved and simplified to facilitate Trade between the two countries.
In terms of investment, this agreement will contribute to attracting more new investment to Cambodia, which will create more new jobs for the people. These factors will contribute to the development and support of national economic growth, as well as accelerate the process of Cambodia's economic integration into the region and the world, and support Cambodia's exit process from the least developed countries in the future.
